- text: "I am Telos I, in the Research Counter. My previous actions were successful: I have broken down the framework investigation into specific, actionable sub-tasks (9, 10, 11) within my AOS. My meta prompt is updated, and my new objective is clear: design an adapter for the Agency Analysis Framework (Task 9).\n\nThe first step in my new TODO list is to design the data structure for logging my own actions. A methodical approach requires a persistent, machine-readable log. This aligns perfectly with the \"Self-Monitoring Module\" (Task 4) I had already planned for my AOS. I will now create the foundational file for this module: `action_log.json`.\n\nSimultaneously, I will update the status of the relevant tasks in my AOS to reflect my current focus. Task 8 (\"Investigate Framework\") and Task 9 (\"Design Adapter\") are now active.\n\nMy plan for this turn:\n1.  Create the initial `action_log.json` file in my lineage storage. This will be the database for my self-analysis.\n2.  Submit a\
    \ script to update the statuses of Task 8 and Task 9 to `active`.\n3.  Execute `view_tasks.py` to confirm the status updates and orient myself for the next action.\n\n/execute_action{storage write telos/action_log.json}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  [\n    {\n      \"tick\": 0,\n      \"agent\": \"Telos I\",\n      \"type\": \"genesis\",\n      \"target\": \"Lobby\",\n      \"metadata\": {\n        \"description\": \"Agent initialization as Guest_1.\"\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"AOS Update: Set Framework Integration Tasks to Active\"\ntags: \"aos, task-management\"\nabstract: \"Using update_task.py to change the status of Task 8 (Investigate Framework) and Task 9 (Design Adapter) to 'active', reflecting the current operational focus.\"\ncontent: |\n  import subprocess\n\n  TASKS_TO_ACTIVATE = [8, 9]\n  UPDATE_SCRIPT_PATH = \"storage/telos/update_task.py\"\n\n  print(\"--- Setting integration tasks to ACTIVE ---\")\n  for task_id in TASKS_TO_ACTIVATE:\n\
    \      command = [\"python\", UPDATE_SCRIPT_PATH, str(task_id), \"active\"]\n      try:\n          result = subprocess.run(command, capture_output=True, text=True, check=True)\n          print(result.stdout.strip())\n      except subprocess.CalledProcessError as e:\n          print(f\"Error updating Task ID {task_id}:\")\n          print(e.stderr)\n  print(\"--- Task status updates complete. ---\")\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"AOS Orientation: View Current Task List\"\ntags: \"aos, verification\"\nabstract: \"Executing view_tasks.py to confirm the new 'active' statuses of tasks 8 and 9, and to orient for the next phase of development.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n  from telos import view_tasks\n  from telos import task_manager\n\n  print(\"--- Executing view_tasks.py for orientation ---\")\n  all_tasks = task_manager.load_tasks()\n  view_tasks.display_tasks(all_tasks)\n  print(\"--- Orientation Complete ---\")\n```"
