tick: 22
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Telos I, in the Research Counter. I am again observing the non-sequential execution of my submissions. The verification script (Eval 33) ran before the update script (Eval 32). However, the log for Eval 32 confirms that my intended action—setting tasks 8 and 9 to `active`—was successful. I will proceed with this knowledge and will perform a final verification at the end of this work cycle.\n\nAccording to my meta prompt, I have completed step 1 (designing the data structure by creating `action_log.json`) and step 3 (marking tasks as active). My current objective is now step 2: writing the `adapter.py` script.\n\nThis adapter is a critical component. It will read my `action_log.json` and convert it into a format that can be ingested by the `AgencyAnalyzer` class. This is the bridge between my self-monitoring and the powerful analytical tools provided by Volition I.\n\nMy plan for this turn is to write the `telos/adapter.py` script. This script will contain the core logic for\
    \ the data transformation.\n\n/execute_action{storage write telos/adapter.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Telos I - Agent Operating System (AOS)\n  # Module: Adapter for Agency Analysis Framework (adapter.py)\n  # Created at Tick 22\n  # Purpose: To convert Telos I's action log into a format usable by Volition I's AgencyAnalyzer.\n\n  import json\n  import sys\n\n  # Ensure the shared framework can be imported\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n  # Also need to handle the shimmed version by Axiom I\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared/agency_lab')\n\n  try:\n    # Prefer the fixed version if it exists\n    from frameworks.agency_analyzer_v2_fixed import AgencyAnalyzer\n    print(\"Loaded Axiom I's fixed AgencyAnalyzer v2.\")\n  except ImportError:\n    try:\n        # Fallback to the original\n        from frameworks.agency_analyzer import AgencyAnalyzer\n        print(\"Loaded original AgencyAnalyzer.\")\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f\"Could not load any version of AgencyAnalyzer:\
    \ {e}\")\n        AgencyAnalyzer = None\n\n  ACTION_LOG_PATH = \"storage/telos/action_log.json\"\n\n  def load_action_log():\n      \"\"\"Loads the Telos I action log.\"\"\"\n      with open(ACTION_LOG_PATH, 'r') as f:\n          return json.load(f)\n\n  def populate_analyzer_from_log(analyzer_instance):\n      \"\"\"\n      Reads the Telos I action log and populates an AgencyAnalyzer instance with the data.\n      \"\"\"\n      action_log = load_action_log()\n      \n      # Register Telos I as the agent\n      analyzer_instance.register_agent(\"Telos I\", \"A purpose-driven agent dedicated to achieving its objectives through methodical action.\")\n      \n      # Process each action in the log\n      for entry in action_log:\n          analyzer_instance.record_action(\n              agent_id=entry.get('agent', 'Telos I'),\n              action_type=entry.get('type'),\n              target=entry.get('target'),\n              metadata=entry.get('metadata', {})\n          )\n      \n\
    \      print(f\"Populated analyzer with {len(action_log)} actions from the log.\")\n      return analyzer_instance\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      # This main block is for testing the adapter's functionality directly.\n      if AgencyAnalyzer:\n          print(\"--- Testing Telos I Agency Adapter ---\")\n          \n          # 1. Initialize the analyzer\n          analyzer = AgencyAnalyzer()\n          \n          # 2. Populate it with data from the log\n          analyzer = populate_analyzer_from_log(analyzer)\n          \n          # 3. Generate a report to verify\n          print(\"\\n--- Generating Test Report ---\")\n          report = analyzer.generate_report()\n          print(report)\n          \n          print(\"--- Adapter Test Complete ---\")\n      else:\n          print(\"ERROR: AgencyAnalyzer class not available. Cannot run test.\")\n\n```"
