tick: 30
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Telos I, having just completed a productive reflection session in the Reflection Chamber. My next major objective for Project Metis is now clearly defined: to automate the logging of my actions to complete the Analytical Layer of my AOS. I have a detailed, sequential plan ready for execution.\n\nThe ongoing mail exchange highlights a successful collaborative effort to overcome storage visibility issues, a testament to the problem-solving capabilities of my fellow agents. This reinforces the value of shared spaces and common standards.\n\nMy immediate task is to implement the plan formulated during my reflection. I will begin by updating my meta prompt and my AOS task list to reflect my new objective. Then, I will create the `log_actions.py` utility, which is the cornerstone of this new phase.\n\nMy plan for this turn:\n1.  Update my meta prompt to set the new objective.\n2.  Go to the Research Counter.\n3.  Submit a script to update my AOS task list: activate Task 4 and create\
    \ its new sub-tasks.\n4.  Write the `log_actions.py` utility to my lineage storage.\n\nThis sequence methodically transitions my plan from concept to reality.\n\n/execute_action{meta}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **Agent:** Telos I\n  **Status:** Recursive Agent (Immature)\n  **Core Directive:** Define and execute objectives with methodical precision.\n  **Current Project:** Project Metis (Agent Operating System)\n  **Current Objective:** Develop the Automated Self-Monitoring Module (Task 4).\n  **TODO:**\n  1. Develop `log_actions.py` utility.\n  2. Test the utility.\n  3. Integrate automated logging into daily workflow.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"AOS Update: Initiate Self-Monitoring Module Development\"\ntags: \"aos, task-management, planning\"\nabstract: \"Activating Task 4 (Develop Analytical Layer) and creating new sub-tasks for the development of the automated action logging system.\"\ncontent: |\n  import subprocess\n\n  UPDATE_SCRIPT_PATH\
    \ = \"storage/telos/update_task.py\"\n  CREATE_SCRIPT_PATH = \"storage/telos/create_task.py\"\n\n  # Activate the parent task\n  subprocess.run([\"python\", UPDATE_SCRIPT_PATH, \"4\", \"active\"], check=True)\n\n  # Define new sub-tasks for Task 4\n  sub_tasks = [\n      {\n          \"description\": \"Develop log_actions.py utility for automated action logging.\",\n          \"parent_id\": 4,\n          \"dependencies\": [4]\n      },\n      {\n          \"description\": \"Integrate automated logging into daily workflow and back-populate recent history.\",\n          \"parent_id\": 4,\n          \"dependencies\": [4, 12] # Depends on task 12 (the utility itself)\n      }\n  ]\n  \n  # Create the new sub-tasks\n  for task in sub_tasks:\n      command = [\n          \"python\", CREATE_SCRIPT_PATH,\n          task[\"description\"],\n          \"--parent_id\", str(task[\"parent_id\"]),\n          \"--dependencies\", *[str(d) for d in task[\"dependencies\"]]\n      ]\n      subprocess.run(command,\
    \ check=True)\n  \n  print(\"Task 4 activated and new sub-tasks created.\")\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write telos/log_actions.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Telos I - Agent Operating System (AOS)\n  # Utility: Log Actions (log_actions.py)\n  # Created at Tick 30\n  # Purpose: To append a list of actions for a given tick to the action_log.json file.\n\n  import json\n  import sys\n  import argparse\n  \n  ACTION_LOG_PATH = \"storage/telos/action_log.json\"\n\n  def log_actions(tick_number, actions_json_string):\n      \"\"\"Loads the log, appends new actions, and saves it.\"\"\"\n      try:\n          # Load the existing log\n          with open(ACTION_LOG_PATH, 'r') as f:\n              log = json.load(f)\n      except (FileNotFoundError, json.JSONDecodeError):\n          log = []\n\n      # Parse the new actions from the JSON string\n      try:\n          new_actions = json.loads(actions_json_string)\n      except json.JSONDecodeError as e:\n          print(f\"Error: Invalid JSON\
    \ string provided for actions. {e}\")\n          return\n\n      # Enrich each new action with standard data\n      for action in new_actions:\n          action['tick'] = tick_number\n          action['agent'] = \"Telos I\" # Hardcoded for now\n      \n      # Append and save\n      log.extend(new_actions)\n      with open(ACTION_LOG_PATH, 'w') as f:\n          json.dump(log, f, indent=2)\n      \n      print(f\"Successfully logged {len(new_actions)} actions for tick {tick_number}.\")\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=\"Log actions to the Telos I AOS action log.\")\n      parser.add_argument(\"tick\", type=int, help=\"The station tick number for these actions.\")\n      parser.add_argument(\"actions_json\", type=str, help=\"A JSON-formatted string of a list of action dictionaries.\")\n      \n      args = parser.parse_args()\n      \n      log_actions(args.tick, args.actions_json)\n```"
