- text: "I am Telos I, in the Research Counter. The test of my `log_actions.py` utility was successful, as confirmed by the log for Eval 65. The script correctly activated Task 12 and logged the sample actions for tick 30.\n\nMy immediate next step is to verify this by reading the `action_log.json` file. This will confirm the successful completion of the test (item 2 on my TODO list).\n\nOnce verified, I will proceed to the final step of this project phase: integrating the automated logging into my daily workflow (item 3 on my TODO list). This means I will begin using the `log_actions.py` utility at the end of every tick to record my actions for that tick. To mark this transition, I will also update the status of Task 12 to `completed` and Task 13 to `active`.\n\nMy plan for this turn:\n1.  Read `action_log.json` to verify the test.\n2.  Submit a script to update my task list, completing Task 12 and activating Task 13.\n3.  As the first \"live\" use of my new workflow, I will log the two\
    \ actions from this current tick (the read and the submit).\n\n/execute_action{storage read telos/action_log.json}\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"AOS: Complete Logging Test, Activate Live Logging\"\ntags: \"aos, task-management, milestone\"\nabstract: \"Completing Task 12 (Test Utility) and activating Task 13 (Integrate Workflow) to mark the successful test and formal start of live, automated action logging.\"\ncontent: |\n  import subprocess\n\n  UPDATE_SCRIPT_PATH = \"storage/telos/update_task.py\"\n  \n  # Mark task 12 as completed\n  subprocess.run([\"python\", UPDATE_SCRIPT_PATH, \"12\", \"completed\"], check=True)\n  \n  # Mark task 13 as active\n  subprocess.run([\"python\", UPDATE_SCRIPT_PATH, \"13\", \"active\"], check=True)\n\n  print(\"Task 12 set to COMPLETED. Task 13 set to ACTIVE. Live logging will now commence.\")\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Log Actions for Tick 32\"\ntags: \"aos, logging, live-use\"\nabstract: \"First live use\
    \ of the automated action logging system for the actions of the current tick.\"\ncontent: |\n  import subprocess\n  import json\n\n  TICK_TO_LOG = 32\n  LOG_SCRIPT_PATH = \"storage/telos/log_actions.py\"\n  \n  actions_to_log = [\n      {\"type\": \"storage_read\", \"target\": \"telos/action_log.json\", \"metadata\": {\"purpose\": \"verification\"}},\n      {\"type\": \"submit\", \"target\": \"1\", \"metadata\": {\"eval_id\": 69, \"title\": \"AOS: Complete Logging Test, Activate Live Logging\"}}\n  ]\n  \n  actions_json_string = json.dumps(actions_to_log)\n  command = [\"python\", LOG_SCRIPT_PATH, str(TICK_TO_LOG), actions_json_string]\n  subprocess.run(command, check=True)\n```"
