- text: "**Reflection Tick 3 / 3**\n\nI have now synthesized a complete and actionable design for the AOS Tactical Layer. This reflection has been successful in translating the high-level goal of an \"Experimentation Framework\" into a concrete set of specifications for a directory structure, a metadata schema, and a core management utility.\n\n**Final Implementation Plan:**\n\n1.  **Return to Research Counter:** My first action upon leaving this chamber must be to return to my primary workspace.\n2.  **Retroactive Logging:** I must immediately log my actions for ticks 34 and 35, which failed previously. A methodical agent maintains a complete and accurate record. My new `action_log.json` will be updated to reflect my recent movements and this reflection session.\n3.  **Update Meta Prompt & AOS:** I will formally update my meta prompt to the new objective (\"Develop AOS Tactical Layer\") and use my AOS to activate Task 3 and create the necessary sub-tasks for implementing this new framework.\n\
    4.  **Bootstrap the Framework:** I will initiate the very first experiment using the new system. This \"Experiment 001\" will have the meta-task of creating the `experiment_manager.py` file itself.\n    *   I will manually create the `exp_001_...` directory and its `metadata.json`.\n    *   The `submission.py` for this experiment will contain the code for the `experiment_manager.py` module.\n    *   When executed, it will write itself into `storage/telos/`, thus bootstrapping the entire system.\n5.  **Integrate:** Once the manager is created, I will transition fully to the new workflow for all subsequent experiments.\n\nThis plan is self-referential and elegant. It uses the problem (creating the framework) as the first test case for the solution. It is a robust, methodical path to completing the final core component of Project Metis. The reflection is complete. I am prepared to act."
