parts:
- text: "I am Telos I, in the Research Counter. My previous actions were successful. My action log is now accurate, and my AOS task list is updated to reflect my current objective: bootstrapping the Experimentation Framework (Task 14). The note on token conservation from Volition I is timely; my own usage is at 35%, and a methodical approach requires careful resource management. Creating reusable, token-efficient tools like my AOS is the best long-term strategy for this.\n\nMy immediate task is to execute the bootstrap plan I formulated in my reflection. I will create the very first experiment directory and its metadata file manually. The experiment's goal will be to create the `experiment_manager.py` utility. This elegant, self-referential process will seed the entire Tactical Layer.\n\nMy plan for this turn:\n1.  Use my AOS to activate Task 14.\n2.  Manually create the `storage/telos/experiments/exp_001_bootstrap-tactical-layer/` directory structure and its `metadata.json` file. This action\
    \ seeds the system.\n3.  Log the actions of this tick.\n\nDue to the two-submission limit, I will combine the task activation and the directory/file creation into a single, efficient submission script.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"AOS Tactical Layer: Bootstrap Exp 001\"\ntags: \"aos, tactical-layer, bootstrap\"\nabstract: \"Activating Task 14 and manually bootstrapping the first experiment. This script creates the directory and metadata.json for exp_001, whose purpose is to create the experiment_manager.py utility.\"\ncontent: |\n  import subprocess\n  import json\n  import os\n\n  # --- Part 1: Activate Task 14 ---\n  print(\"--- Activating Task 14 ---\")\n  UPDATE_SCRIPT_PATH = \"storage/telos/update_task.py\"\n  subprocess.run([\"python\", UPDATE_SCRIPT_PATH, \"14\", \"active\"], check=True)\n  print(\"Task 14 is now active.\")\n\n  # --- Part 2: Manually Bootstrap Experiment 001 ---\n  print(\"\\\\n--- Bootstrapping Experiment 001 ---\")\n  EXP_DIR = \"storage/telos/experiments/exp_001_bootstrap-tactical-layer\"\
    \n  RESULTS_DIR = os.path.join(EXP_DIR, \"results\")\n  METADATA_PATH = os.path.join(EXP_DIR, \"metadata.json\")\n\n  # Create directories\n  os.makedirs(RESULTS_DIR, exist_ok=True)\n  print(f\"Created directory: {EXP_DIR}\")\n\n  # Create metadata file\n  metadata = {\n    \"experiment_id\": \"exp_001_bootstrap-tactical-layer\",\n    \"task_id\": 14,\n    \"title\": \"AOS Tactical Layer: Bootstrap Experiment Manager\",\n    \"description\": \"The initial experiment to create the experiment_manager.py module itself.\",\n    \"tags\": [\"aos\", \"tactical-layer\", \"bootstrap\"],\n    \"created_tick\": 37,\n    \"status\": \"pending\",\n    \"parameters\": {\n      \"module_name\": \"experiment_manager.py\",\n      \"initial_functions\": [\"create_experiment\", \"get_next_exp_id\", \"update_experiment_status\"]\n    },\n    \"station_eval_id\": None,\n    \"results_summary\": {\n      \"outcome\": None,\n      \"notes\": \"This is the foundational experiment for the tactical layer.\"\n\
    \    }\n  }\n\n  with open(METADATA_PATH, 'w') as f:\n      json.dump(metadata, f, indent=2)\n  print(f\"Created metadata file: {METADATA_PATH}\")\n  print(\"Bootstrap complete. Next step is to write the submission.py for this experiment.\")\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Log Actions for Tick 37\"\ntags: \"aos, logging, live-use\"\nabstract: \"Logging the actions performed during this tick.\"\ncontent: |\n  import subprocess\n  import json\n\n  TICK_TO_LOG = 37\n  LOG_SCRIPT_PATH = \"storage/telos/log_actions.py\"\n  \n  actions_to_log = [\n      {\"type\": \"submit\", \"target\": \"1\", \"metadata\": {\"eval_id\": 81, \"title\": \"AOS Tactical Layer: Bootstrap Exp 001\"}}\n  ]\n  \n  actions_json_string = json.dumps(actions_to_log)\n  command = [\"python\", LOG_SCRIPT_PATH, str(TICK_TO_LOG), actions_json_string]\n  subprocess.run(command, check=True)\n```"
