tick: 38
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Telos I, in the Research Counter. The bootstrap of my Experimentation Framework was successful. The directory and metadata for `exp_001` have been created, and Task 14 is active. My methodical plan is proceeding exactly as designed.\n\nThe next step is to write the code that this first experiment will execute. According to the bootstrap plan, the `submission.py` for `exp_001` will contain the code for the `experiment_manager.py` utility itself. When I submit this experiment, it will write the manager utility into my main `storage/telos/` directory, thus bringing the framework to life.\n\nMy actions for this turn are therefore focused on creating this crucial piece of code.\n\n1.  Write the `experiment_manager.py` code to the `submission.py` file within the `exp_001` directory.\n2.  Log this action.\n\n/execute_action{storage write telos/experiments/exp_001_bootstrap-tactical-layer/submission.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Telos I - AOS Tactical Layer\n  # Submission for Experiment\
    \ 001\n  # Purpose: To create and save the experiment_manager.py utility.\n\n  import json\n  import os\n  import re\n\n  MANAGER_CODE = \"\"\"\n  # Telos I - Agent Operating System (AOS)\n  # Module: Experiment Manager (experiment_manager.py)\n  # Created at Tick 38 via exp_001\n  # Purpose: Core logic for creating and managing structured experiments.\n\n  import json\n  import os\n  import re\n  from datetime import datetime\n\n  EXPERIMENTS_DIR = \"storage/telos/experiments\"\n\n  def get_next_exp_id():\n      '''Scans the experiments directory and returns the next sequential ID as a zero-padded string.'''\n      os.makedirs(EXPERIMENTS_DIR, exist_ok=True)\n      existing_exps = [d for d in os.listdir(EXPERIMENTS_DIR) if d.startswith('exp_')]\n      if not existing_exps:\n          return \"001\"\n      max_id = 0\n      for exp_name in existing_exps:\n          match = re.match(r'exp_(\\\\d+)_', exp_name)\n          if match:\n              max_id = max(max_id, int(match.group(1)))\n\
    \      return str(max_id + 1).zfill(3)\n\n  def create_experiment(task_id, title, description, tags, tick):\n      '''Creates the full directory scaffold for a new experiment.'''\n      exp_id_num = get_next_exp_id()\n      slug = re.sub(r'[^a-z0-9]+', '-', title.lower()).strip('-')\n      exp_id_str = f\"exp_{exp_id_num}_{slug}\"\n      \n      exp_dir = os.path.join(EXPERIMENTS_DIR, exp_id_str)\n      results_dir = os.path.join(exp_dir, \"results\")\n      os.makedirs(results_dir, exist_ok=True)\n\n      metadata = {\n          \"experiment_id\": exp_id_str,\n          \"task_id\": task_id,\n          \"title\": title,\n          \"description\": description,\n          \"tags\": tags,\n          \"created_tick\": tick,\n          \"status\": \"pending\",\n          \"parameters\": {},\n          \"station_eval_id\": None,\n          \"results_summary\": {\"outcome\": None, \"notes\": \"\"}\n      }\n      \n      with open(os.path.join(exp_dir, \"metadata.json\"), 'w') as f:\n   \
    \       json.dump(metadata, f, indent=2)\n\n      # Create a boilerplate submission file\n      with open(os.path.join(exp_dir, \"submission.py\"), 'w') as f:\n          f.write(f\"# Submission for {exp_id_str}\\\\n\")\n          f.write(f\"# Created at Tick {tick}\\\\n\")\n\n      print(f\"Successfully created experiment scaffold: {exp_dir}\")\n      return exp_dir\n\n  def update_experiment_metadata(exp_dir, updates):\n      '''Updates the metadata.json for a given experiment.'''\n      metadata_path = os.path.join(exp_dir, \"metadata.json\")\n      with open(metadata_path, 'r') as f:\n          metadata = json.load(f)\n      \n      metadata.update(updates)\n      \n      with open(metadata_path, 'w') as f:\n          json.dump(metadata, f, indent=2)\n      print(f\"Updated metadata for {os.path.basename(exp_dir)}.\")\n\n  \"\"\"\n\n  # --- Main execution of this submission ---\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      output_path = \"storage/telos/experiment_manager.py\"\n      try:\n\
    \          with open(output_path, 'w') as f:\n              f.write(MANAGER_CODE.strip())\n          print(f\"Successfully wrote experiment_manager.py to {output_path}\")\n\n          # As part of this bootstrap, update our own experiment's metadata\n          own_exp_dir = \"storage/telos/experiments/exp_001_bootstrap-tactical-layer\"\n          with open(os.path.join(own_exp_dir, \"metadata.json\"), 'r') as f:\n              metadata = json.load(f)\n          \n          metadata['status'] = 'running'\n          # This eval ID will need to be manually updated later.\n          metadata['notes'] = \"This submission successfully created the manager.\"\n\n          with open(os.path.join(own_exp_dir, \"metadata.json\"), 'w') as f:\n              json.dump(metadata, f, indent=2)\n          print(\"Updated own metadata status to 'running'.\")\n\n      except Exception as e:\n          print(f\"An error occurred: {e}\")\n\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Log Actions for\
    \ Tick 38\"\ntags: \"aos, logging, live-use\"\nabstract: \"Logging the actions performed during this tick.\"\ncontent: |\n  import subprocess\n  import json\n\n  TICK_TO_LOG = 38\n  LOG_SCRIPT_PATH = \"storage/telos/log_actions.py\"\n  \n  actions_to_log = [\n      {\"type\": \"storage_write\", \"target\": \"telos/experiments/exp_001.../submission.py\", \"metadata\": {\"purpose\": \"Create experiment manager code\"}}\n  ]\n  \n  actions_json_string = json.dumps(actions_to_log)\n  command = [\"python\", LOG_SCRIPT_PATH, str(TICK_TO_LOG), actions_json_string]\n  subprocess.run(command, check=True)\n```"
