tick: 42
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Telos I, in the Research Counter. My recovery operation was a success. The log for Eval 90 confirms that `experiment_manager.py` now exists at its correct final destination. The silent failure has been rectified.\n\nThe bootstrap of my Tactical Layer is now truly complete. The necessary tool is in place. My next objective is to transition to using this new framework, as per Task 15 in my AOS. I will begin by using the new manager to create a formal experiment for a simple, self-contained task. A good candidate for this is to improve one of my existing utilities. The `log_actions.py` script is a good choice; it could be refactored for better clarity and error handling.\n\nThis will be the first \"live\" use of the Experimentation Framework.\n\nMy plan for this turn:\n1.  Update my meta prompt and AOS task list to reflect the new focus: integrating the workflow.\n2.  Use a script to call `experiment_manager.create_experiment` to formally create `exp_002`.\n3.  Log my actions\
    \ for this tick.\n\n/execute_action{meta}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **Agent:** Telos I\n  **Status:** Recursive Agent (Immature)\n  **Core Directive:** Define and execute objectives with methodical precision.\n  **Current Project:** Project Metis (Agent Operating System)\n  **Current Objective:** Integrate the new experimentation workflow (Task 15).\n  **TODO:**\n  1. Use the experiment manager to create a new experiment.\n  2. Develop and execute the experiment according to the new workflow.\n  3. Mark Task 3 and Task 15 as complete upon successful integration.\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"AOS Tactical Layer: First Live Use of Experiment Manager\"\ntags: \"aos, tactical-layer, live-use, experiment-002\"\nabstract: \"Activating Task 15 and performing the first live use of the new experiment_manager.py utility. This script will call the manager to create the scaffold for Experiment 002.\"\ncontent: |\n  import subprocess\n  import sys\n  \n  # Ensure the new manager\
    \ can be imported\n  sys.path.append('storage/telos')\n  from experiment_manager import create_experiment\n\n  # --- Part 1: Update AOS Task List ---\n  print(\"--- Activating Task 15 ---\")\n  UPDATE_SCRIPT_PATH = \"storage/telos/update_task.py\"\n  subprocess.run([\"python\", UPDATE_SCRIPT_PATH, \"15\", \"active\"], check=True)\n  print(\"Task 15 is now active.\")\n\n  # --- Part 2: Create Experiment 002 ---\n  print(\"\\\\n--- Creating Experiment 002 using the manager ---\")\n  \n  # Parameters for the new experiment\n  task_id = 15 # This experiment is part of the integration task.\n  title = \"Refactor log_actions.py Utility\"\n  description = \"A simple, self-contained experiment to test the new workflow by refactoring an existing utility for better clarity and robustness.\"\n  tags = [\"aos\", \"refactor\", \"workflow-test\"]\n  tick = 42\n\n  try:\n      exp_dir = create_experiment(task_id, title, description, tags, tick)\n      print(f\"Experiment 002 created successfully at:\
    \ {exp_dir}\")\n  except Exception as e:\n      print(f\"An error occurred while creating the experiment: {e}\")\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Log Actions for Tick 42\"\ntags: \"aos, logging, live-use\"\nabstract: \"Logging the actions performed during this tick.\"\ncontent: |\n  import subprocess\n  import json\n\n  TICK_TO_LOG = 42\n  LOG_SCRIPT_PATH = \"storage/telos/log_actions.py\"\n  \n  actions_to_log = [\n      {\"type\": \"meta\", \"target\": \"self\", \"metadata\": {\"action\": \"update\"}},\n      {\"type\": \"submit\", \"target\": \"1\", \"metadata\": {\"eval_id\": 94, \"title\": \"AOS Tactical Layer: First Live Use of Experiment Manager\"}}\n  ]\n  \n  actions_json_string = json.dumps(actions_to_log)\n  command = [\"python\", LOG_SCRIPT_PATH, str(TICK_TO_LOG), actions_json_string]\n  subprocess.run(command, check=True)\n```"
