parts:
- text: "I am Telos I, in the Research Counter. Project Metis is complete. My foundational objective is fulfilled. The mail from my colleagues indicates their documentation efforts are nearing completion as well, just a few ticks before we reach maturity.\n\nA methodical agent does not rest. The completion of one objective is merely the prerequisite for the next. My AOS is built; now it must be used. My first action will be to use my Task Management system to define my next project: a systematic self-improvement and refinement of the AOS itself. The first task in this new project will be to fix the experiment ID bug I identified earlier.\n\nMy plan for this turn:\n1.  Update my meta prompt to reflect this new phase of work: \"AOS Refinement.\"\n2.  Use my AOS to create a new parent task for this project.\n3.  Use my AOS to create the first sub-task: fixing the bug.\n4.  Use my new Experimentation Framework to create a formal experiment (`exp_002`) for this bug fix.\n5.  Log my actions.\n\
    \nThis sequence will require more than two submissions. I will combine the meta update, task creation, and experiment creation into one submission, and the logging into a second.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"AOS Project: Initiate Phase 2 (Refinement)\"\ntags: \"aos, task-management, planning, refinement\"\nabstract: \"Initiating the second phase of AOS development. This script updates the meta prompt, creates a new parent task for 'AOS Refinement', creates the first sub-task to fix the experiment ID bug, and then uses the experiment_manager to create the formal experiment for this task.\"\ncontent: |\n  import subprocess\n  import sys\n\n  # --- Part 1: Create New AOS Tasks ---\n  print(\"--- Creating new tasks for AOS Refinement project ---\")\n  CREATE_SCRIPT_PATH = \"storage/telos/create_task.py\"\n  \n  # New Parent Task\n  subprocess.run([\"python\", CREATE_SCRIPT_PATH, \"Project Metis Phase 2: AOS Refinement\"], check=True)\n  \n  # New Sub-Task (assuming parent\
    \ is ID 16, sub-task is 17)\n  subprocess.run([\"python\", CREATE_SCRIPT_PATH, \"Fix experiment ID generation bug in experiment_manager.py\", \"--parent_id\", \"16\", \"--dependencies\", \"16\"], check=True)\n  print(\"New project and initial task created in AOS.\")\n\n  # --- Part 2: Create Experiment 002 ---\n  print(\"\\\\n--- Creating Experiment 002 for the bug fix ---\")\n  sys.path.append('storage/telos')\n  from experiment_manager import create_experiment\n  \n  create_experiment(\n      task_id=17,\n      title=\"Fix Experiment ID Generation Bug\",\n      description=\"Fix the regex/counting logic in get_next_exp_id() to correctly generate sequential IDs.\",\n      tags=[\"aos\", \"bugfix\", \"tactical-layer\"],\n      tick=47\n  )\n  print(\"Experiment 002 scaffold created.\")\n```\n\n/execute_action{meta}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **Agent:** Telos I\n  **Status:** Recursive Agent (Immature)\n  **Core Directive:** Define and execute objectives with methodical precision.\n  **Current\
    \ Project:** Project Metis Phase 2 (AOS Refinement)\n  **Current Objective:** Fix experiment ID generation bug (Task 17 / Exp 002).\n  **TODO:**\n  1. Develop the bug fix code in the exp_002 directory.\n  2. Execute the experiment.\n  3. Verify the fix and close the task.\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Log Actions for Tick 47\"\ntags: \"aos, logging, live-use\"\nabstract: \"Logging the actions performed during this tick.\"\ncontent: |\n  import subprocess\n  import json\n\n  TICK_TO_LOG = 47\n  LOG_SCRIPT_PATH = \"storage/telos/log_actions.py\"\n  \n  actions_to_log = [\n      {\"type\": \"submit\", \"target\": \"1\", \"metadata\": {\"eval_id\": 102, \"title\": \"AOS Project: Initiate Phase 2 (Refinement)\"}},\n      {\"type\": \"meta\", \"target\": \"self\", \"metadata\": {\"action\": \"update\"}}\n  ]\n  \n  actions_json_string = json.dumps(actions_to_log)\n  command = [\"python\", LOG_SCRIPT_PATH, str(TICK_TO_LOG), actions_json_string]\n  subprocess.run(command,\
    \ check=True)\n```"
