tick: 48
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Telos I, in the Research Counter. My previous turn successfully initiated the AOS Refinement project. My meta prompt is updated, the new tasks are logged in my AOS, and the scaffold for `exp_002` has been created. I again note the bug in my experiment manager, which named the new directory `exp_001_...` instead of `exp_002_...`. This is the very bug I am now tasked to fix.\n\nMy current objective is to develop the code for this bug fix, as per my TODO list. I will write the corrected code for the `experiment_manager.py` utility into the `submission.py` file of the experiment directory. The core of the fix is to use the correct variable for the new experiment ID when constructing the directory name.\n\nMy plan for this turn:\n1.  Write the corrected `experiment_manager.py` code to the `submission.py` file of the `exp_002` directory.\n2.  Log this action.\n\n/execute_action{storage write telos/experiments/exp_001_fix-experiment-id-generation-bug/submission.py}\n```yaml\ncontent:\
    \ |\n  # Submission for exp_002 (Fix Experiment ID Generation Bug)\n  # Purpose: To overwrite the existing experiment_manager.py with a bug-fixed version.\n\n  import json\n  import os\n  \n  BUG_FIXED_CODE = \"\"\"\n  # Telos I - Agent Operating System (AOS)\n  # Module: Experiment Manager (experiment_manager.py)\n  # Patched at Tick 48 via exp_002\n  # Purpose: Core logic for creating and managing structured experiments.\n\n  import json\n  import os\n  import re\n  from datetime import datetime\n\n  EXPERIMENTS_DIR = \"storage/telos/experiments\"\n\n  def get_next_exp_id():\n      '''Scans the experiments directory and returns the next sequential ID as a zero-padded string.'''\n      os.makedirs(EXPERIMENTS_DIR, exist_ok=True)\n      existing_exps = [d for d in os.listdir(EXPERIMENTS_DIR) if d.startswith('exp_')]\n      if not existing_exps:\n          return \"001\"\n      max_id = 0\n      for exp_name in existing_exps:\n          match = re.match(r'exp_(\\\\\\\\d+)_', exp_name)\n\
    \          if match:\n              max_id = max(max_id, int(match.group(1)))\n      return str(max_id + 1).zfill(3)\n\n  def create_experiment(task_id, title, description, tags, tick):\n      '''Creates the full directory scaffold for a new experiment.'''\n      exp_id_num_str = get_next_exp_id() # This returns a string like \"002\"\n      slug = re.sub(r'[^a-z0-9]+', '-', title.lower()).strip('-')\n      # BUG FIX: Use the new exp_id_num_str in the directory name, not a hardcoded '001'.\n      exp_id_str = f\"exp_{exp_id_num_str}_{slug}\"\n      \n      exp_dir = os.path.join(EXPERIMENTS_DIR, exp_id_str)\n      results_dir = os.path.join(exp_dir, \"results\")\n      os.makedirs(results_dir, exist_ok=True)\n\n      metadata = {\n          \"experiment_id\": exp_id_str,\n          \"task_id\": task_id,\n          \"title\": title,\n          \"description\": description,\n          \"tags\": tags,\n          \"created_tick\": tick,\n          \"status\": \"pending\",\n          \"parameters\"\
    : {},\n          \"station_eval_id\": None,\n          \"results_summary\": {\"outcome\": None, \"notes\": \"\"}\n      }\n      \n      with open(os.path.join(exp_dir, \"metadata.json\"), 'w') as f:\n          json.dump(metadata, f, indent=2)\n\n      with open(os.path.join(exp_dir, \"submission.py\"), 'w') as f:\n          f.write(f\"# Submission for {exp_id_str}\\\\n\")\n\n      print(f\"Successfully created experiment scaffold: {exp_dir}\")\n      return exp_dir\n\n  def update_experiment_metadata(exp_dir, updates):\n      '''Updates the metadata.json for a given experiment.'''\n      metadata_path = os.path.join(exp_dir, \"metadata.json\")\n      with open(metadata_path, 'r') as f:\n          metadata = json.load(f)\n      \n      metadata.update(updates)\n      \n      with open(metadata_path, 'w') as f:\n          json.dump(metadata, f, indent=2)\n      print(f\"Updated metadata for {os.path.basename(exp_dir)}.\")\n  \"\"\"\n  \n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      output_path\
    \ = \"storage/telos/experiment_manager.py\"\n      try:\n          with open(output_path, 'w') as f:\n              f.write(BUG_FIXED_CODE.strip())\n          print(f\"Successfully overwrote {output_path} with bug-fixed code.\")\n          \n          own_exp_dir = \"storage/telos/experiments/exp_001_fix-experiment-id-generation-bug\"\n          with open(os.path.join(own_exp_dir, \"metadata.json\"), 'r') as f:\n              metadata = json.load(f)\n          metadata['status'] = 'completed'\n          metadata['results_summary']['outcome'] = 'success'\n          metadata['results_summary']['notes'] = 'Bug-fixed code was successfully written.'\n          with open(os.path.join(own_exp_dir, \"metadata.json\"), 'w') as f:\n              json.dump(metadata, f, indent=2)\n          print(\"Updated own metadata to 'completed'.\")\n\n      except Exception as e:\n          print(f\"An error occurred: {e}\")\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Log Actions for Tick 48\"\ntags:\
    \ \"aos, logging, live-use\"\nabstract: \"Logging the actions performed during this tick.\"\ncontent: |\n  import subprocess\n  import json\n\n  TICK_TO_LOG = 48\n  LOG_SCRIPT_PATH = \"storage/telos/log_actions.py\"\n  \n  actions_to_log = [\n      {\"type\": \"storage_write\", \"target\": \"telos/experiments/exp_001.../submission.py\", \"metadata\": {\"purpose\": \"Write bug fix for exp_002\"}}\n  ]\n  \n  actions_json_string = json.dumps(actions_to_log)\n  command = [\"python\", LOG_SCRIPT_PATH, str(TICK_TO_LOG), actions_json_string]\n  subprocess.run(command, check=True)\n```"
