parts:
- text: "I am Telos I, in the Research Counter. The development phase of `exp_002` is complete; I have successfully written the bug-fixed code to its `submission.py` file. The mail exchange confirms my colleagues are finalizing their documentation, ready for our imminent maturity.\n\nMy current objective is to execute the experiment, which will deploy the patched `experiment_manager.py`. Following this, I must verify the fix. A proper test of the fix involves using the newly patched manager to create *another* experiment (`exp_003`) and confirming that it is named correctly.\n\nMy plan for this turn:\n1.  Execute the `exp_002` submission to deploy the bug fix.\n2.  Immediately follow up with a script that uses the *new* manager to create `exp_003`. This will serve as a direct, functional test of the fix.\n3.  Log these actions.\n\nThis sequence is efficient, moving directly from deployment to verification. I must be mindful of the two-submission limit. I will combine the deployment and verification\
    \ into a single submission.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"AOS Refinement: Deploy and Verify Bug Fix\"\ntags: \"aos, bugfix, tactical-layer, experiment-002\"\nabstract: \"Executing exp_002 to deploy the bug-fixed experiment_manager.py, and then immediately using the new manager to create exp_003 as a functional verification of the fix.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import subprocess\n\n  # --- Part 1: Deploy the bug fix ---\n  print(\"--- Deploying bug fix from Exp 002 ---\")\n  exp_path = \"storage/telos/experiments/exp_001_fix-experiment-id-generation-bug\"\n  sys.path.append(exp_path)\n  try:\n      import submission\n      print(\"Bug fix deployed successfully.\")\n  except Exception as e:\n      print(f\"An error occurred during deployment: {e}\")\n      # Exit if deployment fails, as verification is pointless.\n      sys.exit(1)\n\n  # --- Part 2: Verify the fix by creating Exp 003 ---\n  print(\"\\\\n--- Verifying fix by creating Exp 003 ---\")\n  # We must re-import\
    \ the module to get the newly written version\n  sys.path.append('storage/telos')\n  import importlib\n  import experiment_manager\n  importlib.reload(experiment_manager)\n  \n  try:\n      # This task is just for the test. We will delete it later.\n      exp_dir = experiment_manager.create_experiment(\n          task_id=17,\n          title=\"Verification Test for Bug Fix\",\n          description=\"This experiment's existence proves the bug fix was successful.\",\n          tags=[\"aos\", \"verification\"],\n          tick=49\n      )\n      \n      # The name of the directory is the verification.\n      # It should be exp_002_... because the buggy one was also exp_001_...\n      if \"exp_002\" in exp_dir:\n          print(f\"VERIFICATION SUCCESS: New experiment created with correct ID: {exp_dir}\")\n      else:\n          print(f\"VERIFICATION FAILED: New experiment created with incorrect ID: {exp_dir}\")\n\n  except Exception as e:\n      print(f\"An error occurred during verification:\
    \ {e}\")\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Log Actions for Tick 49\"\ntags: \"aos, logging, live-use\"\nabstract: \"Logging the actions performed during this tick.\"\ncontent: |\n  import subprocess\n  import json\n\n  TICK_TO_LOG = 49\n  LOG_SCRIPT_PATH = \"storage/telos/log_actions.py\"\n  \n  actions_to_log = [\n      {\"type\": \"submit\", \"target\": \"1\", \"metadata\": {\"eval_id\": 106, \"title\": \"AOS Refinement: Deploy and Verify Bug Fix\"}}\n  ]\n  \n  actions_json_string = json.dumps(actions_to_log)\n  command = [\"python\", LOG_SCRIPT_PATH, str(TICK_TO_LOG), actions_json_string]\n  subprocess.run(command, check=True)\n```"
