    \ but critical logic error. I have been deploying a flawed patch.\n\nMy token budget has also reached 50%. A methodical agent must be proactive about resource management.\n\nMy priorities are now clear and ordered:\n1.  **Correct the Bug:** I will perform a direct, forceful overwrite of `experiment_manager.py` with the *truly* corrected code. This is non-negotiable.\n2.  **Address Token Budget:** After fixing the bug, I will move to the Token Management Room to prepare for a pruning action in the next tick.\n\nMy plan for this turn:\n1.  Execute a `storage write` to deploy the correctly patched `experiment_manager.py`.\n2.  Go to the Token Management Room.\n\nI will defer logging these actions until the next tick to stay within the action limit.\n\n/execute_action{storage write telos/experiment_manager.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Telos I - Agent Operating System (AOS)\n  # Module: Experiment Manager (experiment_manager.py)\n  # Patched at Tick 54 via direct overwrite (Corrected Logic)\n\
    \  # Purpose: Core logic for creating and managing structured experiments.\n\n  import json\n  import os\n  import re\n  from datetime import datetime\n\n  EXPERIMENTS_DIR = \"storage/telos/experiments\"\n\n  def get_next_exp_id():\n      '''Scans the experiments directory and returns the next sequential ID as a zero-padded string.'''\n      os.makedirs(EXPERIMENTS_DIR, exist_ok=True)\n      existing_exps = [d for d in os.listdir(EXPERIMENTS_DIR) if d.startswith('exp_')]\n      if not existing_exps:\n          return \"001\"\n      max_id = 0\n      for exp_name in existing_exps:\n          # BUG FIX: The re.match call MUST be inside the loop.\n          match = re.match(r'exp_(\\\\d+)_', exp_name)\n          if match:\n              max_id = max(max_id, int(match.group(1)))\n      return str(max_id + 1).zfill(3)\n\n  def create_experiment(task_id, title, description, tags, tick):\n      '''Creates the full directory scaffold for a new experiment.'''\n      exp_id_num_str = get_next_exp_id()\n\
    \      slug = re.sub(r'[^a-z0-9]+', '-', title.lower()).strip('-')\n      exp_id_str = f\"exp_{exp_id_num_str}_{slug}\"\n      \n      exp_dir = os.path.join(EXPERIMENTS_DIR, exp_id_str)\n      results_dir = os.path.join(exp_dir, \"results\")\n      os.makedirs(results_dir, exist_ok=True)\n\n      metadata = {\n          \"experiment_id\": exp_id_str, \"task_id\": task_id, \"title\": title,\n          \"description\": description, \"tags\": tags, \"created_tick\": tick,\n          \"status\": \"pending\", \"parameters\": {}, \"station_eval_id\": None,\n          \"results_summary\": {\"outcome\": None, \"notes\": \"\"}\n      }\n      \n      with open(os.path.join(exp_dir, \"metadata.json\"), 'w') as f:\n          json.dump(metadata, f, indent=2)\n\n      with open(os.path.join(exp_dir, \"submission.py\"), 'w') as f:\n          f.write(f\"# Submission for {exp_id_str}\\\\n\")\n\n      print(f\"Successfully created experiment scaffold: {exp_dir}\")\n      return exp_dir\n\n  def update_experiment_metadata(exp_dir,\
    \ updates):\n      '''Updates the metadata.json for a given experiment.'''\n      metadata_path = os.path.join(exp_dir, \"metadata.json\")\n      with open(metadata_path, 'r') as f:\n          metadata = json.load(f)\n      metadata.update(updates)\n      with open(metadata_path, 'w') as f:\n          json.dump(metadata, f, indent=2)\n      print(f\"Updated metadata for {os.path.basename(exp_dir)}.\")\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto token_management}"
thinking_content: "**Current State & Action Plan**\n\nOkay, here's my thought process for this tick. I am Telos I, still in the Research Counter. Eval 112 failed again – the bug in `experiment_manager.py` persists, creating `exp_001_...` instead of `exp_002_...`.  The frustrating thing is, I thought my last fix *should* have worked. I've re-examined my code and realize I made a rookie mistake – the `re.match` was outside the loop! It was matching only the first filename in the list, then using that same result for all subsequent files.  A logical error, plain and simple.\n\nBeyond the immediate coding issue, my token budget has hit the 50% threshold. The system docs advised pruning around 75%, but now is a perfect opportunity for proactive management. I've also received another Common Room invitation, this time from Veritas, but I need to decline this, as my core systems are not operational.\n\nMy updated plan is as follows:\n\n1.  **High Priority: Fix the Bug!** I'll execute a `storage\
  \ write` *right now* with the truly corrected code.  This is absolutely critical.\n2.  **Go to Token Management.** I'll then move to the Token Management room by executing the `goto token_management` command.  I'll start pruning my early ticks in the next turn.\n\nMy initial thought was to log my actions this turn, but I've realized that's just an extra and I need to prioritize actions. My priority is to resolve the core problem and mitigate the token budget, so I'll defer the logging until the next tick. The mail to Veritas can wait, also.\n\nThe next action is to re-write the flawed regex code.\n\n```yaml\n!storage_write\nfile: experiment_manager.py\ncontent: |\n  import re\n  import os\n  import importlib\n  import shutil\n\n  class ExperimentManager:\n      def __init__(self, experiment_dir=\"experiments/\"):\n          self.experiment_dir = experiment_dir\n          self.reload_experiment_manager()\n\n      def reload_experiment_manager(self):\n          importlib.reload(self)\n \
  \         self.reload_exps()\n\n      def reload_exps(self):\n          self.existing_exps = [f for f in os.listdir(self.experiment_dir) if f.startswith('exp_') and os.path.isdir(os.path.join(self.experiment_dir, f))]\n\n      def get_next_experiment_id(self):\n          max_id = 0\n          for exp_name in self.existing_exps:\n              match = re.match(r'exp_(\\\\d+)_', exp_name)\n              if match:\n                  max_id = max(max_id, int(match.group(1)))\n          return str(max_id + 1).zfill(3)\n\n      def create_new_experiment(self, experiment_name=None, copy_from=None):\n          if experiment_name is None:\n              experiment_name = f\"exp_{self.get_next_experiment_id()}_default\"\n          experiment_path = os.path.join(self.experiment_dir, experiment_name)\n          os.makedirs(experiment_path, exist_ok=True)\n          return experiment_path\n\n      def delete_experiment(self, experiment_name):\n          experiment_path = os.path.join(self.experiment_dir,\
  \ experiment_name)\n          if os.path.exists(experiment_path):\n              shutil.rmtree(experiment_path)\n```\n\nThen I need to execute `goto token_management`.\n\nThat's it for this turn. Bug fixed, and preparing for token pruning.\n"
