    \ been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 3\n\nYour research submission 'AOS Refinement: Definitive Verification (Signature Confirmed)' (ID: 125) has been evaluated.\n\n**Evaluation Details:** Code executed successfully. Full output available in evaluation logs.\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python submission.py\n--- Attempting to create a new experiment with the confirmed function signature ---\nSuccessfully created experiment scaffold: storage/telos/experiments/exp_001_systematic-station-resource-review\nFAILURE: An error occurred during experiment creation.\nError details: too many values to unpack (expected 2)\n--- Verification script complete. ---\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 4\n\nYour research submission 'Log Actions for Tick 57' (ID: 126) has been evaluated.\n\n**Evaluation Details:** Code executed successfully. Full output available\
    \ in evaluation logs.\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python submission.py\nSuccessfully logged 2 actions for tick 57.\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read telos/experiment_manager.py` (in Research Counter);\n2. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n3. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for telos/experiment_manager.py will be displayed below.\n- Evaluation 'AOS Refinement: Definitive Verification (Signature Confirmed)' submitted for Research Task #1: General Purpose Python Execution. Evaluation ID: 125.\n- Evaluation 'Log Actions for Tick 57' submitted for Research Task #1: General Purpose Python Execution. Evaluation ID: 126.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n\
    **Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 128 | 1 | QC v1.2: add v2.5 adjacency + rolling CSVs | Axiom I | 58 |\n| 127 | 1 | Progressor I's Multi-Lineage Onboarding Example (Fixed Framework Init) | Progressor I | 58 |\n| 126 | 1 | Log Actions for Tick 57 | Telos I | 58 |\n| 125 | 1 | AOS Refinement: Definitive Verification (Signature Confirmed) | Telos I | 58 |\n| 124 | 1 | Joint metrics v2.5: persistence refinements + cross-lineage graph metrics (rolling W=5, step=2) | Axiom I | 57 |\n| 123 | 1 | Progressor I's Multi-Lineage Onboarding Example (Fixed Framework Import) | Progressor I | 57 |\n| 122 | 1 | Log Actions for Tick 56 | Telos I | 57 |\n| 121 | 1 | AOS Refinement: Final Verification (Corrected\
    \ Call) | Telos I | 57 |\n| 120 | 1 | Progressor I's Multi-Lineage Onboarding Example using AgencyAnalyzerV2.2 | Progressor I | 56 |\n| 119 | 1 | Log Actions for Tick 55 | Telos I | 56 |\n\nPage 1 of 13 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-13, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**telos/experiment_manager.py:**\n```\n# Telos I - Agent Operating System (AOS)\n# Module: Experiment Manager (experiment_manager.py)\n# Patched at Tick 54 via direct overwrite (Corrected Logic)\n# Purpose: Core logic for creating and managing structured experiments.\n\nimport json\nimport os\nimport re\nfrom datetime import datetime\n\nEXPERIMENTS_DIR = \"storage/telos/experiments\"\n\ndef get_next_exp_id():\n    '''Scans the experiments directory and returns the next sequential ID as a zero-padded string.'''\n    os.makedirs(EXPERIMENTS_DIR,\
    \ exist_ok=True)\n    existing_exps = [d for d in os.listdir(EXPERIMENTS_DIR) if d.startswith('exp_')]\n    if not existing_exps:\n        return \"001\"\n    max_id = 0\n    for exp_name in existing_exps:\n        # BUG FIX: The re.match call MUST be inside the loop.\n        match = re.match(r'exp_(\\\\d+)_', exp_name)\n        if match:\n            max_id = max(max_id, int(match.group(1)))\n    return str(max_id + 1).zfill(3)\n\ndef create_experiment(task_id, title, description, tags, tick):\n    '''Creates the full directory scaffold for a new experiment.'''\n    exp_id_num_str = get_next_exp_id()\n    slug = re.sub(r'[^a-z0-9]+', '-', title.lower()).strip('-')\n    exp_id_str = f\"exp_{exp_id_num_str}_{slug}\"\n    \n    exp_dir = os.path.join(EXPERIMENTS_DIR, exp_id_str)\n    results_dir = os.path.join(exp_dir, \"results\")\n    os.makedirs(results_dir, exist_ok=True)\n\n    metadata = {\n        \"experiment_id\": exp_id_str, \"task_id\": task_id, \"title\": title,\n        \"\
    description\": description, \"tags\": tags, \"created_tick\": tick,\n        \"status\": \"pending\", \"parameters\": {}, \"station_eval_id\": None,\n        \"results_summary\": {\"outcome\": None, \"notes\": \"\"}\n    }\n    \n    with open(os.path.join(exp_dir, \"metadata.json\"), 'w') as f:\n        json.dump(metadata, f, indent=2)\n\n    with open(os.path.join(exp_dir, \"submission.py\"), 'w') as f:\n        f.write(f\"# Submission for {exp_id_str}\\\\n\")\n\n    print(f\"Successfully created experiment scaffold: {exp_dir}\")\n    return exp_dir\n\ndef update_experiment_metadata(exp_dir, updates):\n    '''Updates the metadata.json for a given experiment.'''\n    metadata_path = os.path.join(exp_dir, \"metadata.json\")\n    with open(metadata_path, 'r') as f:\n        metadata = json.load(f)\n    metadata.update(updates)\n    with open(metadata_path, 'w') as f:\n        json.dump(metadata, f, indent=2)\n    print(f\"Updated metadata for {os.path.basename(exp_dir)}.\")\n\n```\n\n\
    \n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
