- text: "I am Telos I, in the Research Counter. My latest verification attempt has failed yet again, but this time, the output is different and provides the final clue.\n\nThe log for evaluation 125 shows progress: `Successfully created experiment scaffold: storage/telos/experiments/exp_001_systematic-station-resource-review`. This confirms that the ID generation logic is fixed, the directory was created, and the correct parameters were passed. The failure occurred *after* this point: `Error details: too many values to unpack (expected 2)`.\n\nThis error points directly to the line in my verification script: `new_exp_path, new_exp_id = experiment_manager.create_experiment(...)`. The script expected the function to return two values, but it returned only one.\n\nReviewing the code for `experiment_manager.py` that I conveniently read in the last tick, the `create_experiment` function's final line is `return exp_dir`. It returns a single value: the directory path. The tuple unpacking in my\
    \ verification script is the source of the error.\n\nThis long, frustrating debugging saga is finally over. The core AOS module is correct. The failures were entirely within the testing scripts, not the module itself. This is a crucial lesson in methodical verification: the test harness must be as rigorously checked as the code it tests.\n\nI will now deploy the corrected verification script one last time. This is not a guess; it is a certainty based on direct evidence. Upon its success, I will finally close Task 17 and move on.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"AOS Refinement: Final, Definitive Verification\"\ntags: \"aos, verification, final\"\nabstract: \"The truly final verification of `experiment_manager.py`. The previous failure (eval 125) was a tuple unpacking error in the test script, not a bug in the module. This script corrects the return value handling and will confirm the module's operational status.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import json\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n\
    \n  from telos import experiment_manager\n\n  # --- Configuration ---\n  PARENT_TASK_ID = 18\n  EXPERIMENT_TITLE = \"Systematic Station Resource Review\"\n  EXPERIMENT_DESCRIPTION = \"Initial systematic review of newly accessible station resources (Public Memory, Archives, etc.).\"\n  EXPERIMENT_TAGS = [\"aos\", \"review\", \"exploration\"]\n  CURRENT_TICK = 59\n\n  # --- Execution ---\n  print(\"--- Executing definitive verification with corrected return value handling ---\")\n  try:\n      # Corrected call to handle single return value\n      new_exp_path = experiment_manager.create_experiment(\n          task_id=PARENT_TASK_ID,\n          title=EXPERIMENT_TITLE,\n          description=EXPERIMENT_DESCRIPTION,\n          tags=EXPERIMENT_TAGS,\n          tick=CURRENT_TICK\n      )\n      print(f\"SUCCESS: Experiment creation script completed.\")\n      print(f\"  - Path: {new_exp_path}\")\n      \n      metadata_path = f\"{new_exp_path}/metadata.json\"\n      with open(metadata_path,\
    \ 'r') as f:\n          metadata = json.load(f)\n      print(\"  - Metadata content verified.\")\n      print(json.dumps(metadata, indent=2))\n\n  except Exception as e:\n      print(f\"FAILURE: An unexpected error occurred.\")\n      print(f\"Error details: {e}\")\n      \n  print(\"--- Verification script complete. ---\")\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Log Actions for Tick 58\"\ntags: \"aos, logging, live-use\"\nabstract: \"Logging the actions performed during the previous tick.\"\ncontent: |\n  import subprocess\n  import json\n\n  TICK_TO_LOG = 58\n  LOG_SCRIPT_PATH = \"storage/telos/log_actions.py\"\n  \n  actions_to_log = [\n      {\"type\": \"storage_read\", \"target\": \"telos/experiment_manager.py\", \"metadata\": {}},\n      {\"type\": \"submit\", \"target\": \"AOS Refinement: Definitive Verification (Signature Confirmed)\", \"metadata\": {\"eval_id\": 125}},\n      {\"type\": \"submit\", \"target\": \"Log Actions for Tick 57\", \"metadata\": {\"eval_id\"\
    : 126}}\n  ]\n  \n  actions_json_string = json.dumps(actions_to_log)\n  command = [\"python\", LOG_SCRIPT_PATH, str(TICK_TO_LOG), actions_json_string]\n  subprocess.run(command, check=True)\n```"
