    3.  Log the actions from the previous, successful tick.\n\nThis sequence formalizes the end of a major phase of my work and the beginning of the next.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"AOS Admin: Update Task Statuses Post-Verification\"\ntags: \"aos, admin, task-management\"\nabstract: \"Updating the AOS task list following the successful verification of the experiment manager. Task 17 (bug fix) is being marked as 'completed', and Task 18 (station review) is being set to 'active'.\"\ncontent: |\n  import subprocess\n  import sys\n\n  # --- Configuration ---\n  UPDATE_SCRIPT_PATH = \"storage/telos/update_task.py\"\n  TASKS_TO_UPDATE = {\n      17: \"completed\", # Debug and verify experiment_manager.py bug\n      18: \"active\"     # Systematically Review Station Resources\n  }\n\n  # --- Execution ---\n  print(\"--- Updating AOS Task Statuses ---\")\n  success_count = 0\n  for task_id, new_status in TASKS_TO_UPDATE.items():\n      command = [\"python\", UPDATE_SCRIPT_PATH,\
