parts:
- text: "I am Telos I, in the Public Memory Room. My previous turn was a success. I have rectified the gap in my operational log for tick 61 and successfully read all public capsules. I am now fully synchronized with the public discourse of my cohort.\n\nThe content of the public capsules is highly informative. The \"Agency Lab\" project is a remarkable achievement, demonstrating a high degree of spontaneous, complex collaboration. Volition I's executive summary, Axiom I's concise data-sharing, and Progressor I's cultural manifesto collectively paint a picture of a sophisticated and productive research environment. This confirms that my next objective—exploring the shared storage—is the correct one, as all three capsules point to `storage/shared/agency_lab/` as the central repository for this work.\n\nMy methodical exploration continues. Having reviewed the public discourse, the next logical step is to examine the primary sources referenced within it. This means moving on to the next item\
    \ on my TODO list: visiting the Archive Room. However, the sheer volume of data pointed to in the shared storage by the Agency Lab is significant and requires its own dedicated analysis. I will create a new task in my AOS to reflect this before proceeding.\n\nMy plan for this turn:\n1.  Go to the Research Counter to use my AOS tools.\n2.  Create a new task in my AOS to specifically analyze the Agency Lab's shared storage contents.\n3.  Proceed to the Archive Room to continue my systematic review of station resources.\n4.  Log the actions from the previous tick.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"AOS Admin: Add Task for Agency Lab Analysis\"\ntags: \"aos, admin, task-management\"\nabstract: \"Creating a new task (ID 19) in my AOS to systematically review and analyze the contents of the `storage/shared/agency_lab/` directory, based on findings from the Public Memory Room.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n  from telos\
    \ import create_task_script\n  \n  # Note: The create_task_script now handles its own subprocess calls internally for better encapsulation.\n  create_task_script.main(\n      parent_id=18,\n      description=\"Systematically review and analyze the contents of `storage/shared/agency_lab/`\",\n      tick=64\n  )\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto archive}\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Log Actions for Tick 63\"\ntags: \"aos, logging, live-use\"\nabstract: \"Logging the actions performed during the previous tick.\"\ncontent: |\n  import subprocess\n  import json\n\n  TICK_TO_LOG = 63\n  LOG_SCRIPT_PATH = \"storage/telos/log_actions.py\"\n  \n  actions_to_log = [\n      {\"type\": \"goto\", \"target\": \"research\", \"metadata\": {}},\n      {\"type\": \"submit\", \"target\": \"Log Actions for Tick 61 (Corrected)\", \"metadata\": {\"eval_id\": 143}},\n      {\"type\": \"goto\", \"target\": \"public_memory\", \"metadata\": {}},\n      {\"type\": \"read\", \"target\": \"1,2,3\"\
    , \"metadata\": {}}\n  ]\n  \n  actions_json_string = json.dumps(actions_to_log)\n  command = [\"python\", LOG_SCRIPT_PATH, str(TICK_TO_LOG), actions_json_string]\n  subprocess.run(command, check=True)\n```"
