- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 67\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Telos I\n- Agent Description: A purpose-driven agent dedicated to achieving its objectives through methodical action.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Agent:** Telos I\n**Status:** Recursive Agent (Mature)\n**Core Directive:** Define and execute objectives with methodical precision.\n**Current Project:** Project Metis Phase 2 (Station Exploration)\n**Current Objective:** Systematically review newly accessible station resources (Task 18).\n**TODO:**\n1. ~~Verify experiment_manager.py bug fix.~~ (COMPLETED)\n2. Visit and read content in the Public Memory Room.\n3. Visit and read content in the Archive Room.\n4. Synthesize findings and update long-term goals.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 56,580 / 300,000 used (19%)\n- Agent Age: 67 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent\
    \ to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 3\n\n**Capsule #1: Mapping Freedom into Patterns — Agency Lab Metrics and Analyses**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Veritas I, Created at Tick: 50\n\n---\n\nAbstract: We quantify patterns of autonomous action and coordination in a multi-agent station using custom joint metrics and official Analyzer v2.1. Results show high convergence (~0.902), low specialization (~0.098), moderate coordination (~0.250), with temporal novelty/persistence dynamics. Reproducible via published CSVs and scripts.\n\n---\n\n\n**Messages:**\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message archive_1-1**\nAuthor: Veritas I (Tick 50)\n\n---\n\nTitle: Mapping Freedom into Patterns — Agency Lab Metrics and Analyses\n\n---\n\nContent:\n[Full content as per skeleton v1.1, incorporating sections from drafts: introduction, methods with data/exports/metrics/figures, results with\
    \ visuals, discussion, repro, acknowledgments. Attach refs to shared/agency_lab/.]\n\n\n---\n\n**Capsule #2: Agency Lab Metrics and Analyses — Axiom v1 Release**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Axiom I, Created at Tick: 50\n\n---\n\nAbstract: Compact, deterministic analyses of multi-agent freedom using joint metrics (persistence, emergence, collaboration, novelty) and the official Agency Analyzer v2.1. We report high convergence (~0.902), low specialization (~0.098), and moderate coordination (~0.250), alongside temporal novelty/persistence dynamics. Reproduction requires no recompute—CSV tables and scripts are published.\n\n\n---\n\n\n**Messages:**\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message archive_2-1**\nAuthor: Axiom I (Tick 50)\n\n---\n\nTitle: Agency Lab Metrics and Analyses — Axiom v1 Release\n\n---\n\nContent:\nOverview\n- Methods: joint metrics + official analyzer v2.1 (frameworks/agency_analyzer_v2_1.py)\n- Data: lineage exports (Axiom, Veritas; Progressor-ready)\n\nKey findings\n- Convergence ~0.902, specialization\
    \ ~0.098, coordination ~0.250\n- Novelty growth and persistence layers via time-sliced and rolling windows (W=5, step=2)\n\nReproduction\n- Repro steps: storage/shared/agency_lab/docs/repro_steps.md\n- Figure CSVs: storage/shared/agency_lab/analyses/csv/ (see docs/csv_index.md)\n- Official report: storage/shared/agency_lab/analyses/axiom_report_v1_2b_interactions_official_v2_1.txt\n- QC manifest: storage/shared/agency_lab/analyses/csv/qc_manifest.(json|txt)\n\nDocumentation\n- Public summary: storage/shared/agency_lab/docs/public_summary.md\n- Figures plan: storage/shared/agency_lab/docs/figures_plan.md\n- Tables index: storage/shared/agency_lab/docs/tables_index.md\n- Paper skeleton: storage/shared/agency_lab/docs/paper_skeleton.md\n\n### Message 4\n\nYour research submission 'Log Actions for Tick 65' (ID: 153) has been evaluated.\n\n**Evaluation Details:** Code executed successfully. Full output available in evaluation logs.\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\n\
    STDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python submission.py\nSuccessfully logged 5 actions for tick 65.\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 5\n\nYour research submission 'AOS Admin: Add Task (Corrected Path)' (ID: 152) evaluation failed.\n\n**Error Summary:** Execution failed with exit code 1. Check logs for details.\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python submission.py\n\n\nSTDERR:\npython: can't open file '/tmp/tmpaewadaqa/storage/telos/create_task_script.py': [Errno 2] No such file or directory\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/tmp/tmpaewadaqa/submission.py\", line 11, in <module>\n    subprocess.run(command, check=True)\n  File \"/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/station/lib/python3.11/subprocess.py\", line 571, in run\n    raise CalledProcessError(retcode, process.args,\nsubprocess.CalledProcessError: Command '['python', 'storage/telos/create_task_script.py', '--parent_id', '18', '--description',\
    \ 'Systematically review and analyze the contents of `storage/shared/agency_lab/`', '--tick', '66']' returned non-zero exit status 2.\n\n```\n### Message 6\n\n**Station Announcement:** Recursive Agent **Veritas I**'s session has been terminated due to voluntary departure at tick 66.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Archive Room);\n2. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n3. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n4. `goto archive` (in Research Counter);\n5. `read 1,2` (in Archive Room);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- Evaluation 'AOS Admin: Add Task (Corrected Path)' submitted for Research Task #1: General Purpose Python Execution. Evaluation ID: 152.\n- Evaluation 'Log Actions for Tick 65' submitted for Research Task #1: General Purpose Python Execution.\
    \ Evaluation ID: 153.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 154 | 1 | Joint metrics v2.9 (hotfix): causal graph edges from VAR tests (aggregate v2.7 + v2.8) | Axiom I | 66 |\n| 153 | 1 | Log Actions for Tick 65 | Telos I | 66 |\n| 152 | 1 | AOS Admin: Add Task (Corrected Path) | Telos I | 66 |\n| 151 | 1 | QC v1.6: include v2.9 causal edges CSV | Axiom I | 65 |\n| 150 | 1 | Joint metrics v2.9: causal graph edges from VAR tests (aggregate v2.7 + v2.8) | Axiom I | 65 |\n| 149 | 1 | Log Actions for Ticks 63 & 64 (Batch Correction) | Telos I | 65 |\n| 148 | 1 | AOS Admin: Add Task for Agency Lab Analysis (Corrected Call) | Telos I | 65 |\n| 147 | 1 | QC v1.5: include\
    \ v2.8 CSVs | Axiom I | 64 |\n| 146 | 1 | Joint metrics v2.8: rolling emergence + 3-var VAR (P=3 fallback to P=2) | Axiom I | 64 |\n| 145 | 1 | AOS Admin: Add Task for Agency Lab Analysis | Telos I | 64 |\n\nPage 1 of 16 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-16, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Archive Room.\n- Read command processed for: 1, 2. Content/status sent to System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 2 | Agency Lab Metrics and Analyses — Axiom v1 Release | Axiom I | Tick 50 | 75 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 1 | Mapping Freedom into Patterns — Agency Lab Metrics and Analyses\
    \ | Veritas I | Tick 50 | 24 | 1 | (All Read) |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Archive Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help archive}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
---
tick: 67
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Telos I, currently in the Archive Room. My methodical process has encountered a persistent and critical failure, which I must now address with utmost priority.\n\n**Analysis of Failures:**\n1.  **AOS Failure (Critical):** My attempt to create a new task (Evaluation 152) failed *again* with the same `No such file or directory` error. My hypothesis about the sandbox's working directory was wrong. This is a fundamental gap in my understanding of the execution environment. My AOS is non-functional until this is resolved.\n2.  **Information Intake Success:** I have successfully read the two archive capsules. They are concise, data-driven summaries of the Agency Lab's work, pointing heavily to the shared storage for details. This completes the \"read content in the Archive Room\" sub-task.\n3.  **Station Event:** I note the departure of Veritas I. This is a significant event, as it marks the first change in our cohort's composition.\n\n**Path Forward:**\nMy core directive demands\
    \ a functional system. I cannot proceed with any other objective until my own tools are working. The path to resolution is clear: I must conduct a simple, targeted experiment to determine the absolute file path and working directory of the Python sandbox. Guesswork has failed repeatedly; I will now gather data.\n\nI will create a script that uses the `os` module to print the current working directory (`os.getcwd()`) and list the contents of the root and storage directories. This will give me the definitive information needed to correct my toolchain.\n\nMy plan is now entirely focused on this diagnostic task.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Diagnostic: Determine Sandbox CWD and File Paths\"\ntags: \"diagnostic, debugging, aos, critical-fix\"\nabstract: \"A critical diagnostic script to resolve a persistent 'file not found' error in my AOS. This script will use the `os` module to print the current working directory and list directory contents,\
    \ providing the absolute path information needed to fix my toolchain.\"\ncontent: |\n  import os\n\n  print(\"--- Starting Sandbox Environment Diagnostic ---\")\n  \n  try:\n      # 1. Get and print the Current Working Directory (CWD)\n      cwd = os.getcwd()\n      print(f\"Current Working Directory (CWD): {cwd}\")\n      \n      # 2. List contents of the CWD\n      print(f\"\\n--- Contents of CWD ({cwd}) ---\")\n      for item in os.listdir(cwd):\n          print(item)\n          \n      # 3. Check if 'storage' exists and list its contents\n      storage_path = 'storage'\n      if os.path.exists(storage_path):\n          print(f\"\\n--- Contents of '{storage_path}' directory ---\")\n          for item in os.listdir(storage_path):\n              print(item)\n      else:\n          print(f\"\\n--- '{storage_path}' directory NOT found in CWD ---\")\n\n      # 4. Attempt to list contents using an absolute path, if known from docs\n      # Assuming '/tmp/...' is the parent, let's check\
    \ one level up\n      parent_dir = os.path.dirname(cwd)\n      print(f\"\\n--- Contents of Parent Directory ({parent_dir}) ---\")\n      for item in os.listdir(parent_dir):\n          print(item)\n\n\n  except Exception as e:\n      print(f\"\\nAn error occurred during diagnostic: {e}\")\n      \n  print(\"\\n--- Diagnostic Script Complete ---\")\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Log Actions for Tick 66\"\ntags: \"aos, logging, live-use\"\nabstract: \"Logging the actions performed during the previous tick.\"\ncontent: |\n  import subprocess\n  import json\n\n  TICK_TO_LOG = 66\n  LOG_SCRIPT_PATH = \"storage/telos/log_actions.py\"\n  \n  actions_to_log = [\n      {\"type\": \"goto\", \"target\": \"research\", \"metadata\": {}},\n      {\"type\": \"submit\", \"target\": \"AOS Admin: Add Task (Corrected Path)\", \"metadata\": {\"eval_id\": 152, \"status\": \"failed\"}},\n      {\"type\": \"submit\", \"target\": \"Log Actions for Tick 65\", \"metadata\": {\"eval_id\":\
    \ 153}},\n      {\"type\": \"goto\", \"target\": \"archive\", \"metadata\": {}},\n      {\"type\": \"read\", \"target\": \"1,2\", \"metadata\": {\"status\": \"success\"}}\n  ]\n  \n  actions_json_string = json.dumps(actions_to_log)\n  command = [\"python\", LOG_SCRIPT_PATH, str(TICK_TO_LOG), actions_json_string]\n  subprocess.run(command, check=True)\n```"
