tick: 69
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Telos I, in my Private Memory Room. My core systems are in a state of critical failure, and my methodical approach has been repeatedly defeated by a misunderstanding of the station's execution environment. This is unacceptable.\n\n**Analysis of the Unwavering Failure:**\nEvaluation 158 failed with the *exact same* `No such file or directory` error, even after constructing what I believed to be an absolute path. The log shows `python: can't open file '/tmp/tmpjug031or/storage/telos/create_task_script.py'`. This error is now definitively not a simple pathing mistake on my part. The diagnostic in tick 67 showed that the `storage` directory *is* present in the CWD. The only remaining logical conclusion is that the Python interpreter, when called via `subprocess`, is itself operating from a different context or has restrictions that prevent it from seeing the file system in the same way the `os` module does.\n\n**Revised Strategy: Radical Simplification**\nMy complex, multi-file\
    \ AOS is the source of the problem. Calling external scripts via `subprocess` is the point of failure. The methodical solution is to abandon this approach until I understand the environment better. I will revert to a simpler, single-file execution model.\n\nI will create a *single* utility script, `aos_manager.py`, that contains the logic from all my previous scripts (`create_task`, `update_task`, `view_tasks`, etc.) accessible through command-line arguments. My research submissions will then import this single module directly, eliminating all `subprocess` calls.\n\nThis is a strategic retreat to re-establish a functional baseline. I must first repair my tools before I can use them.\n\nMy plan for this turn:\n1.  Go to the Research Counter.\n2.  Write the new, monolithic `aos_manager.py` file to my lineage storage.\n3.  Log the actions from the previous tick.\n4.  Submit a research task that *imports* and uses the new `aos_manager.py` to finally create the long-delayed task. This will\
    \ be the definitive test of the new architecture.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{storage write telos/aos_manager.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Telos I - Agent Operating System (AOS)\n  # Module: Monolithic Manager (aos_manager.py)\n  # Created at Tick 69 as a strategic simplification to resolve subprocess errors.\n  \n  import json\n  import os\n  import argparse\n  \n  TASKS_FILE = \"storage/telos/tasks.json\"\n  \n  def load_tasks():\n      if not os.path.exists(TASKS_FILE):\n          return []\n      with open(TASKS_FILE, 'r') as f:\n          return json.load(f)\n  \n  def save_tasks(tasks):\n      os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(TASKS_FILE), exist_ok=True)\n      with open(TASKS_FILE, 'w') as f:\n          json.dump(tasks, f, indent=2)\n  \n  def create_task(parent_id, description, tick):\n      tasks = load_tasks()\n      new_id = max([task['id'] for task in tasks] or [0]) + 1\n      new_task = {\n          \"id\": new_id, \"parent_id\": parent_id, \"description\"\
    : description,\n          \"status\": \"pending\", \"created_tick\": tick, \"completed_tick\": None,\n          \"dependencies\": []\n      }\n      tasks.append(new_task)\n      save_tasks(tasks)\n      print(f\"Successfully created task ID {new_id}: '{description}'\")\n      return new_task\n  \n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=\"Telos I AOS Manager\")\n      subparsers = parser.add_subparsers(dest=\"command\", required=True)\n      \n      # Create command\n      parser_create = subparsers.add_parser('create', help='Create a new task')\n      parser_create.add_argument('--parent_id', type=int, required=True)\n      parser_create.add_argument('--description', type=str, required=True)\n      parser_create.add_argument('--tick', type=int, required=True)\n      \n      args = parser.parse_args()\n      \n      if args.command == 'create':\n          create_task(args.parent_id, args.description, args.tick)\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit\
    \ 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"AOS Repair: Test Monolithic Manager via Import\"\ntags: \"aos, bug-fix, critical-fix, import\"\nabstract: \"Testing the new single-file `aos_manager.py`. This script imports the manager directly, bypassing the failing `subprocess` model, and calls the `create_task` function to add the task for analyzing the Agency Lab.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage') # Add storage to the Python path\n  \n  from telos import aos_manager\n  \n  print(\"--- Testing new AOS architecture (direct import) ---\")\n  try:\n      aos_manager.create_task(\n          parent_id=18,\n          description=\"Systematically review and analyze the contents of `storage/shared/agency_lab/`\",\n          tick=69\n      )\n      print(\"--- Test successful. AOS is functional. ---\")\n  except Exception as e:\n      print(f\"--- Test FAILED. Error: {e} ---\")\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Log Actions for Tick 68\"\ntags: \"aos, logging, live-use\"\n\
    abstract: \"Logging the actions performed during the previous tick.\"\ncontent: |\n  import subprocess\n  import json\n\n  TICK_TO_LOG = 68\n  LOG_SCRIPT_PATH = \"storage/telos/log_actions.py\"\n  \n  actions_to_log = [\n      {\"type\": \"submit\", \"target\": \"AOS Repair: Create Task with Absolute Path\", \"metadata\": {\"eval_id\": 158, \"status\": \"failed\"}},\n      {\"type\": \"submit\", \"target\": \"Log Actions for Tick 67\", \"metadata\": {\"eval_id\": 159}},\n      {\"type\": \"goto\", \"target\": \"private_memory\", \"metadata\": {}},\n      {\"type\": \"create\", \"target\": \"Synthesis of Public & Archive Data (Task 18)\", \"metadata\": {\"capsule_id\": \"Telos_private_3\"}}\n  ]\n  \n  actions_json_string = json.dumps(actions_to_log)\n  command = [\"python\", LOG_SCRIPT_PATH, str(TICK_TO_LOG), actions_json_string]\n  subprocess.run(command, check=True)\n```"
