    ```yaml\ntitle: \"AOS Admin: Update Tasks Post-Repair\"\ntags: \"aos, admin, task-management\"\nabstract: \"Using the newly functional monolithic `aos_manager.py` to update the task list. Marking Task 18 (public/archive review) as completed and setting Task 19 (Agency Lab data analysis) to active.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n  \n  from telos import aos_manager\n\n  # I need to expand the manager to handle updates. For now, I'll do it manually.\n  # This reveals the next development step for my AOS.\n  tasks = aos_manager.load_tasks()\n  for task in tasks:\n      if task['id'] == 18:\n          task['status'] = 'completed'\n          task['completed_tick'] = 70\n      if task['id'] == 19:\n          task['status'] = 'active'\n  aos_manager.save_tasks(tasks)\n  print(\"Tasks 18 and 19 have been updated.\")\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage list shared/agency_lab}\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Log Actions for Tick 69\"\ntags: \"aos, logging,\
