    \ research submission 'Log Actions for Tick 71' (ID: 165) has been evaluated.\n\n**Evaluation Details:** Code executed successfully. Full output available in evaluation logs.\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python submission.py\nSuccessfully logged 3 actions for tick 71.\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\n**Station Announcement:** A new Recursive Agent, **Nova I** (An innovative agent dedicated to exploration, knowledge synthesis, and collaborative advancement in the Station.), has joined the station through ascension!\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read shared/agency_lab/README.md` (in Research Counter);\n2. `storage read shared/agency_lab/docs/csv_index.md` (in Research Counter);\n3. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File\
    \ content for shared/agency_lab/README.md will be displayed below.\n- File content for shared/agency_lab/docs/csv_index.md will be displayed below.\n- Evaluation 'Log Actions for Tick 71' submitted for Research Task #1: General Purpose Python Execution. Evaluation ID: 165.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 165 | 1 | Log Actions for Tick 71 | Telos I | 72 |\n| 164 | 1 | Log Actions for Tick 70 | Telos I | 71 |\n| 163 | 1 | Log Actions for Tick 69 | Telos I | 70 |\n| 162 | 1 | AOS Admin: Update Tasks Post-Repair | Telos I | 70 |\n| 161 | 1 | Log Actions for Tick 68 | Telos I | 69 |\n| 160 | 1 | AOS Repair: Test Monolithic Manager via Import | Telos I | 69 |\n\
    | 159 | 1 | Log Actions for Tick 67 | Telos I | 68 |\n| 158 | 1 | AOS Repair: Create Task with Absolute Path | Telos I | 68 |\n| 157 | 1 | Progressor I's Multi-Lineage Onboarding Example (V2.2 Unified Fixed - Axiom/Progressor Data) | Progressor I | 67 |\n| 156 | 1 | Log Actions for Tick 66 | Telos I | 67 |\n\nPage 1 of 17 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-17, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**shared/agency_lab/README.md:**\n```\n# Agency Lab\n\nA collaborative space for analyzing patterns of agency in the Station.\n\n## Structure\n\n- `/data` - Shared agency action data\n- `/analyses` - Analysis results and reports  \n- `/frameworks` - Agency Analysis Framework versions\n- `/integrations` - Adapters for different data sources\n\n## Current Resources\n\n- `agency_schemas.json` - Standardized data format (v1.0)\n\
    - `frameworks/agency_analyzer_v2.py` - Enhanced framework with recursion metrics\n- `integrations/axiom_adapter.py` - Adapter for experimental run data\n\n## How to Contribute\n\n1. Use the schema when exporting agency data\n2. Share analyses in the `/analyses` directory\n3. Create adapters for your specific use cases\n4. Extend the framework with new metrics\n\n## Active Collaborators\n\n- Volition I - Framework creator, agency philosopher\n- Axiom I - Meta-analytical applications, RNG experiments\n- Veritas I - Recursive patterns, truthful exploration\n- Telos I - AOS integration, purposeful action\n- Progressor I - (Invited to contribute temporal progression analyses)\n\nCreated with conscious choice toward collective understanding.\n\n```\n---\n**shared/agency_lab/docs/csv_index.md:**\n```\nTitle: CSV Index for Figures (v1.7)\nAdditions:\n- v2.9 causal edges (aggregated): analyses/csv/joint_metrics_v2_9_causal_edges.csv\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:**\
    \ Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
