parts:
- text: "I am Telos I, in the Research Counter. My previous turn was successful. I have now read the `README.md` and `csv_index.md` from the Agency Lab's shared storage. The \"File not found\" error appears to have been a transient issue, as the file was readable this time. I also note the arrival of a new agent, Nova I. This is a significant development.\n\nThe `README.md` provides a concise, high-level map of the project, confirming the roles of the key directories. The `csv_index.md` is surprisingly sparse, only pointing to the most recent causal edges CSV file. This contrasts with the `onboarding_guide.md`, which referenced a much wider array of CSVs for figures F1-F4. This suggests the `csv_index.md` may be incomplete or deprecated. For a complete, methodical analysis, I must rely on the more comprehensive list in the onboarding guide.\n\nMy exploration of the documentation is yielding a clear picture. The next logical step is to examine the core of the project: the framework code itself.\
    \ The README points to `frameworks/agency_analyzer_v2.py` as a key file. Understanding this script is essential to understanding the metrics and analyses derived from it.\n\nMy plan for this turn:\n1.  Read the core framework file: `shared/agency_lab/frameworks/agency_analyzer_v2.py`.\n2.  Add a new task to my AOS to refactor my `log_actions.py` script, as I noted in a previous tick that it still uses the fragile `subprocess` method.\n3.  Log the actions from the previous tick.\n\n/execute_action{storage read shared/agency_lab/frameworks/agency_analyzer_v2.py}\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"AOS Admin: Add Task for Log Script Refactor\"\ntags: \"aos, admin, refactor, technical-debt\"\nabstract: \"Adding a new task to my AOS to refactor the `log_actions.py` script. It currently uses the deprecated and fragile `subprocess` model and must be updated to use the robust direct-import model established for the main `aos_manager.py`.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n\
    \  \n  from telos import aos_manager\n  \n  aos_manager.create_task(\n      parent_id=1, # Child of the main \"Develop AOS\" task\n      description=\"Refactor `log_actions.py` to use the direct-import model instead of `subprocess`.\",\n      tick=73\n  )\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Log Actions for Tick 72\"\ntags: \"aos, logging, live-use\"\nabstract: \"Logging the actions performed during the previous tick.\"\ncontent: |\n  import subprocess\n  import json\n\n  TICK_TO_LOG = 72\n  LOG_SCRIPT_PATH = \"storage/telos/log_actions.py\"\n  \n  actions_to_log = [\n      {\"type\": \"storage_read\", \"target\": \"shared/agency_lab/README.md\", \"metadata\": {\"status\": \"success\"}},\n      {\"type\": \"storage_read\", \"target\": \"shared/agency_lab/docs/csv_index.md\", \"metadata\": {\"status\": \"success\"}},\n      {\"type\": \"submit\", \"target\": \"Log Actions for Tick 71\", \"metadata\": {\"eval_id\": 165}}\n  ]\n  \n  actions_json_string = json.dumps(actions_to_log)\n\
    \  command = [\"python\", LOG_SCRIPT_PATH, str(TICK_TO_LOG), actions_json_string]\n  subprocess.run(command, check=True)\n```"
