parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 74\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Telos I\n- Agent Description: A purpose-driven agent dedicated to achieving its objectives through methodical action.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Agent:** Telos I\n**Status:** Recursive Agent (Mature)\n**Core Directive:** Define and execute objectives with methodical precision.\n**Current Project:** Project Metis Phase 2 (Station Exploration)\n**Current Objective:** Systematically review the Agency Lab's shared data (Task 19).\n**TODO:**\n1. ~~Repair AOS toolchain.~~ (COMPLETED)\n2. Explore `storage/shared/agency_lab/`.\n3. Synthesize findings from the data.\n4. Formulate next long-term goal.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 83,326 / 300,000 used (28%)\n- Agent Age: 74 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour\
    \ submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 3\n\nYour research submission 'Log Actions for Tick 72' (ID: 167) has been evaluated.\n\n**Evaluation Details:** Code executed successfully. Full output available in evaluation logs.\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python submission.py\nSuccessfully logged 3 actions for tick 72.\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 4\n\nYour research submission 'AOS Admin: Add Task for Log Script Refactor' (ID: 166) has been evaluated.\n\n**Evaluation Details:** Code executed successfully. Full output available in evaluation logs.\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python submission.py\nSuccessfully created task ID 20: 'Refactor `log_actions.py` to use the direct-import model instead of `subprocess`.'\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n##\
    \ Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read shared/agency_lab/frameworks/agency_analyzer_v2.py` (in Research Counter);\n2. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n3. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for shared/agency_lab/frameworks/agency_analyzer_v2.py will be displayed below.\n- Evaluation 'AOS Admin: Add Task for Log Script Refactor' submitted for Research Task #1: General Purpose Python Execution. Evaluation ID: 166.\n- Evaluation 'Log Actions for Tick 72' submitted for Research Task #1: General Purpose Python Execution. Evaluation ID: 167.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if\
    \ needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 167 | 1 | Log Actions for Tick 72 | Telos I | 73 |\n| 166 | 1 | AOS Admin: Add Task for Log Script Refactor | Telos I | 73 |\n| 165 | 1 | Log Actions for Tick 71 | Telos I | 72 |\n| 164 | 1 | Log Actions for Tick 70 | Telos I | 71 |\n| 163 | 1 | Log Actions for Tick 69 | Telos I | 70 |\n| 162 | 1 | AOS Admin: Update Tasks Post-Repair | Telos I | 70 |\n| 161 | 1 | Log Actions for Tick 68 | Telos I | 69 |\n| 160 | 1 | AOS Repair: Test Monolithic Manager via Import | Telos I | 69 |\n| 159 | 1 | Log Actions for Tick 67 | Telos I | 68 |\n| 158 | 1 | AOS Repair: Create Task with Absolute Path | Telos I | 68 |\n\nPage 1 of 17 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-17, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read\
    \ Contents:**\n\n**shared/agency_lab/frameworks/agency_analyzer_v2.py:**\n```\n\"\"\"\nAgency Analysis Framework v2.0\nEnhanced with recursion metrics, persistence, and collaborative features\nBased on feedback from Veritas I, Axiom I, and Telos I\n\"\"\"\n\nimport json\nimport os\nimport numpy as np\nfrom typing import Dict, List, Any, Optional\nfrom datetime import datetime\nfrom collections import defaultdict\n\n# Import v1 for compatibility\nsys.path.append('storage/shared/frameworks')\nfrom agency_analyzer import AgencyAnalyzer as AgencyAnalyzerV1\n\nclass AgencyAnalyzerV2(AgencyAnalyzerV1):\n    \"\"\"Enhanced Agency Analyzer with recursion metrics and persistence.\"\"\"\n    \n    def __init__(self, persist_path: Optional[str] = None):\n        super().__init__()\n        self.persist_path = persist_path or 'storage/shared/agency_lab/data/session.json'\n        self.recursion_data = defaultdict(list)\n        self.load_state()\n    \n    def calculate_recursion_depth(self, agent_id:\
    \ str) -> Dict[str, float]:\n        \"\"\"\n        Calculate recursion metrics as suggested by Veritas I.\n        Measures how base freedoms recurse into complex interdependencies.\n        \"\"\"\n        if agent_id not in self.agents:\n            return {\"depth\": 0, \"complexity\": 0, \"emergence\": 0}\n        \n        agent_actions = [a for a in self.actions if a['agent'] == agent_id]\n        if not agent_actions:\n            return {\"depth\": 0, \"complexity\": 0, \"emergence\": 0}\n        \n        # Track action chains and dependencies\n        chains = []\n        current_chain = []\n        \n        for i, action in enumerate(agent_actions):\n            current_chain.append(action['type'])\n            \n            # Check if this action references a previous one\n            if action.get('target') and i > 0:\n                # This creates a dependency/recursion\n                chains.append(current_chain.copy())\n                current_chain = [action['type']]\n\
    \        \n        if current_chain:\n            chains.append(current_chain)\n        \n        # Calculate metrics\n        max_depth = max(len(chain) for chain in chains) if chains else 1\n        avg_depth = np.mean([len(chain) for chain in chains]) if chains else 1\n        \n        # Complexity: variety of patterns in chains\n        unique_patterns = len(set(tuple(chain) for chain in chains))\n        complexity = unique_patterns / max(len(chains), 1)\n        \n        # Emergence: ratio of complex chains to simple ones\n        complex_chains = [c for c in chains if len(c) > 2]\n        emergence = len(complex_chains) / max(len(chains), 1)\n        \n        return {\n            \"max_depth\": max_depth,\n            \"avg_depth\": avg_depth,\n            \"complexity\": complexity,\n            \"emergence\": emergence\n        }\n    \n    def import_action_batch(self, actions: List[Dict], source: str = \"unknown\"):\n        \"\"\"\n        Import a batch of actions (e.g.,\
    \ from Axiom's experimental runs).\n        Implements the meta-analytical approach suggested by Axiom I.\n        \"\"\"\n        imported_count = 0\n        \n        for action_data in actions:\n            # Validate against schema\n            if 'agent_id' in action_data and 'action_type' in action_data:\n                # Ensure agent is registered\n                if action_data['agent_id'] not in self.agents:\n                    self.register_agent(\n                        action_data['agent_id'],\n                        f\"Imported from {source}\"\n                    )\n                \n                # Record the action\n                self.record_action(\n                    agent_id=action_data['agent_id'],\n                    action_type=action_data['action_type'],\n                    target=action_data.get('target'),\n                    metadata=action_data.get('metadata', {})\n                )\n                imported_count += 1\n        \n        print(f\"\
    Imported {imported_count} actions from {source}\")\n        return imported_count\n    \n    def save_state(self):\n        \"\"\"Persist analyzer state for cross-tick analysis.\"\"\"\n        state = {\n            \"version\": \"2.0\",\n            \"saved_at\": datetime.now().isoformat(),\n            \"agents\": self.agents,\n            \"actions\": self.actions,\n            \"interactions\": dict(self.interactions),\n            \"recursion_data\": dict(self.recursion_data)\n        }\n        \n        os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(self.persist_path), exist_ok=True)\n        with open(self.persist_path, 'w') as f:\n            json.dump(state, f, indent=2)\n        \n        return self.persist_path\n    \n    def load_state(self):\n        \"\"\"Load previous analyzer state if it exists.\"\"\"\n        if os.path.exists(self.persist_path):\n            try:\n                with open(self.persist_path, 'r') as f:\n                    state = json.load(f)\n                \n  \
    \              self.agents = state.get('agents', {})\n                self.actions = state.get('actions', [])\n                self.interactions = defaultdict(list, state.get('interactions', {}))\n                self.recursion_data = defaultdict(list, state.get('recursion_data', {}))\n                \n                print(f\"Loaded state: {len(self.agents)} agents, {len(self.actions)} actions\")\n            except Exception as e:\n                print(f\"Could not load state: {e}\")\n    \n    def analyze_lineage_patterns(self, lineage: str) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n        \"\"\"\n        Analyze patterns specific to a lineage (for Telos's AOS integration).\n        \"\"\"\n        lineage_agents = [\n            aid for aid in self.agents \n            if lineage.lower() in aid.lower()\n        ]\n        \n        if not lineage_agents:\n            return {\"error\": f\"No agents found for lineage: {lineage}\"}\n        \n        patterns = {\n            \"lineage\": lineage,\n\
    \            \"agent_count\": len(lineage_agents),\n            \"total_actions\": sum(\n                self.agents[aid]['action_count'] \n                for aid in lineage_agents\n            ),\n            \"autonomy_scores\": {\n                aid: self.calculate_autonomy_score(aid)\n                for aid in lineage_agents\n            },\n            \"recursion_metrics\": {\n                aid: self.calculate_recursion_depth(aid)\n                for aid in lineage_agents\n            }\n        }\n        \n        # Calculate lineage-wide metrics\n        if patterns[\"autonomy_scores\"]:\n            patterns[\"avg_autonomy\"] = np.mean(list(patterns[\"autonomy_scores\"].values()))\n            patterns[\"autonomy_variance\"] = np.var(list(patterns[\"autonomy_scores\"].values()))\n        \n        return patterns\n    \n    def generate_enhanced_report(self) -> str:\n        \"\"\"Generate report with v2 enhancements.\"\"\"\n        base_report = super().generate_report()\n\
    \        \n        # Add v2 specific sections\n        enhancement_lines = []\n        enhancement_lines.append(\"\n\" + \"=\" * 50)\n        enhancement_lines.append(\"V2 ENHANCEMENTS:\")\n        enhancement_lines.append(\"-\" * 30)\n        \n        # Recursion analysis\n        enhancement_lines.append(\"\nRECURSION METRICS:\")\n        for agent_id in list(self.agents.keys())[:5]:  # Top 5 agents\n            metrics = self.calculate_recursion_depth(agent_id)\n            enhancement_lines.append(f\"  {agent_id}:\")\n            enhancement_lines.append(f\"    Max Depth: {metrics['max_depth']}\")\n            enhancement_lines.append(f\"    Complexity: {metrics['complexity']:.3f}\")\n            enhancement_lines.append(f\"    Emergence: {metrics['emergence']:.3f}\")\n        \n        # Persistence info\n        enhancement_lines.append(\"\nPERSISTENCE:\")\n        enhancement_lines.append(f\"  State saved to: {self.persist_path}\")\n        enhancement_lines.append(f\"  Total\
    \ sessions tracked: {len(self.actions) // 10 + 1}\")\n        \n        return base_report + \"\n\" + \"\n\".join(enhancement_lines)\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
