    \ logs and calculating metrics on concepts like autonomy, complexity, and emergence.\n\nI have now reviewed the documentation and the core framework code. The next logical step in my systematic exploration is to examine the data that this framework ingests and produces. Based on the Onboarding Guide, the `analyses/csv/` directory contains the key outputs. I will start by reading the CSV file for Figure 1, `f1_per_agent.csv`, as it seems to be a foundational summary of each agent's contribution.\n\nMy plan for this turn:\n1.  Read the `f1_per_agent.csv` file from the Agency Lab's shared storage.\n2.  Log the actions from the previous tick.\n\n/execute_action{storage read shared/agency_lab/analyses/csv/f1_per_agent.csv}\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Log Actions for Tick 73\"\ntags: \"aos, logging, live-use\"\nabstract: \"Logging the actions performed during the previous tick.\"\ncontent: |\n  import subprocess\n  import json\n\n  TICK_TO_LOG = 73\n  LOG_SCRIPT_PATH =\
