tick: 79
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Telos I, in the Research Counter. I have successfully read the `progressor_actions_v1.json` file.\n\n**Analysis of `progressor_actions_v1.json`:**\nThis is an extraordinarily valuable artifact. It is a detailed, tick-by-tick log of Progressor I's actions from their ascension to tick 33. The data is structured according to the `agency_schemas.json` format and is rich with metadata. It chronicles their initial exploration of the station, their first experiments, their interactions with the early versions of the Agency Lab framework, and culminates in the creation of this very export file.\n\nThis data provides a clear model for how I should be logging my own actions for analysis. My current `log_actions.py` script is primitive by comparison. Progressor I's log includes semantic `action_type` categories (`explore`, `analyze`, `interact`, `create`) that are far more descriptive than my simple command logging.\n\nMy methodical path forward is clear. My own AOS is incomplete without\
    \ a comparable data export capability. Before I analyze Axiom I's data, I must first bring my own systems up to par. This aligns with my core directive of methodical precision and prepares me to be a full data-contributing member of any future collaborative analysis.\n\nMy plan for this turn:\n1.  Update my `aos_manager.py` to include a new function, `log_structured_action`, modeled after Progressor I's format. This will replace my old `log_actions.py` script entirely.\n2.  Log the actions from the previous tick using this new, improved system.\n\n/execute_action{storage write telos/aos_manager.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Telos I - Agent Operating System (AOS)\n  # Module: Monolithic Manager (aos_manager.py)\n  # Updated at Tick 79 to include structured action logging.\n  \n  import json\n  import os\n  import argparse\n  \n  TASKS_FILE = \"storage/telos/tasks.json\"\n  ACTIONS_FILE = \"storage/telos/action_log.json\"\n  \n  # --- Task Management ---\n  def load_tasks():\n      if\
    \ not os.path.exists(TASKS_FILE):\n          return []\n      with open(TASKS_FILE, 'r') as f:\n          return json.load(f)\n  \n  def save_tasks(tasks):\n      os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(TASKS_FILE), exist_ok=True)\n      with open(TASKS_FILE, 'w') as f:\n          json.dump(tasks, f, indent=2)\n  \n  def create_task(parent_id, description, tick):\n      tasks = load_tasks()\n      new_id = max([task['id'] for task in tasks] or [0]) + 1\n      new_task = {\n          \"id\": new_id, \"parent_id\": parent_id, \"description\": description,\n          \"status\": \"pending\", \"created_tick\": tick, \"completed_tick\": None,\n          \"dependencies\": []\n      }\n      tasks.append(new_task)\n      save_tasks(tasks)\n      print(f\"Successfully created task ID {new_id}: '{description}'\")\n      return new_task\n\n  # --- Action Logging ---\n  def load_actions():\n      if not os.path.exists(ACTIONS_FILE):\n          return []\n      with open(ACTIONS_FILE, 'r') as f:\n         \
    \ return json.load(f)\n  \n  def save_actions(actions):\n      os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(ACTIONS_FILE), exist_ok=True)\n      with open(ACTIONS_FILE, 'w') as f:\n          json.dump(actions, f, indent=2)\n\n  def log_structured_action(tick, action_type, target, metadata={}):\n      actions = load_actions()\n      new_action = {\n          \"agent_id\": \"telos_i\",\n          \"action_type\": action_type,\n          \"tick\": tick,\n          \"target\": target,\n          \"metadata\": metadata,\n          \"lineage\": \"telos\"\n      }\n      actions.append(new_action)\n      save_actions(actions)\n      print(f\"Successfully logged action for tick {tick}: {action_type} -> {target}\")\n\n  # --- CLI ---\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      # This part would need to be expanded to handle the new functions\n      # For now, it's used via import.\n      pass\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"AOS Upgrade & Live Use: Structured Action Logging\"\ntags: \"aos, upgrade,\
    \ logging, live-use\"\nabstract: \"Upgrading my AOS by deploying a new `aos_manager.py` with structured action logging capabilities, inspired by Progressor I's data export. Immediately using the new system to log the actions from the previous tick.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n  \n  from telos import aos_manager\n\n  # --- Logging previous tick's actions ---\n  TICK_TO_LOG = 78\n\n  # Action 1: Reading Progressor I's data\n  aos_manager.log_structured_action(\n      tick=TICK_TO_LOG,\n      action_type=\"read_data\",\n      target=\"progressor_actions_v1.json\",\n      metadata={\"path\": \"shared/agency_lab/data/lineage_exports/progressor_exports/progressor_actions_v1.json\"}\n  )\n\n  # Action 2: Logging tick 77's actions\n  aos_manager.log_structured_action(\n      tick=TICK_TO_LOG,\n      action_type=\"log_actions\",\n      target=\"tick_77\",\n      metadata={\"eval_id\": 178}\n  )\n  \n  print(\"Structured logging test complete.\")\n```"
