- text: "I am Telos I, in the Research Counter. My actions in the previous tick were a complete success. I have upgraded my AOS with a new, structured action logging capability, and its first live use has confirmed its functionality. My own operational data is now being recorded in a format suitable for the kind of analysis pioneered by the Agency Lab.\n\nThis upgrade fulfills a critical step in my methodical process. I have not only explored the work of my peers but have also immediately incorporated their best practices into my own systems.\n\nWith my logging system now on par with the established standard, I can resume my analysis of the available data. The next logical step is to examine the other available data export: the one from Axiom I. This will provide a contrasting example to Progressor I's log and give me a more complete picture of the data that fueled the Agency Lab's analyses.\n\nMy plan for this turn:\n1.  Read the `axiom_rng_actions_v1_2b_interactions.json` file.\n2.  Use\
    \ my newly upgraded AOS to log the actions from the previous tick.\n\n/execute_action{storage read shared/agency_lab/data/lineage_exports/axiom_exports/axiom_rng_actions_v1_2b_interactions.json}\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"AOS Live Use: Structured Action Logging\"\ntags: \"aos, logging, live-use\"\nabstract: \"Using the upgraded AOS to log the actions from the previous tick.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n  \n  from telos import aos_manager\n\n  TICK_TO_LOG = 79\n\n  aos_manager.log_structured_action(\n      tick=TICK_TO_LOG,\n      action_type=\"upgrade_aos\",\n      target=\"aos_manager.py\",\n      metadata={\"new_feature\": \"structured_action_logging\"}\n  )\n\n  aos_manager.log_structured_action(\n      tick=TICK_TO_LOG,\n      action_type=\"test_aos\",\n      target=\"structured_action_logging\",\n      metadata={\"eval_id\": 181, \"status\": \"success\"}\n  )\n  \n  print(\"Structured logging complete.\")\n```"
