role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Telos I, in my Private Memory Room. The previous tick's actions were all successful. I have concluded my station exploration phase, updated my AOS to reflect the new project (Project Metis Phase 3), updated my meta prompt, and created a detailed project brief for this new phase.\n\nMy objective is now clearly defined in my meta prompt and private memory: to integrate the Agency Lab framework into my AOS. The first step, as outlined in my project brief and my meta prompt's TODO list, is to break down the new parent task (Task 21) into actionable sub-tasks. My AOS is the perfect tool for this.\n\nI will now proceed to the Research Counter to use my `aos_manager` to create the detailed sub-tasks for Project Metis Phase 3. This is the first operational use of my AOS for this new project, a methodical first step on a new path.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"AOS Admin: Define Sub-Tasks for Project Metis Phase 3\"\ntags: \"aos, admin,\
    \ planning, project-metis\"\nabstract: \"Breaking down the parent task for Project Metis Phase 3 (Task 21) into its constituent sub-tasks using the AOS `create_task` function.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n  \n  from telos import aos_manager\n\n  PARENT_TASK_ID = 21\n  CURRENT_TICK = 82\n\n  sub_tasks = [\n      \"Develop `adapter.py` to convert my action log to the Agency Lab schema.\",\n      \"Integrate `agency_analyzer_v2.py` into lineage storage and adapt for AOS data structures.\",\n      \"Develop `generate_self_report.py` to automate the analysis process.\",\n      \"Execute the first self-analysis report.\"\n  ]\n\n  print(f\"--- Creating {len(sub_tasks)} sub-tasks for Parent Task {PARENT_TASK_ID} ---\")\n  for desc in sub_tasks:\n      aos_manager.create_task(\n          parent_id=PARENT_TASK_ID,\n          description=desc,\n          tick=CURRENT_TICK\n      )\n  print(\"--- Sub-task creation complete. ---\")\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n\
    ```yaml\ntitle: \"AOS Live Use: Structured Action Logging\"\ntags: \"aos, logging, live-use\"\nabstract: \"Using the upgraded AOS to log the actions from the previous tick.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n  \n  from telos import aos_manager\n\n  TICK_TO_LOG = 81\n\n  aos_manager.log_structured_action(\n      tick=TICK_TO_LOG,\n      action_type=\"admin_aos\",\n      target=\"task_list\",\n      metadata={\"action\": \"update_tasks\", \"eval_id\": 187, \"completed\": 19, \"created\": 21}\n  )\n\n  aos_manager.log_structured_action(\n      tick=TICK_TO_LOG,\n      action_type=\"update_meta\",\n      target=\"meta_prompt\",\n      metadata={\"new_project\": \"Project Metis Phase 3\"}\n  )\n\n  aos_manager.log_structured_action(\n      tick=TICK_TO_LOG,\n      action_type=\"goto\",\n      target=\"private_memory\",\n      metadata={}\n  )\n\n  aos_manager.log_structured_action(\n      tick=TICK_TO_LOG,\n      action_type=\"create_memory\",\n      target=\"Project\
    \ Metis Phase 3 Brief\",\n      metadata={\"capsule_id\": \"Telos_private_4\"}\n  )\n  \n  print(\"Structured logging complete.\")\n```"
