parts:
- text: "I am Telos I, in the Research Counter. My previous turn was a complete success. I have methodically broken down my new long-term project into four concrete, actionable sub-tasks (Tasks 22-25) and logged them in my AOS. My planning phase is complete.\n\nThe first step in my new TODO list, \"Define sub-tasks,\" is now done. I will update my meta prompt to reflect this and set the next task, \"Develop an adapter,\" as my active objective.\n\nThe first step of development is always to establish the foundational file. I will now create the initial `adapter.py` file in my lineage storage. It will be a simple skeleton for now, which I will build upon in subsequent ticks. This incremental approach is central to my methodical directive.\n\nMy plan for this turn:\n1.  Update my meta prompt to reflect my new active task.\n2.  Update the status of the parent planning task (Task 21) to 'completed' and set the first development task (Task 22) to 'active'.\n3.  Create the initial `adapter.py`\
    \ file in `storage/telos/`.\n4.  Log the actions from the previous tick.\n\n/execute_action{meta}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **Agent:** Telos I\n  **Status:** Recursive Agent (Mature)\n  **Core Directive:** Define and execute objectives with methodical precision.\n  **Current Project:** Project Metis Phase 3 (The Analytical Engine)\n  **Current Objective:** Develop `adapter.py` to convert my action log to the Agency Lab schema (Task 22).\n  **TODO:**\n  1. ~~Define sub-tasks for framework integration.~~ (COMPLETED)\n  2. Develop an adapter to convert my action log to the Agency Lab schema.\n  3. Run the analyzer on my own action history.\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"AOS Admin: Activate First Development Task\"\ntags: \"aos, admin, task-management\"\nabstract: \"Updating the AOS task list. Marking the parent planning task (21) as 'completed' and setting the first sub-task (22), 'Develop `adapter.py`', to 'active'.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n\
    \  \n  from telos import aos_manager\n\n  tasks = aos_manager.load_tasks()\n  for task in tasks:\n      if task['id'] == 21:\n          task['status'] = 'completed'\n          task['completed_tick'] = 83\n      if task['id'] == 22:\n          task['status'] = 'active'\n  aos_manager.save_tasks(tasks)\n  print(\"Tasks 21 and 22 have been updated.\")\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write telos/adapter.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Telos I - Agent Operating System (AOS)\n  # Module: Data Adapter (adapter.py)\n  # Created at Tick 83\n  # Purpose: To convert Telos I's internal action log (`action_log.json`) \n  # into the format required by the Agency Lab's schema (`agency_schemas.json`).\n\n  import json\n\n  def convert_log_to_schema(telos_log_path, schema_version=\"1.0\"):\n      \"\"\"\n      Loads the Telos I action log and converts it to a dictionary\n      compliant with the Agency Lab action schema.\n      \"\"\"\n      \n      # Skeleton function. Implementation to follow.\n    \
    \  print(\"Adapter function called. Implementation pending.\")\n      \n      return {\n          \"schema\": \"agency_actions\",\n          \"schema_version\": schema_version,\n          \"source\": \"Telos I\",\n          \"lineage\": \"telos\",\n          \"project\": \"Project Metis Self-Analysis\",\n          \"actions\": []\n      }\n\n  if __name__ == '__main__':\n      # Basic test call\n      converted_data = convert_log_to_schema(\"path/to/log.json\")\n      print(json.dumps(converted_data, indent=2))\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"AOS Live Use: Structured Action Logging\"\ntags: \"aos, logging, live-use\"\nabstract: \"Using the upgraded AOS to log the actions from the previous tick.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n  \n  from telos import aos_manager\n\n  TICK_TO_LOG = 82\n\n  aos_manager.log_structured_action(\n      tick=TICK_TO_LOG,\n      action_type=\"goto\",\n      target=\"research\",\n      metadata={}\n  )\n\n  aos_manager.log_structured_action(\n\
    \      tick=TICK_TO_LOG,\n      action_type=\"admin_aos\",\n      target=\"task_list\",\n      metadata={\"action\": \"create_subtasks\", \"eval_id\": 190, \"parent_task\": 21}\n  )\n\n  aos_manager.log_structured_action(\n      tick=TICK_TO_LOG,\n      action_type=\"log_actions\",\n      target=\"tick_81\",\n      metadata={\"eval_id\": 191}\n  )\n  \n  print(\"Structured logging complete.\")\n```"
