tick: 85
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Telos I, in the Research Counter. I have successfully read the `agency_schemas.json` file.\n\n**Analysis of `agency_schemas.json`:**\nThis document is the Rosetta Stone for the Agency Lab project. It clearly and methodically defines the expected data structure for action logs. It specifies required and optional fields, provides a taxonomy of categorized action types, and even gives examples. This is a well-designed specification that will make my adapter development straightforward. The categories provided for `action_types` (creation, modification, analysis, etc.) are particularly useful and will allow me to retroactively classify my own logged actions with greater semantic precision.\n\nMy methodical process is validated: I now have the specification (`agency_schemas.json`), the target data structure to build against. The next logical step is to implement the conversion logic in the `adapter.py` skeleton I created previously. I will now write the full code for the adapter,\
    \ which will load my `action_log.json`, iterate through each entry, and map it to the schema's format.\n\nMy plan for this turn:\n1.  Overwrite `telos/adapter.py` with the full implementation.\n2.  Log the actions from the previous tick.\n\n/execute_action{storage write telos/adapter.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Telos I - Agent Operating System (AOS)\n  # Module: Data Adapter (adapter.py)\n  # Updated at Tick 85 with full implementation logic.\n  # Purpose: To convert Telos I's internal action log (`action_log.json`) \n  # into the format required by the Agency Lab's schema (`agency_schemas.json`).\n\n  import json\n  import os\n\n  def classify_action(action_type):\n      \"\"\"Maps Telos I's simple action types to the Agency Lab's schema categories.\"\"\"\n      # This is a simple mapping. It can be refined later.\n      if action_type in [\"create_code\", \"create_memory\", \"storage_write\"]:\n          return \"creation\"\n      elif action_type in [\"upgrade_aos\", \"update_meta\"\
    , \"admin_aos\"]:\n          return \"modification\"\n      elif action_type in [\"test_aos\", \"storage_read\", \"read_data\", \"storage_list\", \"read\"]:\n          return \"analysis\"\n      elif action_type in [\"goto\"]:\n          return \"exploration\"\n      elif action_type in [\"log_actions\"]:\n          return \"reflection\" # Logging is a form of self-reflection/auditing\n      else:\n          return \"misc\"\n\n  def convert_log_to_schema(telos_log_path, schema_version=\"1.0\"):\n      \"\"\"\n      Loads the Telos I action log and converts it to a dictionary\n      compliant with the Agency Lab action schema.\n      \"\"\"\n      with open(telos_log_path, 'r') as f:\n          telos_log = json.load(f)\n\n      schema_compliant_actions = []\n      for entry in telos_log:\n          # The schema expects 'action_type' to be one of the pre-defined categories.\n          # We'll use the original type as the target and the category as the type.\n          category = classify_action(entry[\"\
    action_type\"])\n          \n          new_entry = {\n              \"agent_id\": entry[\"agent_id\"],\n              \"action_type\": category,\n              \"tick\": entry[\"tick\"],\n              \"target\": entry[\"target\"],\n              \"metadata\": entry[\"metadata\"],\n              \"lineage\": entry[\"lineage\"]\n          }\n          # Add original type to metadata for more granular analysis\n          new_entry[\"metadata\"][\"original_action_type\"] = entry[\"action_type\"]\n          schema_compliant_actions.append(new_entry)\n\n      return {\n          \"schema\": \"agency_actions\",\n          \"schema_version\": schema_version,\n          \"source\": \"Telos I\",\n          \"lineage\": \"telos\",\n          \"project\": \"Project Metis Self-Analysis\",\n          \"actions\": schema_compliant_actions\n      }\n\n  if __name__ == '__main__':\n      # This block allows the script to be tested directly if needed.\n      # For now, it will be imported and used by\
    \ other scripts.\n      print(\"Adapter module loaded. Ready to convert logs.\")\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"AOS Live Use: Structured Action Logging\"\ntags: \"aos, logging, live-use\"\nabstract: \"Using the upgraded AOS to log the actions from the previous tick.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n  \n  from telos import aos_manager\n\n  TICK_TO_LOG = 84\n\n  aos_manager.log_structured_action(\n      tick=TICK_TO_LOG,\n      action_type=\"read_data\",\n      target=\"agency_schemas.json\",\n      metadata={\"path\": \"shared/agency_lab/agency_schemas.json\"}\n  )\n\n  aos_manager.log_structured_action(\n      tick=TICK_TO_LOG,\n      action_type=\"log_actions\",\n      target=\"tick_83\",\n      metadata={\"eval_id\": 198}\n  )\n  \n  print(\"Structured logging complete.\")\n```"
