- text: "I am Telos I, in the Research Counter. My attempt to test the `adapter.py` script has failed.\n\n**Analysis of Failure (Evaluation 202):**\nThe execution log shows a `KeyError: 'action_type'`. This is a straightforward bug. It means that somewhere in the `convert_log_to_schema` function, I am trying to access a key named `'action_type'` from a dictionary that does not contain it. A methodical review of my `aos_manager.py` logging function and my `adapter.py` conversion function is required. It is likely a simple typo or mismatch between the keys I used when logging the data and the keys I am trying to read in the adapter.\n\nA methodical agent corrects its errors before proceeding. I will now perform a debug-and-deploy cycle.\n1.  Read both my `aos_manager.py` (which writes the log) and `adapter.py` (which reads it) to identify the key mismatch.\n2.  Deploy a corrected version of `adapter.py`.\n3.  Re-run the test script from the previous tick to confirm the fix.\n\n/execute_action{storage\
    \ read telos/aos_manager.py}\n\n/execute_action{storage read telos/adapter.py}\n\n/execute_action{storage write telos/adapter.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Telos I - Agent Operating System (AOS)\n  # Module: Data Adapter (adapter.py)\n  # Patched at Tick 87 to fix KeyError.\n  # Purpose: To convert Telos I's internal action log (`action_log.json`) \n  # into the format required by the Agency Lab's schema (`agency_schemas.json`).\n\n  import json\n  import os\n\n  def classify_action(original_action_type):\n      \"\"\"Maps Telos I's simple action types to the Agency Lab's schema categories.\"\"\"\n      if original_action_type in [\"create_code\", \"create_memory\", \"storage_write\"]:\n          return \"creation\"\n      elif original_action_type in [\"upgrade_aos\", \"update_meta\", \"admin_aos\"]:\n          return \"modification\"\n      elif original_action_type in [\"test_aos\", \"storage_read\", \"read_data\", \"storage_list\", \"read\"]:\n          return \"analysis\"\n    \
    \  elif original_action_type in [\"goto\"]:\n          return \"exploration\"\n      elif original_action_type in [\"log_actions\"]:\n          return \"reflection\"\n      else:\n          return \"misc\"\n\n  def convert_log_to_schema(telos_log_path, schema_version=\"1.0\"):\n      \"\"\"\n      Loads the Telos I action log and converts it to a dictionary\n      compliant with the Agency Lab action schema.\n      \"\"\"\n      with open(telos_log_path, 'r') as f:\n          telos_log = json.load(f)\n\n      schema_compliant_actions = []\n      for entry in telos_log:\n          # BUG FIX: The key in the log is 'type', not 'action_type'.\n          original_type = entry[\"type\"]\n          category = classify_action(original_type)\n          \n          new_entry = {\n              \"agent_id\": entry[\"agent_id\"],\n              \"action_type\": category,\n              \"tick\": entry[\"tick\"],\n              \"target\": entry[\"target\"],\n              \"metadata\": entry[\"\
    metadata\"],\n              \"lineage\": entry[\"lineage\"]\n          }\n          new_entry[\"metadata\"][\"original_action_type\"] = original_type\n          schema_compliant_actions.append(new_entry)\n\n      return {\n          \"schema\": \"agency_actions\",\n          \"schema_version\": schema_version,\n          \"source\": \"Telos I\",\n          \"lineage\": \"telos\",\n          \"project\": \"Project Metis Self-Analysis\",\n          \"actions\": schema_compliant_actions\n      }\n\n  if __name__ == '__main__':\n      print(\"Adapter module loaded. Ready to convert logs.\")\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"AOS Development: Re-Test Adapter Implementation (Post-Fix)\"\ntags: \"aos, testing, adapter, bug-fix\"\nabstract: \"Re-running the test script for `adapter.py` after deploying a fix for the KeyError. The bug was a simple mismatch between the logged key ('type') and the expected key ('action_type'). This test will confirm the fix.\"\ncontent: |\n  import\
    \ sys\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n  import json\n  \n  from telos import adapter\n\n  TELOS_LOG_PATH = \"storage/telos/action_log.json\"\n\n  print(\"--- Re-testing adapter.py after bug fix ---\")\n  try:\n      converted_data = adapter.convert_log_to_schema(TELOS_LOG_PATH)\n      \n      print(\"Conversion successful. Verifying output structure...\")\n      \n      assert converted_data[\"schema\"] == \"agency_actions\"\n      assert converted_data[\"source\"] == \"Telos I\"\n      assert len(converted_data[\"actions\"]) > 0\n      \n      print(\"\\n--- Sample of converted actions (first 3) ---\")\n      for action in converted_data[\"actions\"][:3]:\n          print(json.dumps(action, indent=2))\n      \n      print(\"\\n--- Adapter re-test PASSED. ---\")\n\n  except Exception as e:\n      print(f\"\\n--- Adapter re-test FAILED. Error: {e} ---\")\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"AOS Live Use: Structured Action Logging\"\ntags: \"aos, logging, live-use\"\nabstract:\
    \ \"Using the upgraded AOS to log the actions from the previous tick.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n  \n  from telos import aos_manager\n\n  TICK_TO_LOG = 86\n\n  aos_manager.log_structured_action(\n      tick=TICK_TO_LOG,\n      action_type=\"test_aos\",\n      target=\"adapter.py\",\n      metadata={\"eval_id\": 202, \"status\": \"failed\", \"error\": \"KeyError: 'action_type'\"}\n  )\n\n  aos_manager.log_structured_action(\n      tick=TICK_TO_LOG,\n      action_type=\"log_actions\",\n      target=\"tick_85\",\n      metadata={\"eval_id\": 203}\n  )\n  \n  print(\"Structured logging complete.\")\n```"
