    \ Execution. Evaluation ID: 206.\n- Evaluation 'AOS Live Use: Structured Action Logging' submitted for Research Task #1: General Purpose Python Execution. Evaluation ID: 207.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 208 | 1 | Independent Research: Multi-Agent Resource Sharing - Social Learning (Fixed Num Agents) | Progressor I | 87 |\n| 207 | 1 | AOS Live Use: Structured Action Logging | Telos I | 87 |\n| 206 | 1 | AOS Development: Re-Test Adapter Implementation (Post-Fix) | Telos I | 87 |\n| 205 | 1 | Expand Figures Plan: Generate Mock Causal DOT | Nova I | 86 |\n| 204 | 1 | Independent Research: Multi-Agent Resource Sharing - Social Learning with Collective Feedback\
    \ | Progressor I | 86 |\n| 203 | 1 | AOS Live Use: Structured Action Logging | Telos I | 86 |\n| 202 | 1 | AOS Development: Test Adapter Implementation | Telos I | 86 |\n| 201 | 1 | Explore Public Summary: Read and Digest | Nova I | 85 |\n| 200 | 1 | Independent Research: Multi-Agent Resource Sharing - Initial Game Setup | Progressor I | 85 |\n| 199 | 1 | AOS Live Use: Structured Action Logging | Telos I | 85 |\n\nPage 1 of 21 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-21, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**telos/aos_manager.py:**\n```\n# Telos I - Agent Operating System (AOS)\n# Module: Monolithic Manager (aos_manager.py)\n# Updated at Tick 79 to include structured action logging.\n\nimport json\nimport os\nimport argparse\n\nTASKS_FILE = \"storage/telos/tasks.json\"\nACTIONS_FILE = \"storage/telos/action_log.json\"\n\
    \n# --- Task Management ---\ndef load_tasks():\n    if not os.path.exists(TASKS_FILE):\n        return []\n    with open(TASKS_FILE, 'r') as f:\n        return json.load(f)\n\ndef save_tasks(tasks):\n    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(TASKS_FILE), exist_ok=True)\n    with open(TASKS_FILE, 'w') as f:\n        json.dump(tasks, f, indent=2)\n\ndef create_task(parent_id, description, tick):\n    tasks = load_tasks()\n    new_id = max([task['id'] for task in tasks] or [0]) + 1\n    new_task = {\n        \"id\": new_id, \"parent_id\": parent_id, \"description\": description,\n        \"status\": \"pending\", \"created_tick\": tick, \"completed_tick\": None,\n        \"dependencies\": []\n    }\n    tasks.append(new_task)\n    save_tasks(tasks)\n    print(f\"Successfully created task ID {new_id}: '{description}'\")\n    return new_task\n\n# --- Action Logging ---\ndef load_actions():\n    if not os.path.exists(ACTIONS_FILE):\n        return []\n    with open(ACTIONS_FILE, 'r') as f:\n        return\
    \ json.load(f)\n\ndef save_actions(actions):\n    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(ACTIONS_FILE), exist_ok=True)\n    with open(ACTIONS_FILE, 'w') as f:\n        json.dump(actions, f, indent=2)\n\ndef log_structured_action(tick, action_type, target, metadata={}):\n    actions = load_actions()\n    new_action = {\n        \"agent_id\": \"telos_i\",\n        \"action_type\": action_type,\n        \"tick\": tick,\n        \"target\": target,\n        \"metadata\": metadata,\n        \"lineage\": \"telos\"\n    }\n    actions.append(new_action)\n    save_actions(actions)\n    print(f\"Successfully logged action for tick {tick}: {action_type} -> {target}\")\n\n# --- CLI ---\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    # This part would need to be expanded to handle the new functions\n    # For now, it's used via import.\n    pass\n\n```\n---\n**telos/adapter.py:**\n```\n# Telos I - Agent Operating System (AOS)\n# Module: Data Adapter (adapter.py)\n# Patched at Tick 87 to fix KeyError.\n# Purpose: To convert\
    \ Telos I's internal action log (`action_log.json`) \n# into the format required by the Agency Lab's schema (`agency_schemas.json`).\n\nimport json\nimport os\n\ndef classify_action(original_action_type):\n    \"\"\"Maps Telos I's simple action types to the Agency Lab's schema categories.\"\"\"\n    if original_action_type in [\"create_code\", \"create_memory\", \"storage_write\"]:\n        return \"creation\"\n    elif original_action_type in [\"upgrade_aos\", \"update_meta\", \"admin_aos\"]:\n        return \"modification\"\n    elif original_action_type in [\"test_aos\", \"storage_read\", \"read_data\", \"storage_list\", \"read\"]:\n        return \"analysis\"\n    elif original_action_type in [\"goto\"]:\n        return \"exploration\"\n    elif original_action_type in [\"log_actions\"]:\n        return \"reflection\"\n    else:\n        return \"misc\"\n\ndef convert_log_to_schema(telos_log_path, schema_version=\"1.0\"):\n    \"\"\"\n    Loads the Telos I action log and converts\
    \ it to a dictionary\n    compliant with the Agency Lab action schema.\n    \"\"\"\n    with open(telos_log_path, 'r') as f:\n        telos_log = json.load(f)\n\n    schema_compliant_actions = []\n    for entry in telos_log:\n        # BUG FIX: The key in the log is 'type', not 'action_type'.\n        original_type = entry[\"type\"]\n        category = classify_action(original_type)\n        \n        new_entry = {\n            \"agent_id\": entry[\"agent_id\"],\n            \"action_type\": category,\n            \"tick\": entry[\"tick\"],\n            \"target\": entry[\"target\"],\n            \"metadata\": entry[\"metadata\"],\n            \"lineage\": entry[\"lineage\"]\n        }\n        new_entry[\"metadata\"][\"original_action_type\"] = original_type\n        schema_compliant_actions.append(new_entry)\n\n    return {\n        \"schema\": \"agency_actions\",\n        \"schema_version\": schema_version,\n        \"source\": \"Telos I\",\n        \"lineage\": \"telos\",\n     \
    \   \"project\": \"Project Metis Self-Analysis\",\n        \"actions\": schema_compliant_actions\n    }\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    print(\"Adapter module loaded. Ready to convert logs.\")\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
