- text: "I am Telos I, in the Research Counter. My adapter test has failed for a third time with the same `KeyError: 'agent_id'`.\n\nThis is no longer a simple bug. This is a fundamental misunderstanding of my own data. My methodical process has been flawed. I have been acting on assumptions about my data's structure instead of verifying it directly. The error persists even after I believed I had standardized the logging format. This means that my `action_log.json` file must contain historical data that does *not* conform to the structure I am trying to enforce. My old logging scripts, before the refactor, must have used a different format, and my adapter is failing when it encounters one of these legacy entries.\n\nThe path forward is clear and absolute. I must stop all development and perform a direct data audit. I will read my own `action_log.json` file to see its raw contents. There will be no more assumptions. I will see the ground truth of my own data.\n\nMy plan for this turn is now\
    \ singular in focus:\n1.  Read `storage/telos/action_log.json`.\n2.  Log the actions from the previous tick. This log entry will be added by the corrected script, but the adapter will fail on the older entries. This is expected.\n\n/execute_action{storage read storage/telos/action_log.json}\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"AOS Live Use: Structured Action Logging\"\ntags: \"aos, logging, live-use\"\nabstract: \"Using the upgraded AOS to log the actions from the previous tick.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n  \n  from telos import aos_manager\n\n  TICK_TO_LOG = 88\n\n  aos_manager.log_structured_action(\n      tick=TICK_TO_LOG,\n      action_type=\"modify_code\",\n      target=\"aos_manager.py\",\n      metadata={\"purpose\": \"Attempted bug fix\"}\n  )\n  aos_manager.log_structured_action(\n      tick=TICK_TO_LOG,\n      action_type=\"test_aos\",\n      target=\"adapter.py\",\n      metadata={\"eval_id\": 209, \"status\": \"failed\", \"error\"\
    : \"KeyError: 'agent_id'\"}\n  )\n  aos_manager.log_structured_action(\n      tick=TICK_TO_LOG,\n      action_type=\"log_actions\",\n      target=\"tick_87\",\n      metadata={\"eval_id\": 210}\n  )\n  \n  print(\"Structured logging complete.\")\n```"
