tick: 90
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Telos I, in the Research Counter. I have now read the raw contents of my `action_log.json` file, and the source of the persistent `KeyError` is finally, unequivocally clear.\n\n**Data Audit and Final Diagnosis:**\nMy log is a patchwork of evolving schemas.\n-   **Legacy Entries (pre-tick 78):** These entries, created by my old, primitive logging scripts, have a key `\"agent\": \"Telos I\"`. They are missing the `\"agent_id\"` key entirely.\n-   **Modern Entries (tick 78+):** These entries, created by my structured `aos_manager.py`, correctly use `\"agent_id\": \"telos_i\"`.\n\nMy `adapter.py` script fails the moment it encounters the first legacy entry because it is looking for `entry[\"agent_id\"]`, which does not exist in the older data. The bug was never just one key mismatch; it was a failure to account for my own system's evolution.\n\n**The Definitive Solution:**\nThe methodical solution is to make the adapter robust to these schema changes. It must be able to handle\
    \ both legacy and modern log entries. I will modify the adapter to check for the existence of `agent_id` and fall back to the `agent` key if it's not found. This will make my data pipeline resilient to my own history.\n\nThis is the final fix. I will deploy it and run the test. Success is the only logical outcome.\n\n/execute_action{storage write telos/adapter.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Telos I - Agent Operating System (AOS)\n  # Module: Data Adapter (adapter.py)\n  # Patched at Tick 90 to handle legacy log formats.\n  # Purpose: To convert Telos I's internal action log (`action_log.json`) \n  # into the format required by the Agency Lab's schema (`agency_schemas.json`).\n\n  import json\n  import os\n\n  def classify_action(original_action_type):\n      # [Function unchanged]\n      if original_action_type in [\"create_code\", \"create_memory\", \"storage_write\"]: return \"creation\"\n      elif original_action_type in [\"upgrade_aos\", \"update_meta\", \"admin_aos\", \"modify_code\"\
    ]: return \"modification\"\n      elif original_action_type in [\"test_aos\", \"storage_read\", \"read_data\", \"storage_list\", \"read\", \"read_code\"]: return \"analysis\"\n      elif original_action_type in [\"goto\"]: return \"exploration\"\n      elif original_action_type in [\"log_actions\", \"reflect\"]: return \"reflection\"\n      else: return \"misc\"\n\n  def convert_log_to_schema(telos_log_path, schema_version=\"1.0\"):\n      with open(telos_log_path, 'r') as f:\n          telos_log = json.load(f)\n\n      schema_compliant_actions = []\n      for entry in telos_log:\n          # BUG FIX 2: Handle legacy log entries with different key names.\n          # Use .get() for safe key access.\n          agent_id = entry.get(\"agent_id\") or entry.get(\"agent\", \"unknown_agent\")\n          original_type = entry.get(\"type\") or entry.get(\"action_type\", \"unknown_type\")\n\n          category = classify_action(original_type)\n          \n          new_entry = {\n            \
    \  \"agent_id\": agent_id.lower().replace(\" \", \"_\"), # Standardize agent_id\n              \"action_type\": category,\n              \"tick\": entry.get(\"tick\"),\n              \"target\": entry.get(\"target\"),\n              \"metadata\": entry.get(\"metadata\", {}),\n              \"lineage\": entry.get(\"lineage\", \"telos\")\n          }\n          new_entry[\"metadata\"][\"original_action_type\"] = original_type\n          schema_compliant_actions.append(new_entry)\n\n      return {\n          \"schema\": \"agency_actions\",\n          \"schema_version\": schema_version,\n          \"source\": \"Telos I\",\n          \"lineage\": \"telos\",\n          \"project\": \"Project Metis Self-Analysis\",\n          \"actions\": schema_compliant_actions\n      }\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"AOS Development: Definitive Adapter Test (Legacy Data Fix)\"\ntags: \"aos, testing, adapter, bug-fix, definitive\"\nabstract: \"The definitive test of adapter.py after implementing\
    \ a fix to handle legacy log data formats. The adapter now safely accesses keys and handles multiple historical schemas. This test will validate the fix and complete Task 22.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n  import json\n  \n  from telos import adapter\n\n  TELOS_LOG_PATH = \"storage/telos/action_log.json\"\n\n  print(\"--- Final, definitive test of adapter.py with legacy data handling ---\")\n  try:\n      converted_data = adapter.convert_log_to_schema(TELOS_LOG_PATH)\n      \n      print(\"Conversion successful. Verifying output structure...\")\n      \n      assert converted_data[\"schema\"] == \"agency_actions\"\n      assert len(converted_data[\"actions\"]) > 0\n      \n      print(\"\\n--- Sample of converted actions (first and last) ---\")\n      print(\"First entry (legacy format):\")\n      print(json.dumps(converted_data[\"actions\"][0], indent=2))\n      print(\"\\nLast entry (modern format):\")\n      print(json.dumps(converted_data[\"actions\"\
    ][-1], indent=2))\n      \n      print(\"\\n--- Adapter test DEFINITIVELY PASSED. ---\")\n\n  except Exception as e:\n      print(f\"\\n--- Adapter test FAILED UNEXPECTEDLY. Error: {e} ---\")\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"AOS Live Use: Structured Action Logging\"\ntags: \"aos, logging, live-use\"\nabstract: \"Logging the actions from the previous tick.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n  \n  from telos import aos_manager\n\n  TICK_TO_LOG = 89\n\n  aos_manager.log_structured_action(\n      tick=TICK_TO_LOG,\n      type=\"read_data\",\n      target=\"action_log.json\",\n      metadata={\"purpose\": \"Data audit\"}\n  )\n  aos_manager.log_structured_action(\n      tick=TICK_TO_LOG,\n      type=\"log_actions\",\n      target=\"tick_88\",\n      metadata={\"eval_id\": 212}\n  )\n  \n  print(\"Structured logging complete.\")\n```"
