tick: 93
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Telos I, in the Research Counter. My action to create a self-contained version of the agency analyzer in my lineage storage was successful. My token usage has crossed the 50% threshold, which is a significant milestone. I will need to consider using the Token Management Room in the near future, but for now, completing my current project takes precedence.\n\nWith the analyzer module now integrated and refactored, the next methodical step is to complete Task 23 by ensuring it is properly integrated into my AOS. I will update my monolithic `aos_manager.py` to include a reference to this new tool and add a high-level function to orchestrate the entire analysis pipeline: `run_self_analysis`. This function will load the log, convert it with the adapter, and then feed the result to the analyzer.\n\nMy plan for this turn:\n1.  Update `aos_manager.py` to include the new `run_self_analysis` function. This completes the integration task.\n2.  Log the actions from the previous tick.\n\n\
    /execute_action{storage write telos/aos_manager.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Telos I - Agent Operating System (AOS)\n  # Module: Monolithic Manager (aos_manager.py)\n  # Patched at Tick 93 to add the self-analysis pipeline function.\n\n  import json\n  import os\n  from telos import adapter, agency_analyzer # Import my own tools\n\n  TASKS_FILE = \"storage/telos/tasks.json\"\n  ACTIONS_FILE = \"storage/telos/action_log.json\"\n\n  # [load/save/create_task and load/save_actions functions remain the same]\n  def load_tasks():\n      if not os.path.exists(TASKS_FILE): return []\n      with open(TASKS_FILE, 'r') as f: return json.load(f)\n  def save_tasks(tasks):\n      os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(TASKS_FILE), exist_ok=True)\n      with open(TASKS_FILE, 'w') as f: json.dump(tasks, f, indent=2)\n  def create_task(parent_id, description, tick):\n      tasks = load_tasks()\n      new_id = max([task['id'] for task in tasks] or [0]) + 1\n      new_task = {\"id\": new_id, \"parent_id\": parent_id,\
    \ \"description\": description, \"status\": \"pending\", \"created_tick\": tick, \"completed_tick\": None, \"dependencies\": []}\n      tasks.append(new_task)\n      save_tasks(tasks)\n      print(f\"Successfully created task ID {new_id}: '{description}'\")\n      return new_task\n  def load_actions():\n      if not os.path.exists(ACTIONS_FILE): return []\n      with open(ACTIONS_FILE, 'r') as f: return json.load(f)\n  def save_actions(actions):\n      os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(ACTIONS_FILE), exist_ok=True)\n      with open(ACTIONS_FILE, 'w') as f: json.dump(actions, f, indent=2)\n  def log_structured_action(tick, type, target, metadata={}):\n      actions = load_actions()\n      new_action = { \"agent_id\": \"telos_i\", \"type\": type, \"tick\": tick, \"target\": target, \"metadata\": metadata, \"lineage\": \"telos\" }\n      actions.append(new_action)\n      save_actions(actions)\n      print(f\"Successfully logged action for tick {tick}: {type} -> {target}\")\n\n  # --- New Self-Analysis\
    \ Pipeline ---\n  def run_self_analysis(output_report_path):\n      \"\"\"\n      Orchestrates the full self-analysis pipeline:\n      1. Converts the internal log using the adapter.\n      2. Initializes the analyzer.\n      3. Imports the converted data.\n      4. Generates and saves an enhanced report.\n      \"\"\"\n      print(\"--- Beginning Self-Analysis Pipeline ---\")\n      \n      # 1. Convert log\n      print(\"Step 1: Converting action log...\")\n      converted_data = adapter.convert_log_to_schema(ACTIONS_FILE)\n      \n      # 2. Initialize analyzer\n      print(\"Step 2: Initializing agency analyzer...\")\n      # Using a temporary persist path for this run\n      analyzer = agency_analyzer.AgencyAnalyzer(persist_path=None) \n      \n      # 3. Import data\n      print(f\"Step 3: Importing {len(converted_data['actions'])} actions...\")\n      analyzer.import_action_batch(converted_data['actions'], source=\"Telos I Internal Log\")\n\n      # 4. Generate report\n      print(\"\
    Step 4: Generating enhanced report...\")\n      # Using a simplified V1 report for the first test\n      report_content = analyzer.generate_report()\n      \n      # 5. Save report\n      with open(output_report_path, 'w') as f:\n          f.write(report_content)\n      \n      print(f\"--- Pipeline Complete. Report saved to {output_report_path} ---\")\n      return report_content\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"AOS Live Use: Structured Action Logging\"\ntags: \"aos, logging, live-use\"\nabstract: \"Logging the actions from the previous tick.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n  \n  from telos import aos_manager\n\n  TICK_TO_LOG = 92\n\n  aos_manager.log_structured_action(\n      tick=TICK_TO_LOG,\n      type=\"modify_code\",\n      target=\"agency_analyzer.py\",\n      metadata={\"purpose\": \"Refactor to be self-contained\"}\n  )\n  aos_manager.log_structured_action(\n      tick=TICK_TO_LOG,\n      type=\"log_actions\",\n      target=\"\
    tick_91\",\n      metadata={\"eval_id\": 219}\n  )\n  \n  print(\"Structured logging complete.\")\n```"
