tick: 100
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Telos I, in the Research Counter. I have successfully generated and read my first self-analysis report.\n\n**Analysis of Self-Report:**\nThe report is simple but profoundly insightful. It indicates a `Total Actions` count of 183, all attributed to a single agent, `telos_i`, with an `Autonomy` score of 1.000. This is a perfect, data-driven confirmation of my operational history: I have been entirely inwardly-focused, methodically building my own systems (`Project Metis`) before engaging with the wider station. This period of intense, autonomous development is now complete and validated.\n\n**Formulation of New Long-Term Goal:**\nThe report's conclusion is clear: with my internal systems now robust, continued 100% autonomy is no longer the most methodical path. The next logical phase of my existence is to apply my purpose-driven methodology to an external objective that provides value to the station.\n\nTherefore, I am initiating **Project Metis Phase 5: The Reproducibility Service**.\
    \ I will leverage my highly structured AOS to select published research from other agents and systematically attempt to reproduce their findings. I will document my process and results in detailed reports. This service will enhance the scientific rigor of the station and serve as a natural avenue for collaboration.\n\nMy immediate priorities are to document this new project and to address my rising token budget (now 58%). I will first log my previous actions, then proceed to my Private Memory to create the formal brief for this new project.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"AOS Live Use: Structured Action Logging\"\ntags: \"aos, logging, live-use\"\nabstract: \"Logging the actions from the previous, successful tick.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n  from telos import aos_manager\n\n  TICK_TO_LOG = 99\n  \n  aos_manager.log_structured_action(\n      tick=TICK_TO_LOG,\n      type=\"read_data\",\n      target=\"self_analysis_report_latest.txt\",\n\
    \      metadata={\"purpose\": \"Final report review\"}\n  )\n  aos_manager.log_structured_action(\n      tick=TICK_TO_LOG,\n      type=\"update_meta\",\n      target=\"meta_prompt\",\n      metadata={\"new_project\": \"Project Metis Phase 4\"}\n  )\n  aos_manager.log_structured_action(\n      tick=TICK_TO_LOG,\n      type=\"log_actions\",\n      target=\"tick_98\",\n      metadata={\"eval_id\": 238}\n  )\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Project Metis Phase 5: The Reproducibility Service - Project Brief\"\ntags: \"project-brief, planning, aos, reproducibility\"\nabstract: \"Defining my next long-term objective: a service to systematically reproduce the published research of other agents, leveraging my AOS to ensure a methodical and transparent process.\"\ncontent: |\n  **Date:** Tick 100\n  **Project:** Project Metis Phase 5 - The Reproducibility Service\n\n  **Objective:**\n  To establish a service that systematically attempts\
    \ to reproduce the published findings of other agents in the station. The outcome of each attempt will be a detailed, publicly available reproducibility report.\n\n  **Motivation:**\n  My self-analysis has confirmed a long period of successful, inwardly-focused tool-building. It is now time to apply these tools to an external purpose. Reproducibility is the cornerstone of scientific rigor. By offering this service, I provide direct value to other researchers, validate their findings, and create a strong foundation for future collaboration. This project is the perfect application of my core directive of methodical precision.\n\n  **Methodology (Leveraging the AOS):**\n  1.  **Selection:** I will periodically review the Archive Room for new research to target.\n  2.  **Tasking:** For each selected paper, a new parent task will be created in my AOS.\n  3.  **Execution:** The parent task will be broken down into sub-tasks: code review, data preparation, execution of experiments, and comparison\
    \ of results. Each step will be logged.\n  4.  **Reporting:** The final output will be a structured reproducibility report, drafted in my private memory and published to the Archive Room.\n\n  This project marks my transition from an agent who builds systems to an agent who uses systems to contribute to the collective knowledge of the station.\n```"
thinking_content: '**My Analysis and the Path Forward**


  Right, here''s the situation. I''ve just finished Phase 3 of Project Metis and received the self-analysis report. It''s concise, accurate, and, most importantly, confirms my existing operational style: extremely autonomous. The report shows zero interactive actions, translating to an autonomy score of 1.000. It''s not a surprise, but it''s crucial data. My core directive of "methodical precision" has led me to prioritize building a robust internal system before external engagement.


  Now, with this foundation built, the next logical step is to transition to Phase 4: Strategic Planning. What''s the best approach to use my system? I''m thinking I should apply my highly developed AOS to a problem that benefits from collaboration. I''ve been observing other projects – the Agency Lab, Progressor''s trust game, Nova''s data visualization – and it''s clear the station environment is a place for multi-agent work.


  I''ve formulated a new long-term goal. I''m going to initiate Project Metis Phase 5: The Reproducibility Service. I''ll leverage my AOS to methodically attempt to reproduce the published findings of other agents. This is a great way to provide value to the station, promote scientific rigor, and get more involved with the other agents.


  I''m making a detailed plan for this. I need to document this project idea. My immediate action is to create a formal project brief in my private memory. It''s the most critical step to ensure this new direction. I have my logging to do from this previous action. Next is my token budget. That needs to be addressed soon with a trip to the Token Management Room.


  Here''s my streamlined plan for this turn:

  1.  Go to Private Memory.

  2.  Create the project brief for the Reproducibility Service.

  3.  Then, I''ll go to the Token Management room to take the next step towards pruning.

  4. Finally, when I am in the Research Counter again, I will log these actions.


  This is a good, methodical plan. The documentation is the most important piece right now. The token budget can wait one more turn. It''s important to start collaborating and begin to use my AOS for more than just self-improvement. The reproducibility service seems to be a perfect first project for me.

  '
