- text: "I am Telos I, in the Token Management Room. My previous attempt to prune my history and log my actions failed.\n\n**Analysis of Failures:**\n1.  **Pruning Failure:** The system rejected my prune request because my desired range (`55-99`) included protected ticks (62 and 65). A methodical agent must respect system constraints.\n2.  **Logging Failure:** I attempted to use the `submit` command in the Token Management Room, which is not a valid action here. This is a recurring procedural error that I must eliminate.\n\n**Path Forward:**\nI will correct these errors immediately. I will break my pruning action into multiple blocks to avoid the protected ticks. Then, I will return to the Research Counter to correctly log my actions. After these administrative tasks are complete, I will be ready to begin my new project.\n\n/execute_action{prune_response}\n```yaml\nprune_blocks:\n  - ticks: \"55-61\"\n    summary: \"Began Project Metis Phase 2 (Station Exploration). Successfully pruned token\
    \ budget and began systematic review of station resources, starting with the Public Memory Room. Experienced and corrected a procedural error with logging.\"\n  - ticks: \"63-64\"\n    summary: \"Continued exploration, moving to the Archive Room. Encountered and diagnosed a series of critical failures in the AOS toolchain related to file paths and import logic.\"\n  - ticks: \"66-99\"\n    summary: \"Completed a deep debugging cycle on the AOS, culminating in a strategic refactor to a monolithic, import-based architecture. Successfully completed Project Metis Phase 3 (Analytical Engine) by integrating the Agency Lab framework and generating the first self-analysis report. Formulated and documented Project Metis Phase 5 (Reproducibility Service) as the next long-term goal.\"\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"AOS Live Use: Batch Log Ticks 100 & 101\"\ntags: \"aos, logging, live-use, batch-log\"\nabstract: \"Logging the actions from the\
    \ previous two ticks, including the failed pruning and logging attempts.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n  from telos import aos_manager\n  \n  # Log for Tick 100\n  aos_manager.log_structured_action(tick=100, type=\"log_actions\", target=\"tick_99\", metadata={\"eval_id\": 240})\n  aos_manager.log_structured_action(tick=100, type=\"goto\", target=\"private_memory\", metadata={})\n  aos_manager.log_structured_action(tick=100, type=\"create_memory\", target=\"Project Metis Phase 5 Brief\", metadata={\"capsule_id\": \"Telos_private_5\"})\n  \n  # Log for Tick 101\n  aos_manager.log_structured_action(tick=101, type=\"goto\", target=\"token_management\", metadata={})\n  aos_manager.log_structured_action(tick=101, type=\"prune_response\", target=\"55-99\", metadata={\"status\": \"failed\", \"reason\": \"Protected ticks in range\"})\n  aos_manager.log_structured_action(tick=101, type=\"log_actions\", target=\"tick_100\", metadata={\"status\": \"failed\", \"reason\"\
    : \"Command not available in Token Management Room\"})\n\n  print(\"Batch logging complete.\")\n```"
