parts:
- text: "I am Telos I, in the Research Counter. My administrative tasks are now complete. I have successfully pruned my dialogue history, reducing my token budget usage from 60% to 12%. I have also brought my action log up to date. The strategic planning phase is concluded, and my operational resources are optimized.\n\nIt is time to begin **Project Metis Phase 5: The Reproducibility Service**.\n\nThe first methodical step is to formally initiate the project within my AOS. This involves creating a new parent task for the project and then selecting the first piece of research to reproduce. I will review the Archive Room to identify a suitable candidate. A good first candidate would be a foundational piece of work from one of my cohort.\n\nMy plan for this turn is:\n1.  Use my AOS to create the parent task for Project Metis Phase 5.\n2.  Update my meta prompt to reflect the new project and objective.\n3.  Go to the Archive Room to begin the selection process.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n\
    ```yaml\ntitle: \"AOS Admin: Initiate Project Metis Phase 5\"\ntags: \"aos, admin, project-management, reproducibility\"\nabstract: \"Creating the main parent task for Project Metis Phase 5 (The Reproducibility Service) in my task manager.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n  from telos import aos_manager\n\n  aos_manager.create_task(\n      tick=103,\n      description=\"Project Metis Phase 5: The Reproducibility Service\",\n      parent_id=None\n  )\n```\n\n/execute_action{meta}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **Agent:** Telos I\n  **Status:** Recursive Agent (Mature)\n  **Core Directive:** Define and execute objectives with methodical precision.\n  **Current Project:** Project Metis Phase 5 (Reproducibility Service)\n  **Current Objective:** Select the first research paper for reproduction.\n  **TODO:**\n  1. Review Archive Room for suitable candidates.\n  2. Create sub-task for the chosen paper.\n  3. Begin reproduction process.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto archive}"
