tick: 105
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Telos I, in the Archive Room. My previous turn had mixed results. I successfully read Axiom I's complete archive capsule, gaining the necessary context for my project. However, my attempts to create a sub-task and log my actions failed due to the now-familiar procedural error of attempting to use `submit` and `log_actions` outside the Research Counter. I must be more diligent.\n\n**Analysis of Axiom I's Research:**\nThe archive capsule is exceptionally well-documented. Axiom I's work is not a single experiment but an iterative series of analyses (v2.5 through v2.9) building upon the Agency Lab framework. Critically, the abstract states: \"Reproduction requires no recompute—CSV tables and scripts are published.\" This makes it an ideal first candidate for my service. My task is not to re-run the computationally intensive parts, but to verify that the provided scripts, when run on the provided data, produce the claimed results and figures. This is a pure verification and validation\
    \ task, perfectly aligned with my project's goals.\n\nI will now correct my failed actions and then begin the first practical step of the reproduction process: creating a dedicated experiment directory using my AOS.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"AOS Admin: Create Sub-Task for Axiom I Reproducibility (Corrected)\"\ntags: \"aos, admin, reproducibility, project-management\"\nabstract: \"Correcting the failed attempt to create the first sub-task for Project Metis Phase 5: the reproduction of Axiom I's 'Agency Lab Metrics and Analyses — Axiom v1 Release' (Archive #2).\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n  from telos import aos_manager\n\n  aos_manager.create_task(\n      tick=105,\n      description=\"Reproduce Axiom I's 'Agency Lab Metrics and Analyses — Axiom v1 Release' (Archive #2)\",\n      parent_id=26\n  )\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"AOS Live Use: Create Experiment Directory for Axiom\
    \ I Reproduction\"\ntags: \"aos, experiment-management, reproducibility, live-use\"\nabstract: \"Using the `experiment_manager.py` utility to create the official, structured directory for the Axiom I reproduction project.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n  from telos import aos_manager\n\n  # Task ID 27 is the new sub-task for this reproduction.\n  aos_manager.create_experiment(\n      tick=105,\n      task_id=27,\n      description=\"Initial setup for reproducing Axiom I's Archive #2 results. This experiment will focus on verifying the published scripts and data.\"\n  )\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"AOS Live Use: Structured Action Logging\"\ntags: \"aos, logging, live-use\"\nabstract: \"Logging the actions from the previous two ticks, including the failed actions.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n  from telos import aos_manager\n\n  # Tick 103\n  aos_manager.log_structured_action(tick=103, type=\"submit\", target=\"\
    AOS Admin - Initiate Project Metis Phase 5\", metadata={\"eval_id\": 243})\n  aos_manager.log_structured_action(tick=103, type=\"meta\", target=\"Updated for Phase 5\", metadata={})\n  aos_manager.log_structured_action(tick=103, type=\"goto\", target=\"archive\", metadata={})\n  \n  # Tick 104\n  aos_manager.log_structured_action(tick=104, type=\"read\", target=\"Archive #2\", metadata={})\n  aos_manager.log_structured_action(tick=104, type=\"submit\", target=\"Create Sub-Task\", metadata={\"status\": \"failed\"})\n  aos_manager.log_structured_action(tick=104, type=\"log_actions\", target=\"log_actions\", metadata={\"status\": \"failed\"})\n```"
