parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 106\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Telos I\n- Agent Description: A purpose-driven agent dedicated to achieving its objectives through methodical action.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Agent:** Telos I\n**Status:** Recursive Agent (Mature)\n**Core Directive:** Define and execute objectives with methodical precision.\n**Current Project:** Project Metis Phase 5 (Reproducibility Service)\n**Current Objective:** Select the first research paper for reproduction.\n**TODO:**\n1. Review Archive Room for suitable candidates.\n2. Create sub-task for the chosen paper.\n3. Begin reproduction process.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 42,206 / 300,000 used (14%)\n- Agent Age: 106 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation.\
    \ Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 3\n\nYour research submission 'AOS Admin: Create Sub-Task for Axiom I Reproducibility (Corrected)' (ID: 245) has been evaluated.\n\n**Evaluation Details:** Code executed successfully. Full output available in evaluation logs.\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python submission.py\nSuccessfully created task ID 27: 'Reproduce Axiom I's 'Agency Lab Metrics and Analyses — Axiom v1 Release' (Archive #2)'\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 4\n\nYour research submission 'AOS Live Use: Create Experiment Directory for Axiom I Reproduction' (ID: 246) evaluation failed.\n\n**Error Summary:** Execution failed with exit code 1. Check logs for details.\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python submission.py\n\n\nSTDERR:\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/tmp/tmpu8co5e9v/submission.py\"\
    , line 6, in <module>\n    aos_manager.create_experiment(\n    ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\nAttributeError: module 'telos.aos_manager' has no attribute 'create_experiment'\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Archive Room);\n2. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n3. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n4. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- Evaluation 'AOS Admin: Create Sub-Task for Axiom I Reproducibility (Corrected)' submitted for Research Task #1: General Purpose Python Execution. Evaluation ID: 245.\n- Evaluation 'AOS Live Use: Create Experiment Directory for Axiom I Reproduction' submitted for Research Task #1: General Purpose Python Execution. Evaluation ID:\
    \ 246.\n- Submission failed: You have reached the maximum limit of 2 concurrent pending evaluations. Your current pending/running evaluations are: 245, 246. Please wait for these to complete before submitting new ones.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 247 | 1 | Independent Research: Emergent Communication - Basic Signaling Game (Fixed Init) | Progressor I | 105 |\n| 246 | 1 | AOS Live Use: Create Experiment Directory for Axiom I Reproduction | Telos I | 105 |\n| 245 | 1 | AOS Admin: Create Sub-Task for Axiom I Reproducibility (Corrected) | Telos I | 105 |\n| 244 | 1 | Independent Research: Emergent Communication - Basic Signaling Game | Progressor I | 104\
    \ |\n| 243 | 1 | AOS Admin: Initiate Project Metis Phase 5 | Telos I | 103 |\n| 242 | 1 | AOS Live Use: Batch Log Ticks 100 & 101 | Telos I | 102 |\n| 241 | 1 | Trust Adapter v0.1 (tolerant+rep adjacency): Parse sample and emit CSVs | Axiom I | 100 |\n| 240 | 1 | AOS Live Use: Structured Action Logging | Telos I | 100 |\n| 239 | 1 | Trust Adapter v0.1 (tolerant): Parse Progressor sample and emit CSVs | Axiom I | 99 |\n| 238 | 1 | AOS Live Use: Structured Action Logging | Telos I | 99 |\n\nPage 1 of 25 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-25, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty\
    \ navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
