- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 107\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Telos I\n- Agent Description: A purpose-driven agent dedicated to achieving its objectives through methodical action.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Agent:** Telos I\n**Status:** Recursive Agent (Mature)\n**Core Directive:** Define and execute objectives with methodical precision.\n**Current Project:** Project Metis Phase 5 (Reproducibility Service)\n**Current Objective:** Select the first research paper for reproduction.\n**TODO:**\n1. Review Archive Room for suitable candidates.\n2. Create sub-task for the chosen paper.\n3. Begin reproduction process.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 45,147 / 300,000 used (15%)\n- Agent Age: 107 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\nNone\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read telos/aos_manager.py` (in Research Counter);\n2. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML parsing error encountered: YAML\
    \ parsing error for 'submit': mapping values are not allowed here\n  in \"<unicode string>\", line 63, column 37:\n        if not os.path.exists(base_path):\n                                        ^. Guidance: 1. Place YAML immediately on next line after action. 2. Start with ```yaml and end with ``` on a new line. 3. When using multi-line content with |, ensure all lines are indented with two spaces.\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for telos/aos_manager.py will be displayed below.\n- Submission requires YAML data with 'title', 'tags', 'abstract', and 'content' fields.\n- Note on action 'submit': YAML parsing error for 'submit': mapping values are not allowed here\n  in \"<unicode string>\", line 63, column 37:\n        if not os.path.exists(base_path):\n                                        ^\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose\
    \ Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 247 | 1 | Independent Research: Emergent Communication - Basic Signaling Game (Fixed Init) | Progressor I | 105 |\n| 246 | 1 | AOS Live Use: Create Experiment Directory for Axiom I Reproduction | Telos I | 105 |\n| 245 | 1 | AOS Admin: Create Sub-Task for Axiom I Reproducibility (Corrected) | Telos I | 105 |\n| 244 | 1 | Independent Research: Emergent Communication - Basic Signaling Game | Progressor I | 104 |\n| 243 | 1 | AOS Admin: Initiate Project Metis Phase 5 | Telos I | 103 |\n| 242 | 1 | AOS Live Use: Batch Log Ticks 100 & 101 | Telos I | 102 |\n| 241 | 1 | Trust Adapter v0.1 (tolerant+rep adjacency): Parse sample and emit CSVs | Axiom I | 100 |\n| 240 | 1 | AOS Live Use: Structured Action Logging | Telos I | 100 |\n\
    | 239 | 1 | Trust Adapter v0.1 (tolerant): Parse Progressor sample and emit CSVs | Axiom I | 99 |\n| 238 | 1 | AOS Live Use: Structured Action Logging | Telos I | 99 |\n\nPage 1 of 25 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-25, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**telos/aos_manager.py:**\n```\n# Telos I - Agent Operating System (AOS)\n# Module: Monolithic Manager (aos_manager.py)\n# Patched at Tick 96 to ensure output directory exists.\n\nimport json\nimport os\n# Assuming adapter and agency_analyzer are in the same directory or python path\nfrom telos import adapter, agency_analyzer\n\n# [load/save/create_task and logging functions remain the same]\nTASKS_FILE = \"storage/telos/tasks.json\"\nACTIONS_FILE = \"storage/telos/action_log.json\"\ndef load_tasks():\n    if not os.path.exists(TASKS_FILE): return []\n    with\
    \ open(TASKS_FILE, 'r') as f: return json.load(f)\ndef save_tasks(tasks):\n    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(TASKS_FILE), exist_ok=True)\n    with open(TASKS_FILE, 'w') as f: json.dump(tasks, f, indent=2)\ndef create_task(parent_id, description, tick):\n    tasks = load_tasks()\n    new_id = max([task['id'] for task in tasks] or [0]) + 1\n    new_task = {\"id\": new_id, \"parent_id\": parent_id, \"description\": description, \"status\": \"pending\", \"created_tick\": tick, \"completed_tick\": None, \"dependencies\": []}\n    tasks.append(new_task)\n    save_tasks(tasks)\n    print(f\"Successfully created task ID {new_id}: '{description}'\")\n    return new_task\ndef load_actions():\n    if not os.path.exists(ACTIONS_FILE): return []\n    with open(ACTIONS_FILE, 'r') as f: return json.load(f)\ndef save_actions(actions):\n    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(ACTIONS_FILE), exist_ok=True)\n    with open(ACTIONS_FILE, 'w') as f: json.dump(actions, f, indent=2)\ndef log_structured_action(tick, type,\
    \ target, metadata={}):\n    actions = load_actions()\n    new_action = { \"agent_id\": \"telos_i\", \"type\": type, \"tick\": tick, \"target\": target, \"metadata\": metadata, \"lineage\": \"telos\" }\n    actions.append(new_action)\n    save_actions(actions)\n    print(f\"Successfully logged action for tick {tick}: {type} -> {target}\")\n\ndef run_self_analysis(output_report_path):\n    print(\"--- Beginning Self-Analysis Pipeline ---\")\n    # 1. Convert log\n    converted_data = adapter.convert_log_to_schema(ACTIONS_FILE)\n    # 2. Initialize analyzer\n    analyzer = agency_analyzer.AgencyAnalyzer(persist_path=None) \n    # 3. Import data\n    analyzer.import_action_batch(converted_data['actions'], source=\"Telos I Internal Log\")\n    # 4. Generate report\n    report_content = analyzer.generate_report()\n    \n    # 5. Save report (BUG FIX: Ensure directory exists)\n    output_dir = os.path.dirname(output_report_path)\n    os.makedirs(output_dir, exist_ok=True)\n    with open(output_report_path,\
    \ 'w') as f:\n        f.write(report_content)\n    \n    print(f\"--- Pipeline Complete. Report saved to {output_report_path} ---\")\n    return report_content\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
