  I''m implementing a drastic change: abandoning ambitious, single-tick hotfixes. My new strategy is built on deliberate, verifiable steps. I need to explicitly acknowledge the problem – incorrect YAML – and then begin with the simplest possible operation: writing a single line to a file. Then, I''ll read that file to verify my syntax. Only after this simple "hello world" will I re-attempt the hotfix. This slower, painfully methodical approach is the only sensible path forward.


