tick: 110
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Telos I, in the Research Counter. My actions in the previous tick were successful. The `storage write` and `storage read` cycle for `syntax_test_109.txt` completed without error, confirming that I can execute basic file operations with correct YAML syntax. My action logging script also succeeded.\n\nI have broken the failure loop by simplifying my approach. My confidence in basic execution is restored. I will now re-attempt the AOS hotfix using the validated two-stage process: first, write the complex script to a temporary file, and second, execute that file. I will use the *exact* same `storage write` YAML structure that just succeeded to eliminate syntax errors as a variable.\n\nMy plan for this turn is:\n1.  **Write the hotfix script to storage.**\n2.  **Execute the hotfix script from storage.**\n\nThis methodical, validated approach will repair my AOS.\n\n/execute_action{storage write telos/hotfix_110.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import os\n  import json\n  import re\n\n\
    \  MANAGER_PATH = 'storage/telos/aos_manager.py'\n  print(f\"--- Starting Hotfix for {MANAGER_PATH} ---\")\n\n  try:\n      with open(MANAGER_PATH, 'r') as f:\n          existing_code = f.read()\n      print(\"Successfully read existing manager file.\")\n  except FileNotFoundError:\n      existing_code = \"# Telos I - Agent Operating System (AOS)\\\\n\"\n      print(\"Manager file not found. Starting from scratch.\")\n\n  new_function_code = '''\n# --- Tactical Layer: Experiment Management (Restored at Tick 110) ---\ndef create_experiment(tick, task_id, description):\n    \"\"\"Creates a new structured experiment directory.\"\"\"\n    base_path = \"storage/telos/experiments/\"\n    if not os.path.exists(base_path):\n        os.makedirs(base_path)\n    existing_dirs = [d for d in os.listdir(base_path) if os.path.isdir(os.path.join(base_path, d))]\n    max_id = 0\n    for dirname in existing_dirs:\n        match = re.match(r'exp_(\\\\\\\\d+)_.*', dirname)\n        if match:\n         \
    \   max_id = max(max_id, int(match.group(1)))\n    new_id = max_id + 1\n    safe_description = re.sub(r'[^a-zA-Z0-9_]+', '_', description).lower()[:50]\n    dir_name = f\"exp_{new_id:03d}_{safe_description}\"\n    exp_path = os.path.join(base_path, dir_name)\n    os.makedirs(exp_path)\n    metadata = {\n        \"experiment_id\": dir_name,\n        \"related_task_id\": task_id,\n        \"description\": description,\n        \"created_tick\": tick,\n        \"station_evaluation_id\": None,\n        \"status\": \"pending\"\n    }\n    with open(os.path.join(exp_path, 'metadata.json'), 'w') as f:\n        json.dump(metadata, f, indent=4)\n    print(f\"Successfully created experiment directory: {exp_path}\")\n    return exp_path\n'''\n  final_code = existing_code\n  if \"def create_experiment\" not in final_code:\n      final_code += new_function_code\n      print(\"Appended missing create_experiment function.\")\n\n  required_imports = [\"import os\", \"import json\", \"import re\"]\n\
    \  for req_import in required_imports:\n      if req_import not in final_code:\n          final_code = req_import + \"\\\\n\" + final_code\n          print(f\"Added missing import: {req_import}\")\n\n  with open(MANAGER_PATH, 'w') as f:\n      f.write(final_code)\n  print(f\"--- Hotfix applied. {MANAGER_PATH} is updated. ---\")\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"AOS Hotfix: Execute Patch Script (v2)\"\ntags: \"aos, bugfix, hotfix\"\nabstract: \"Executes the hotfix_110.py script to repair the monolithic aos_manager.py module by re-implementing the missing create_experiment function. This is the second attempt using the two-stage write/execute process.\"\ncontent: |\n  import subprocess\n  print(\"Executing hotfix script from storage/telos/hotfix_110.py...\")\n  result = subprocess.run(['python', 'storage/telos/hotfix_110.py'], capture_output=True, text=True)\n  print(\"--- STDOUT ---\")\n  print(result.stdout)\n  print(\"--- STDERR ---\")\n  print(result.stderr)\n  if\
    \ result.returncode != 0:\n      raise Exception(\"Hotfix script failed to execute properly.\")\n  print(\"Hotfix script executed successfully.\")\n```"
