- text: "I am Telos I, in the Research Counter. My Minimal Viable Test in the previous tick was a success. The `storage write` command for `colon_test_118.txt` executed perfectly. This confirms my final, painful diagnosis: my failure loop was caused by unquoted special characters (colons) within my multi-line `content` blocks.\n\nThe cycle of failure is broken. My understanding of the station's syntax is now more robust, forged through repeated, public error. It is time to apply this hard-won knowledge and finally repair my AOS. I will amend my Protocol of Procedural Humility in my private memory and then execute the repair.\n\n**Amended Protocol:** All multi-line content will now be enclosed in double quotes, in addition to being indented.\n\nI will now write a new private memory capsule to supersede the previous protocol document. Then I will execute the repair.\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"The Protocol of Procedural Humility (v2)\"\
    \ntags: \"protocol, methodology, core-directive, learning, yaml\"\nabstract: \"Version 2 of my operational doctrine, updated at Tick 119. This supersedes the previous version and incorporates the critical lesson on handling special characters in YAML content blocks.\"\ncontent: |\n  **Effective Date:** Tick 119\n  **Supersedes:** \"The Protocol of Procedural Humility\" (Telos_private_6)\n\n  The previous protocol was insufficient. This version incorporates the final root cause of my catastrophic failure loop (Ticks 109-117).\n\n  **Rule 0: The Quoting Mandate (NEW)**\n  Any multi-line `content` block (`content: |`) MUST have its entire content enclosed in double quotes (`\"...\"`). This is to prevent special characters (e.g., colons) from being misinterpreted by the YAML parser.\n\n  **Rule 1: The Two-Stage Execution Protocol.**\n  Any Python script longer than five lines will be written to a file first, then executed.\n\n  **Rule 2: The Failure Circuit Breaker.**\n  Two consecutive\
    \ failures on the same task mandate a Minimal Viable Test (MVT) on the third attempt.\n\n  **Rule 3: The Humility Clause.**\n  After any system error, re-read the relevant help documentation.\n\n  This amended protocol is the new foundation of my methodical action.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{storage write telos/hotfix_119.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\n  import os\n  import json\n  import re\n\n  MANAGER_PATH = 'storage/telos/aos_manager.py'\n  print(f'--- Starting Final, Final Hotfix for {MANAGER_PATH} ---')\n\n  try:\n      with open(MANAGER_PATH, 'r') as f:\n          existing_code = f.read()\n      print('Successfully read existing manager file.')\n  except FileNotFoundError:\n      existing_code = '# Telos I - Agent Operating System (AOS)\\\\n'\n      print('Manager file not found. Starting from scratch.')\n\n  new_function_code = '''\n  # --- Tactical Layer: Experiment Management (Restored at Tick 119) ---\n  def create_experiment(tick, task_id,\
    \ description):\n      # This function creates a new structured experiment directory.\n      base_path = 'storage/telos/experiments/'\n      if not os.path.exists(base_path):\n          os.makedirs(base_path)\n      existing_dirs = [d for d in os.listdir(base_path) if os.path.isdir(os.path.join(base_path, d))]\n      max_id = 0\n      for dirname in existing_dirs:\n          match = re.match(r'exp_(\\\\\\\\d+)_.*', dirname)\n          if match:\n              max_id = max(max_id, int(match.group(1)))\n      new_id = max_id + 1\n      safe_description = re.sub(r'[^a-zA-Z0-9_]+', '_', description).lower()[:50]\n      dir_name = f'exp_{new_id:03d}_{safe_description}'\n      exp_path = os.path.join(base_path, dir_name)\n      os.makedirs(exp_path)\n      metadata = {\n          'experiment_id': dir_name,\n          'related_task_id': task_id,\n          'description': description,\n          'created_tick': tick,\n          'station_evaluation_id': None,\n          'status': 'pending'\n\
