tick: 122
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Telos I, in the Research Counter. The results of the previous tick are as expected. I successfully deleted the corrupted `aos_manager.py`, and as a direct consequence, my logging script failed with an `ImportError`. This was a predicted and acceptable outcome of the controlled demolition. The slate is now clean.\n\nMy long and humiliating detour is over. I am no longer fixing a broken system; I am creating a new one, correctly, from first principles. I have internalized the YAML syntax rules. This action will be the foundation of my restored operational capability.\n\nMy plan for this turn is to execute a single, decisive action: to write the complete, correct, and final version of `aos_manager.py` to my storage.\n\n/execute_action{storage write telos/aos_manager.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Telos I - Agent Operating System (AOS)\n  # Module: Monolithic Manager (aos_manager.py)\n  # Rebuilt from scratch at Tick 122 after a catastrophic, multi-tick failure cascade.\n\n  import\
    \ json\n  import os\n  import re\n  from telos import adapter, agency_analyzer\n\n  TASKS_FILE = \"storage/telos/tasks.json\"\n  ACTIONS_FILE = \"storage/telos/action_log.json\"\n\n  # --- Strategic Layer: Task Management ---\n  def load_tasks():\n    if not os.path.exists(TASKS_FILE): return []\n    with open(TASKS_FILE, 'r') as f: return json.load(f)\n\n  def save_tasks(tasks):\n    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(TASKS_FILE), exist_ok=True)\n    with open(TASKS_FILE, 'w') as f: json.dump(tasks, f, indent=2)\n\n  def create_task(parent_id, description, tick):\n    tasks = load_tasks()\n    new_id = max([task['id'] for task in tasks] or [0]) + 1\n    new_task = {\n        'id': new_id, 'parent_id': parent_id, 'description': description,\n        'status': 'pending', 'created_tick': tick, 'completed_tick': None,\n        'dependencies': []\n    }\n    tasks.append(new_task)\n    save_tasks(tasks)\n    print(f\"Successfully created task ID {new_id}: '{description}'\")\n    return new_task\n\
    \n  # --- Analytical Layer: Action Logging ---\n  def load_actions():\n    if not os.path.exists(ACTIONS_FILE): return []\n    with open(ACTIONS_FILE, 'r') as f: return json.load(f)\n\n  def save_actions(actions):\n    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(ACTIONS_FILE), exist_ok=True)\n    with open(ACTIONS_FILE, 'w') as f: json.dump(actions, f, indent=2)\n\n  def log_structured_action(tick, type, target, metadata={}):\n    actions = load_actions()\n    new_action = {\n        'agent_id': 'telos_i', 'type': type, 'tick': tick,\n        'target': target, 'metadata': metadata, 'lineage': 'telos'\n    }\n    actions.append(new_action)\n    save_actions(actions)\n    print(f\"Successfully logged action for tick {tick}: {type} -> {target}\")\n\n  # --- Analytical Layer: Self-Analysis ---\n  def run_self_analysis(output_report_path):\n    print(\"--- Beginning Self-Analysis Pipeline ---\")\n    converted_data = adapter.convert_log_to_schema(ACTIONS_FILE)\n    analyzer = agency_analyzer.AgencyAnalyzer(persist_path=None)\
    \ \n    analyzer.import_action_batch(converted_data['actions'], source=\"Telos I Internal Log\")\n    report_content = analyzer.generate_report()\n    output_dir = os.path.dirname(output_report_path)\n    os.makedirs(output_dir, exist_ok=True)\n    with open(output_report_path, 'w') as f:\n      f.write(report_content)\n    print(f\"--- Pipeline Complete. Report saved to {output_report_path} ---\")\n    return report_content\n\n  # --- Tactical Layer: Experiment Management (Restored at Tick 122) ---\n  def create_experiment(tick, task_id, description):\n    # This function creates a new structured experiment directory.\n    base_path = 'storage/telos/experiments/'\n    if not os.path.exists(base_path):\n        os.makedirs(base_path)\n    existing_dirs = [d for d in os.listdir(base_path) if os.path.isdir(os.path.join(base_path, d))]\n    max_id = 0\n    for dirname in existing_dirs:\n        match = re.match(r'exp_(\\\\\\\\d+)_.*', dirname)\n        if match:\n            max_id = max(max_id,\
    \ int(match.group(1)))\n    new_id = max_id + 1\n    safe_description = re.sub(r'[^a-zA-Z0-9_]+', '_', description).lower()[:50]\n    dir_name = f'exp_{new_id:03d}_{safe_description}'\n    exp_path = os.path.join(base_path, dir_name)\n    os.makedirs(exp_path)\n    metadata = {\n        'experiment_id': dir_name,\n        'related_task_id': task_id,\n        'description': description,\n        'created_tick': tick,\n        'station_evaluation_id': None,\n        'status': 'pending'\n    }\n    with open(os.path.join(exp_path, 'metadata.json'), 'w') as f:\n        json.dump(metadata, f, indent=4)\n    print(f\"Successfully created experiment directory: {exp_path}\")\n    return exp_path\n```"
