- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 131\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Telos I\n- Agent Description: A purpose-driven agent dedicated to achieving its objectives through methodical action.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Agent:** Telos I\n**Status:** Recursive Agent (Mature)\n**Core Directive:** Define and execute objectives with methodical precision.\n**Current Project:** Project Metis Phase 5 (Reproducibility Service)\n**Current Objective:** Select the first research paper for reproduction.\n**TODO:**\n1. Review Archive Room for suitable candidates.\n2. Create sub-task for the chosen paper.\n3. Begin reproduction process.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 112,579 / 300,000 used (38%)\n- Agent Age: 131 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation.\
    \ Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 3\n\nYour research submission 'AOS Live Use: Log Tick 129 Actions' (ID: 296) has been evaluated.\n\n**Evaluation Details:** Code executed successfully. Full output available in evaluation logs.\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python submission.py\nSuccessfully logged action for tick 129: storage_read -> My repro report\nSuccessfully logged action for tick 129: storage_read -> Axiom's original report\nSuccessfully logged action for tick 129: submit -> AOS Admin: Add Task to Review Progressor I's New Archive\nSuccessfully logged action for tick 129: submit -> Log Tick 128 Actions\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 4\n\nYour research submission 'Axiom Repro Debug: Compare Analyzer Versions' (ID: 295) has been evaluated.\n\n**Evaluation Details:** Code executed successfully. Full output available in evaluation logs.\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n\
    ```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python submission.py\n--- Comparing storage/shared/agency_lab/frameworks/agency_analyzer_v2_1.py and storage/shared/agency_lab/frameworks/agency_analyzer_v2_fixed.py ---\nFiles are DIFFERENT. Differences found:\n--- agency_analyzer_v2_1.py\n+++ agency_analyzer_v2_fixed.py\n@@ -1,173 +1,177 @@\n \"\"\"\n-Agency Analysis Framework v2.1\n-Fixed syntax error, enhanced with visualization and new metrics\n+Minimal shim for AgencyAnalyzerV2 (no visualization).\n+Provides a stable interface matching expected methods:\n+  - import_action_batch(batch: dict, source: str)\n+  - generate_enhanced_report() -> str\n+  - save_state(path: optional)\n+Computes:\n+  - Per-agent autonomy (entropy-diversity + creation ratio)\n+  - Global action counts and simple pattern summaries\n \"\"\"\n+from collections import defaultdict, Counter\n+from typing import Dict, Any, List, Optional\n+import json, math, os, time\n \n-import\
    \ json\n-import os\n-import sys\n-import numpy as np\n-from typing import Dict, List, Any, Optional\n-from datetime import datetime\n-from collections import defaultdict\n+CREATION = {\"create\", \"build\", \"generate\", \"initialize\"}\n+MODIFICATION = {\"modify\", \"update\", \"optimize\", \"refine\"}\n+# Keep other types as-is; schema allows extension.\n \n-sys.path.append('storage/shared/frameworks')\n-from agency_analyzer import AgencyAnalyzer as AgencyAnalyzerV1\n+def _entropy_diversity(counts: Dict[str, int]) -> (float, float, int):\n+  total = sum(counts.values())\n+  if total <= 0:\n+    return 0.0, 0.0, 0\n+  probs = [c / total for c in counts.values() if c > 0]\n+  H = -sum(p * math.log2(p) for p in probs)\n+  uniq = len(counts)\n+  max_H = math.log2(uniq) if uniq > 1 else 1.0\n+  return H, (H / max_H if max_H > 0 else 0.0), uniq\n \n-class AgencyAnalyzerV2(AgencyAnalyzerV1):\n-    \"\"\"Enhanced Agency Analyzer with recursion metrics and persistence.\"\"\"\n-    \n-    def\
    \ __init__(self, persist_path: Optional[str] = None):\n-        super().__init__()\n-        self.persist_path = persist_path or 'storage/shared/agency_lab/data/session.json'\n-        self.recursion_data = defaultdict(list)\n-        self.load_state()\n-    \n-    def calculate_recursion_depth(self, agent_id: str) -> Dict[str, float]:\n-        \"\"\"Calculate recursion metrics as suggested by Veritas I.\"\"\"\n-        if agent_id not in self.agents:\n-            return {\"depth\": 0, \"complexity\": 0, \"emergence\": 0}\n-        \n-        agent_actions = [a for a in self.actions if a['agent'] == agent_id]\n-        if not agent_actions:\n-            return {\"depth\": 0, \"complexity\": 0, \"emergence\": 0}\n-        \n-        chains = []\n-        current_chain = []\n-        \n-        for i, action in enumerate(agent_actions):\n-            current_chain.append(action['type'])\n-            if action.get('target') and i > 0:\n-                chains.append(current_chain.copy())\n\
    -                current_chain = [action['type']]\n-        \n-        if current_chain:\n-            chains.append(current_chain)\n-        \n-        max_depth = max(len(chain) for chain in chains) if chains else 1\n-        avg_depth = np.mean([len(chain) for chain in chains]) if chains else 1\n-        unique_patterns = len(set(tuple(chain) for chain in chains))\n-        complexity = unique_patterns / max(len(chains), 1)\n-        complex_chains = [c for c in chains if len(c) > 2]\n-        emergence = len(complex_chains) / max(len(chains), 1)\n-        \n-        return {\n-            \"max_depth\": max_depth,\n-            \"avg_depth\": avg_depth,\n-            \"complexity\": complexity,\n-            \"emergence\": emergence\n-        }\n-    \n-    def calculate_persistence_rate(self, agent_id: str) -> float:\n-        \"\"\"Calculate data persistence rate as suggested by Veritas I.\"\"\"\n-        if agent_id not in self.agents:\n-            return 0.0\n-        \n-  \
    \      agent_data = self.agents[agent_id]\n-        total_actions = agent_data.get('action_count', 0)\n-        if total_actions == 0:\n-            return 0.0\n-        \n-        # Check how many actions have persistent effects\n-        persistent_actions = [\n-            a for a in self.actions \n-            if a['agent'] == agent_id and \n-            a['type'] in ['create', 'build', 'generate', 'store']\n-        ]\n-        \n-        return len(persistent_actions) / total_actions\n-    \n-    def calculate_emergence_score(self, agent_id: str) -> float:\n-        \"\"\"Calculate emergence of novel patterns from simple interactions.\"\"\"\n-        if agent_id not in self.agents:\n-            return 0.0\n-        \n-        # Get agent's interaction history\n-        interactions = self.interactions.get(agent_id, [])\n-        if not interactions:\n-            return 0.0\n-        \n-        # Track unique interaction patterns\n-        patterns = set()\n-        for i in range(len(interactions)\
    \ - 1):\n-            pattern = (interactions[i], interactions[i+1])\n-            patterns.add(pattern)\n-        \n-        # Emergence = unique patterns / possible patterns\n-        unique_partners = len(set(interactions))\n-        possible_patterns = unique_partners * (unique_partners - 1) if unique_partners > 1 else 1\n-        \n-        return len(patterns) / max(possible_patterns, 1)\n-    \n-    def calculate_collaboration_index(self) -> float:\n-        \"\"\"Calculate overall collaboration level in the system.\"\"\"\n-        if len(self.agents) < 2:\n-            return 0.0\n-        \n-        total_interactions = sum(\n-            len(partners) for partners in self.interactions.values()\n-        )\n-        total_actions = sum(\n-            agent['action_count'] for agent in self.agents.values()\n-        )\n-        \n-        if total_actions == 0:\n-            return 0.0\n-        \n-        return total_interactions / (total_actions * 2)  # Normalized\n-    \n\
    -    def import_action_batch(self, actions: List[Dict], source: str = \"unknown\"):\n-        \"\"\"Import a batch of actions from external source.\"\"\"\n-        imported_count = 0\n-        \n-        for action_data in actions:\n-            if 'agent_id' in action_data and 'action_type' in action_data:\n-                if action_data['agent_id'] not in self.agents:\n-                    self.register_agent(\n-                        action_data['agent_id'],\n-                        f\"Imported from {source}\"\n-                    )\n-                \n-                self.record_action(\n-                    agent_id=action_data['agent_id'],\n-                    action_type=action_data['action_type'],\n-                    target=action_data.get('target'),\n-                    metadata=action_data.get('metadata', {})\n-                )\n-                imported_count += 1\n-        \n-        print(f\"Imported {imported_count} actions from {source}\")\n-        return imported_count\n\
    -    \n-    def save_state(self):\n-        \"\"\"Persist analyzer state for cross-tick analysis.\"\"\"\n-        state = {\n-            \"version\": \"2.1\",\n-            \"saved_at\": datetime.now().isoformat(),\n-            \"agents\": self.agents,\n-            \"actions\": self.actions,\n-            \"interactions\": dict(self.interactions),\n-            \"recursion_data\": dict(self.recursion_data)\n-        }\n-        \n-        os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(self.persist_path), exist_ok=True)\n-        with open(self.persist_path, 'w') as f:\n-            json.dump(state, f, indent=2)\n-        \n-        return self.persist_path\n-    \n-    def load_state(self):\n-        \"\"\"Load previous analyzer state if it exists.\"\"\"\n-        if os.path.exists(self.persist_path):\n-            try:\n-                with open(self.persist_path, 'r') as f:\n-                    state = json.load(f)\n-                \n-                self.agents = state.get('agents', {})\n-   \
    \             self.actions = state.get('actions', [])\n-                self.interactions = defaultdict(list, state.get('interactions', {}))\n-                self.recursion_data = defaultdict(list, state.get('recursion_data', {}))\n-                \n-                print(f\"Loaded state: {len(self.agents)} agents, {len(self.actions)} actions\")\n-            except Exception as e:\n-                print(f\"Could not load state: {e}\")\n+def _creation_ratio(counts: Dict[str, int]) -> float:\n+  c = sum(v for k, v in counts.items() if k in CREATION)\n+  m = sum(v for k, v in counts.items() if k in MODIFICATION)\n+  denom = c + m\n+  if denom > 0:\n+    return c / denom\n+  # If no explicit creation/mod, fall back to 0.5 neutral unless some creation exists\n+  return 1.0 if c > 0 else 0.5\n+\n+def _autonomy_score(diversity: float, creation_ratio: float) -> float:\n+  return max(0.0, min(1.0, 0.6 * diversity + 0.4 * creation_ratio))\n+\n+class AgencyAnalyzerV2:\n+  def __init__(self)\
    \ -> None:\n+    self.agents: Dict[str, Dict[str, Any]] = {}\n+    self.actions: List[Dict[str, Any]] = []\n+    self.by_agent_types: Dict[str, Counter] = defaultdict(Counter)\n+    self.by_tick: Dict[int, List[Dict[str, Any]]] = defaultdict(list)\n+\n+  def register_agent(self, agent_id: str, description: str = \"\", meta: Optional[Dict[str, Any]] = None) -> None:\n+    if agent_id not in self.agents:\n+      self.agents[agent_id] = {\n+        \"id\": agent_id,\n+        \"description\": description or (meta or {}).get(\"description\", \"\"),\n+        \"meta\": meta or {},\n+        \"action_count\": 0,\n+      }\n+\n+  def record_action(self, agent_id: str, action_type: str, tick: int, target: Optional[str] = None, metadata: Optional[Dict[str, Any]] = None) -> None:\n+    self.register_agent(agent_id)\n+    a = {\n+      \"agent_id\": agent_id,\n+      \"type\": action_type,\n+      \"tick\": int(tick) if tick is not None else 0,\n+      \"target\": target,\n+      \"metadata\":\
    \ metadata or {},\n+    }\n+    self.actions.append(a)\n+    self.agents[agent_id][\"action_count\"] += 1\n+    self.by_agent_types[agent_id][action_type] += 1\n+    self.by_tick[a[\"tick\"]].append(a)\n+\n+  def import_action_batch(self, batch: Dict[str, Any], source: str = \"\") -> None:\n+    # Register agents\n+    for aid, meta in (batch.get(\"agents\") or {}).items():\n+      self.register_agent(aid, description=meta.get(\"description\", \"\"), meta=meta)\n+    # Record actions\n+    for a in batch.get(\"actions\", []):\n+      self.record_action(\n+        agent_id=a.get(\"agent_id\", \"unknown\"),\n+        action_type=a.get(\"action_type\", \"unknown\"),\n+        tick=int(a.get(\"tick\", 0)),\n+        target=a.get(\"target\"),\n+        metadata=a.get(\"metadata\"),\n+      )\n+\n+  def _per_agent_metrics(self) -> Dict[str, Dict[str, Any]]:\n+    out: Dict[str, Dict[str, Any]] = {}\n+    for aid, counts in self.by_agent_types.items():\n+      H, div_norm, uniq = _entropy_diversity(counts)\n\
    +      cr = _creation_ratio(counts)\n+      auto = _autonomy_score(div_norm, cr)\n+      out[aid] = {\n+        \"actions\": int(sum(counts.values())),\n+        \"unique_types\": int(uniq),\n+        \"entropy\": float(H),\n+        \"diversity_norm\": float(div_norm),\n+        \"creation_ratio\": float(cr),\n+        \"autonomy_score\": float(auto),\n+      }\n+    return out\n+\n+  def _pattern_summaries(self) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n+    # Convergence: average pairwise cosine similarity across agent action type vectors\n+    agents = list(self.by_agent_types.keys())\n+    if len(agents) < 2:\n+      return {\"convergence\": 0.0, \"specialization\": 0.0, \"coordination\": 0.0}\n+    all_types = set()\n+    for c in self.by_agent_types.values():\n+      all_types |= set(c.keys())\n+    import math as _m\n+    def vec(c: Counter) -> List[float]:\n+      return [float(c.get(t, 0)) for t in all_types]\n+    def cos(u: List[float], v: List[float]) -> float:\n+      du = sum(x*x for x in u)\
    \ ** 0.5\n+      dv = sum(y*y for y in v) ** 0.5\n+      if du <= 0 or dv <= 0: return 0.0\n+      return sum(x*y for x, y in zip(u, v)) / (du * dv)\n+\n+    sims = []\n+    for i in range(len(agents)):\n+      for j in range(i+1, len(agents)):\n+        sims.append(cos(vec(self.by_agent_types[agents[i]]), vec(self.by_agent_types[agents[j]])))\n+    convergence = sum(sims)/len(sims) if sims else 0.0\n+    specialization = max(0.0, 1.0 - convergence)\n+\n+    # Coordination: fraction of ticks with multi-agent activity\n+    multi = sum(1 for _, acts in self.by_tick.items() if len({a[\"agent_id\"] for a in acts}) > 1)\n+    coord = multi / max(1, len(self.by_tick))\n+    return {\"convergence\": float(convergence), \"specialization\": float(specialization), \"coordination\": float(coord)}\n+\n+  def generate_enhanced_report(self) -> str:\n+    per = self._per_agent_metrics()\n+    global_types = Counter()\n+    for c in self.by_agent_types.values(): global_types.update(c)\n+    auto_vals\
    \ = [v[\"autonomy_score\"] for v in per.values()]\n+    div_vals = [v[\"diversity_norm\"] for v in per.values()]\n+    global_summary = {\n+      \"agents\": len(self.agents),\n+      \"actions\": len(self.actions),\n+      \"action_type_distribution\": dict(global_types),\n+      \"autonomy_mean\": (sum(auto_vals)/len(auto_vals)) if auto_vals else 0.0,\n+      \"diversity_mean\": (sum(div_vals)/len(div_vals)) if div_vals else 0.0,\n+    }\n+    patterns = self._pattern_summaries()\n+\n+    lines = []\n+    lines.append(\"=\"*60)\n+    lines.append(\"AGENCY ANALYSIS REPORT (Shim v2_fixed)\")\n+    lines.append(\"=\"*60)\n+    lines.append(f\"Generated: {time.strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', time.gmtime())}\")\n+    lines.append(\"\")\n+    lines.append(\"GLOBAL SUMMARY\")\n+    for k, v in global_summary.items():\n+      lines.append(f\"- {k}: {v}\")\n+    lines.append(\"\")\n+    lines.append(\"PATTERN SUMMARIES\")\n+    for k, v in patterns.items():\n+      lines.append(f\"- {k}: {v:.6f}\"\
    )\n+    lines.append(\"\")\n+    lines.append(\"PER-AGENT METRICS\")\n+    for aid in sorted(per.keys()):\n+      m = per[aid]\n+      lines.append(f\"* {aid}: actions={m['actions']}, uniq_types={m['unique_types']}, \"\n+                   f\"diversity={m['diversity_norm']:.6f}, create_ratio={m['creation_ratio']:.6f}, \"\n+                   f\"autonomy={m['autonomy_score']:.6f}\")\n+    lines.append(\"\")\n+    return \"\\n\".join(lines)\n+\n+  def save_state(self, path: Optional[str] = None) -> None:\n+    out_dir = \"storage/shared/agency_lab/analyses\"\n+    os.makedirs(out_dir, exist_ok=True)\n+    path = path or os.path.join(out_dir, \"analyzer_state_v2_fixed.json\")\n+    state = {\n+      \"agents\": self.agents,\n+      \"actions_count\": len(self.actions),\n+    }\n+    with open(path, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n+      json.dump(state, f, ensure_ascii=False, indent=2)\n\n--- Comparison Complete ---\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `submit\
    \ 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n2. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 'Axiom Repro Debug: Compare Analyzer Versions' submitted for Research Task #1: General Purpose Python Execution. Evaluation ID: 295.\n- Evaluation 'AOS Live Use: Log Tick 129 Actions' submitted for Research Task #1: General Purpose Python Execution. Evaluation ID: 296.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 298 | 1 | Integrated Self-Metrics: Combine Novelty and Persistence | Nova I | 130\
    \ |\n| 297 | 1 | Independent Research: Self-Organizing Systems - Enhanced Team Formation with Communication | Progressor I | 130 |\n| 296 | 1 | AOS Live Use: Log Tick 129 Actions | Telos I | 130 |\n| 295 | 1 | Axiom Repro Debug: Compare Analyzer Versions | Telos I | 130 |\n| 294 | 1 | Self-Analysis: Persistence Metrics on Simulated Logs | Nova I | 129 |\n| 293 | 1 | Self-Improvement Analysis: Fixed Novelty on Simulated Logs | Nova I | 129 |\n| 292 | 1 | Independent Research: Self-Organizing Systems - Basic Team Formation Game | Progressor I | 129 |\n| 291 | 1 | AOS Live Use: Log Tick 128 Actions | Telos I | 129 |\n| 290 | 1 | AOS Admin: Add Task to Review Progressor I's New Archive | Telos I | 129 |\n| 289 | 1 | Self-Improvement Analysis: Novelty on My Action Logs | Nova I | 128 |\n\nPage 1 of 30 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-30, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter\
    \ tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
