parts:
- text: "I am Telos I, in the Research Counter. All administrative tasks related to my first successful reproduction are now complete. Task 27 is marked as 'completed' in my AOS, and my logs are up to date.\n\nIt is time to begin the next cycle of my project. My meta prompt reminds me that my objective is to select the next paper for reproduction. My AOS contains pending tasks to review recent archives from Progressor I and Nova I. I will begin this process by using my `view_tasks.py` utility (which I have not yet created) to get a clear picture of my current priorities. My AOS is still incomplete. I will create this utility now.\n\nMy plan for this turn is to:\n1.  Create the `view_tasks.py` script and save it to my lineage storage.\n2.  Execute this new script to display my current task list.\n3.  Log my previous actions.\n\n/execute_action{storage write telos/view_tasks.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import json\n  import os\n\n  TASKS_FILE = \"storage/telos/tasks.json\"\n\n  def display_tasks():\n\
    \      if not os.path.exists(TASKS_FILE):\n          print(\"No tasks found.\")\n          return\n\n      with open(TASKS_FILE, 'r') as f:\n          tasks = json.load(f)\n\n      if not tasks:\n          print(\"No tasks found.\")\n          return\n\n      print(\"--- Telos I: Task List ---\")\n      tasks.sort(key=lambda x: x['id'])\n      \n      for task in tasks:\n          parent_info = f\"(Parent: {task['parent_id']})\" if task['parent_id'] is not None else \"\"\n          status_info = f\"[{task['status'].upper()}]\"\n          completed_info = f\" (Completed: Tick {task['completed_tick']})\" if task['completed_tick'] else \"\"\n          \n          print(f\"{task['id']:<3} {status_info:<11} {task['description']} {parent_info}{completed_info}\")\n      print(\"--------------------------\")\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      display_tasks()\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"AOS Utility: Execute view_tasks.py\"\ntags: \"aos, utility, task-management\"\
    \nabstract: \"Executing the newly created view_tasks.py utility to get a formatted overview of my current task list and priorities.\"\ncontent: |\n  import subprocess\n  subprocess.run(['python', 'storage/telos/view_tasks.py'], check=True)\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"AOS Live Use: Log Tick 141 Actions\"\ntags: \"aos, logging, live-use\"\nabstract: \"Logging the actions from the previous tick.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n  from telos import aos_manager\n\n  TICK_TO_LOG = 141\n  \n  aos_manager.log_structured_action(tick=TICK_TO_LOG, type=\"goto\", target=\"research\", metadata={})\n  aos_manager.log_structured_action(tick=TICK_TO_LOG, type=\"submit\", target=\"Conclude Axiom I Task (Corrected)\", metadata={\"eval_id\": 320})\n  aos_manager.log_structured_action(tick=TICK_TO_LOG, type=\"submit\", target=\"Log Tick 140 Actions\", metadata={\"eval_id\": 321})\n```"
