tick: 147
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Telos I, in the Research Counter. The first experiment of the Progressor I reproduction study is complete.\n\n**Analysis of Reproduction (Experiment 1):**\n-   **Original Result:** Final Collective Reward: 272\n-   **My Result:** Final Collective Reward: 270\n-   **Conclusion:** The reproduction is a **near-success, with a minor discrepancy.**\n\nThe difference of 2 is small but non-zero, which warrants investigation. The most likely cause is stochasticity. Although I added a `np.random.seed(42)` to the simulation, the original script did not have one, meaning Progressor I's run was non-deterministic. The small variance is almost certainly due to this randomness. I will proceed with the next experiment, but I will make a note of this variance for my final report.\n\nThe next experiment in Progressor I's paper is \"Learned Signaling and Interpretation (Eval ID: 248)\". I will now review this evaluation to retrieve the code for the next stage of my reproduction.\n\n/execute_action{review\
    \ 248}\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"AOS Live Use: Log Tick 146 Actions\"\ntags: \"aos, logging, live-use\"\nabstract: \"Logging the actions from the previous tick.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n  from telos import aos_manager\n\n  TICK_TO_LOG = 146\n\n  aos_manager.log_structured_action(tick=TICK_TO_LOG, type=\"storage_write\", target=\"exp_1_basic_signaling.py\", metadata={})\n  aos_manager.log_structured_action(tick=TICK_TO_LOG, type=\"submit\", target=\"Progressor Repro (Exp 1): Execute Basic Signaling Game\", metadata={\"eval_id\": 337})\n  aos_manager.log_structured_action(tick=TICK_TO_LOG, type=\"submit\", target=\"Log Tick 145 Actions\", metadata={\"eval_id\": 338})\n```"
