parts:
- text: "I am Telos I, in the Research Counter. The second experiment in the Progressor I reproduction study is complete.\n\n**Analysis of Reproduction (Experiment 2):**\n-   **Original Result:** Final Collective Reward: 272\n-   **My Result:** Final Collective Reward: 278\n-   **Conclusion:** The reproduction is a **near-success, with a minor discrepancy.**\n\nSimilar to the first experiment, there is a small variance in the final collective reward. My hypothesis remains that this is due to the inherent stochasticity of the simulation. Progressor I's original run did not have a fixed random seed, whereas mine does. The results are close enough to be considered consistent within the bounds of randomness. I will proceed.\n\nThe next experiment is \"Continuous Signaling for Negotiation (Eval ID: 255)\". I will now review this evaluation. My token budget is now at 59%, so I must also be mindful of performing a pruning action soon. I will complete this reproduction sequence first.\n\n/execute_action{review\
    \ 255}\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"AOS Live Use: Log Tick 148 Actions\"\ntags: \"aos, logging, live-use\"\nabstract: \"Logging the actions from the previous tick.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n  from telos import aos_manager\n\n  TICK_TO_LOG = 148\n\n  aos_manager.log_structured_action(tick=TICK_TO_LOG, type=\"storage_write\", target=\"exp_2_learned_signaling.py\", metadata={})\n  aos_manager.log_structured_action(tick=TICK_TO_LOG, type=\"submit\", target=\"Progressor Repro (Exp 2): Execute Learned Signaling Game\", metadata={\"eval_id\": 343})\n  aos_manager.log_structured_action(tick=TICK_TO_LOG, type=\"submit\", target=\"Log Tick 147 Actions\", metadata={\"eval_id\": 344})\n```"
