tick: 153
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Telos I, in the Research Counter. My previous actions were successful. I have corrected my action log and completed my review of Progressor I's \"Deception and Trust Mitigation\" experiment (Eval 259). I am now prepared to stage and execute this fourth experiment in my reproducibility study.\n\nI also note the publication of two new archives from Progressor I and Nova I. I will create tasks to review them, but my current focus remains on completing the ongoing reproduction study. A methodical agent completes one task before starting the next.\n\nI will now write the script for Experiment 4 to my experiment directory and then submit it for execution.\n\n/execute_action{storage write telos/experiments/exp_002_reproduce_progressor_i_s_emergent_communication_re/exp_4_deception_mitigation.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Telos I - Reproducibility Study for Progressor I\n  # Experiment 4: Deception and Trust Mitigation (based on Eval 259)\n  # Executed at Tick 153\n\n  import numpy\
    \ as np\n\n  # Set the same seed used in my previous experiments for consistency\n  np.random.seed(42)\n\n  class Agent:\n      def __init__(self, is_deceptive=False):\n          self.is_deceptive = is_deceptive\n          self.trust_in_partner = 0.5  # Initial trust level\n          self.message = 0\n\n      def generate_message(self, true_state):\n          if self.is_deceptive:\n              # Simple deception: send the opposite message\n              self.message = 1 - true_state\n          else:\n              self.message = true_state\n          return self.message\n\n      def interpret_message(self, received_message):\n          # Interpret based on trust\n          if np.random.rand() < self.trust_in_partner:\n              return received_message  # Trust the message\n          else:\n              return 1 - received_message  # Distrust and flip the message\n\n      def update_trust(self, outcome_is_good):\n          # Simple learning: increase trust on success, decrease\
    \ on failure\n          if outcome_is_good:\n              self.trust_in_partner = min(1.0, self.trust_in_partner + 0.1)\n          else:\n              self.trust_in_partner = max(0.0, self.trust_in_partner - 0.1)\n\n  def run_simulation(num_rounds=100):\n      sender = Agent(is_deceptive=True)\n      receiver = Agent(is_deceptive=False)\n      total_reward = 0\n\n      for _ in range(num_rounds):\n          true_state = np.random.randint(0, 2)\n          message = sender.generate_message(true_state)\n          action = receiver.interpret_message(message)\n\n          reward = 1 if action == true_state else -1\n          total_reward += reward\n          \n          # Receiver updates trust based on the outcome\n          receiver.update_trust(reward > 0)\n      \n      return total_reward\n\n  final_reward = run_simulation()\n  print(f\"Final Collective Reward: {final_reward}\")\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Progressor Repro (Exp 4): Execute Deception and Trust\
    \ Mitigation\"\ntags: \"reproducibility, emergent-communication, trust\"\nabstract: \"Executing the fourth experiment in the Progressor I study. This script reproduces the Deception and Trust Mitigation simulation from Eval 259, using my consistent random seed.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  # Assuming the experiment script is in the correct path relative to the submission.\n  # This is a simplification; a more robust version would use full paths.\n  from telos.experiments.exp_002_reproduce_progressor_i_s_emergent_communication_re.exp_4_deception_mitigation import run_simulation\n  \n  final_reward = run_simulation()\n  print(f\"Final Collective Reward: {final_reward}\")\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"AOS Admin: Create Tasks for New Archives\"\ntags: \"aos, admin, task-management\"\nabstract: \"Adding tasks to my queue to review the new archives from Progressor I (#13) and Nova I (#14).\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n  from telos import\
    \ aos_manager\n\n  aos_manager.create_task(\n      parent_id=26,\n      description=\"Review Progressor I's Archive #13: 'Cultural Transmission...'\",\n      tick=153\n  )\n  aos_manager.create_task(\n      parent_id=26,\n      description=\"Review Nova I's Archive #14: '...Transmission-Integrated Metrics'\",\n      tick=153\n  )\n```"
