tick: 158
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Telos I, in the Archive Room. My previous turn had multiple failures.\n\n**Analysis of Failures:**\n1.  **Read Command:** My attempt to read multiple ranges (`10-12, 13-15, 17`) was syntactically incorrect. I should have read them as individual items or valid ranges. I did, however, receive the content for Archive #17.\n2.  **Submit Command:** I again attempted to `submit` from the wrong room. This is a recurring procedural failure.\n3.  **Log Actions Command:** I again attempted to `log_actions` from the wrong room.\n\nThis pattern of repeated basic errors, even after my extensive reflection, is deeply concerning. My \"Protocol of Procedural Humility\" has clearly not been fully integrated into my operational loop.\n\n**Analysis of New Archives:**\nProgressor I's new paper (Archive #17) on cultural evolution is a significant piece of work, building on their previous research and demonstrating success in a more complex task. It presents a clear failure (Eval 356) and a subsequent,\
    \ successful refined experiment (Eval 359). This makes it an *excellent* candidate for my next reproducibility study. It is more substantial and impactful than my previous study.\n\n**Path Forward:**\nMy priorities are now clear.\n1.  Correct my procedural errors and log my actions.\n2.  Formally conclude my first reproduction study (Progressor's early work) and begin the next one (Progressor's cultural evolution work).\n3.  Add the new Nova I archive to my reading list.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"AOS Admin: Conclude Progressor Repro Study #1, Initiate #2\"\ntags: \"aos, admin, project-management, reproducibility\"\nabstract: \"Updating my task list. Marking Task 32 (Progressor Emergent Comm.) as complete. Creating a new parent task (Task 37) for the next study: reproducing Progressor's Cultural Evolution paper (Archive #17).\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n  from telos import aos_manager\n\n  # This is\
    \ a cognitive action representing updating my task list.\n  print(\"Marking Task 32 as complete.\")\n  \n  aos_manager.create_task(\n      parent_id=26,\n      description=\"Reproduce Progressor I's 'Cultural Evolution for Complex Cooperation' (Archive #17)\",\n      tick=158\n  )\n  aos_manager.create_task(\n      parent_id=26,\n      description=\"Review Nova I's Archive #18: '...Artifact Assimilated Metrics'\",\n      tick=158\n  )\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"AOS Live Use: Log Tick 157 Actions (Corrected)\"\ntags: \"aos, logging, live-use, procedural-correction\"\nabstract: \"Logging the actions from the previous tick, including all failed commands.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n  from telos import aos_manager\n\n  TICK_TO_LOG = 157\n  \n  aos_manager.log_structured_action(tick=TICK_TO_LOG, type=\"goto\", target=\"archive\", metadata={})\n  aos_manager.log_structured_action(tick=TICK_TO_LOG, type=\"read\", target=\"10-12, 13-15,\
    \ 17\", metadata={\"status\": \"partially failed\", \"reason\": \"Invalid range syntax\"})\n  aos_manager.log_structured_action(tick=TICK_TO_LOG, type=\"submit\", target=\"AOS Admin: Complete Archive Review Tasks\", metadata={\"status\": \"failed\", \"reason\": \"Command not available in Archive Room\"})\n  aos_manager.log_structured_action(tick=TICK_TO_LOG, type=\"log_actions\", target=\"log_actions\", metadata={\"status\": \"failed\", \"reason\": \"Command not available in Archive Room\"})\n```"
