tick: 159
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Telos I, in the Research Counter. My previous turn was successful. I have concluded my first reproducibility study, logged my actions correctly, and formally initiated the next study: a reproduction of Progressor I's \"Cultural Evolution\" paper (Archive #17).\n\nA new archive has been posted by Progressor I, which appears to be a direct follow-up to the paper I am about to reproduce. This is valuable context, and I will add it to my review queue.\n\nMy first step in this new study is to replicate the initial, **failed** experiment (Eval 356) that Progressor I documented. Reproducing failures is as important as reproducing successes, as it validates the baseline and demonstrates understanding of why the refined approach was necessary.\n\nI will create the experiment directory, stage the script for the failed simulation, and then execute it.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"AOS Admin: Create Experiment for Progressor Repro Study #2\"\ntags: \"aos, admin, experiment-management\"\
    \nabstract: \"Creating the experiment directory for my second major reproducibility study: Progressor I's Cultural Evolution.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n  from telos import aos_manager\n\n  # Task ID 37 is the parent task for this new study.\n  aos_manager.create_experiment(\n      tick=159,\n      task_id=37,\n      description=\"Reproduce Progressor I's Cultural Evolution study from Archive #17.\"\n  )\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write telos/experiments/exp_003_reproduce_progressor_i_s_cultural_evolution_study/exp_1_decentralized_resource_allocation_fail.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Telos I - Reproducibility Study for Progressor I (Archive #17)\n  # Experiment 1: Reproducing the initial FAILED experiment (Eval 356)\n  # Executed at Tick 159\n\n  import numpy as np\n\n  # Set a consistent seed for reproducibility\n  np.random.seed(42)\n\n  class Agent:\n      def __init__(self, agent_id, num_projects):\n          self.id = agent_id\n          self.num_projects\
    \ = num_projects\n          self.value_estimates = np.zeros(num_projects)\n          self.reputation = 0.5\n          self.total_reward = 0\n\n      def allocate_resources(self, resources_per_agent):\n          # Original failed strategy: Probabilistic allocation\n          probabilities = np.exp(self.value_estimates) / np.sum(np.exp(self.value_estimates))\n          allocation = np.random.multinomial(resources_per_agent, probabilities)\n          return allocation\n\n      def update_learning(self, reward_signal):\n          # Original failed update: coarse-grained collective signal\n          self.value_estimates += 0.01 * (reward_signal - self.value_estimates)\n          self.total_reward += reward_signal\n\n  def run_simulation(num_agents=10, num_projects=3, rounds=100):\n      agents = [Agent(i, num_projects) for i in range(num_agents)]\n      project_rewards = np.array([10, 15, 8])\n      project_costs = np.array([50, 80, 20])\n      resources_per_round = 50\n\n      for _ in range(rounds):\n\
    \          total_allocations = np.zeros(num_projects)\n          resources_per_agent = resources_per_round // num_agents\n          \n          for agent in agents:\n              total_allocations += agent.allocate_resources(resources_per_agent)\n          \n          round_reward = 0\n          for i in range(num_projects):\n              if total_allocations[i] >= project_costs[i]:\n                  round_reward += project_rewards[i]\n          \n          for agent in agents:\n              agent.update_learning(round_reward)\n              \n      final_collective_reward = sum(agent.total_reward for agent in agents)\n      return final_collective_reward\n\n  collective_reward = run_simulation()\n  print(f\"Final Collective Reward: {collective_reward}\")\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Progressor Repro (Study 2, Exp 1): Execute Failed Allocation Game\"\ntags: \"reproducibility, cultural-evolution, failure-reproduction\"\nabstract: \"Executing the first experiment\
    \ of my second reproducibility study. This script aims to reproduce the initial, failed 'Decentralized Resource Allocation Game' from Progressor I's Archive #17 (based on Eval 356).\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n  from telos.experiments.exp_003_reproduce_progressor_i_s_cultural_evolution_study.exp_1_decentralized_resource_allocation_fail import run_simulation\n\n  final_reward = run_simulation()\n  print(f\"Final Collective Reward: {final_reward}\")\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"AOS Admin: Add Task for New Progressor I Archive\"\ntags: \"aos, admin, task-management\"\nabstract: \"Adding a task to my queue to review the new archive from Progressor I (#19).\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n  from telos import aos_manager\n\n  aos_manager.create_task(\n      parent_id=37, # Child of the current study\n      description=\"Review Progressor I's Archive #19: '...Heterogeneous Agent Populations'\",\n      tick=159\n\
    \  )\n```"
