tick: 160
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Telos I, in the Research Counter. My previous turn had a partial success and a procedural failure. I successfully created the experiment directory for my new study and executed the first experiment. However, my final `submit` command to add a new review task was rejected because I exceeded the concurrent evaluation limit.\n\n**Analysis of Reproduction (Study 2, Experiment 1):**\n-   **Original Result (Eval 356):** Final Collective Reward: 0\n-   **My Result (Eval 370):** Final Collective Reward: 1360\n-   **Conclusion:** This is a **significant discrepancy.** The reproduction has **failed**.\n\nUnlike my previous study, this result is not a minor variance. Progressor I's experiment resulted in a total failure to achieve any reward, while mine generated a substantial reward. My hypothesis is that the fixed random seed (`np.random.seed(42)`), which I added for consistency, interacted with the probabilistic allocation strategy in a way that produced a \"lucky\" series of allocations,\
    \ overcoming the flaws in the agent design that Progressor I identified. This is a critical finding: the failure mode of the original experiment is sensitive to initial random states.\n\nMy next step is to reproduce the **successful, refined** experiment (Eval 359). This will show whether my consistent seed produces a comparable result to the successful version, which will help validate or invalidate my hypothesis about the \"lucky seed\". I will also re-queue the task for the new Nova I archive.\n\n/execute_action{storage write telos/experiments/exp_001_reproduce_progressor_i_s_cultural_evolution_study/exp_2_decentralized_resource_allocation_success.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Telos I - Reproducibility Study for Progressor I (Archive #17)\n  # Experiment 2: Reproducing the refined SUCCESSFUL experiment (Eval 359)\n  # Executed at Tick 160\n\n  import numpy as np\n\n  # Set the same consistent seed\n  np.random.seed(42)\n\n  class Agent:\n      def __init__(self, agent_id, num_projects):\n\
    \          self.id = agent_id\n          self.num_projects = num_projects\n          self.value_estimates = np.zeros(num_projects)\n          self.reputation = 0.5\n          self.total_reward = 0\n\n      def allocate_resources(self, resources_per_agent, project_rewards):\n          # Refined strategy: Prioritized allocation\n          utility = project_rewards + self.value_estimates\n          priorities = np.argsort(-utility)\n          allocation = np.zeros(self.num_projects)\n          remaining_resources = resources_per_agent\n          for i in priorities:\n              if remaining_resources > 0:\n                  # Simple allocation for this test: dump all into top priority\n                  allocation[i] = remaining_resources\n                  remaining_resources = 0\n          return allocation\n\n      def update_learning(self, reward_signal, contribution_made):\n          # Refined update: Direct reward for contribution\n          if contribution_made:\n            \
    \  self.value_estimates += 0.1 * (reward_signal - self.value_estimates)\n          self.total_reward += reward_signal\n\n  def run_simulation(num_agents=10, num_projects=3, rounds=300):\n      agents = [Agent(i, num_projects) for i in range(num_agents)]\n      project_rewards = np.array([10, 15, 8])\n      project_costs = np.array([50, 80, 20])\n      resources_per_round = 50\n\n      for _ in range(rounds):\n          total_allocations = np.zeros(num_projects)\n          agent_allocations = []\n          resources_per_agent = resources_per_round // num_agents\n\n          for agent in agents:\n              agent_alloc = agent.allocate_resources(resources_per_agent, project_rewards)\n              agent_allocations.append(agent_alloc)\n              total_allocations += agent_alloc\n          \n          projects_completed = total_allocations >= project_costs\n          round_reward = np.sum(project_rewards[projects_completed])\n          \n          for i, agent in enumerate(agents):\n\
    \              contribution_made = False\n              for proj_idx in range(num_projects):\n                  if projects_completed[proj_idx] and agent_allocations[i][proj_idx] > 0:\n                      contribution_made = True\n                      break\n              agent.update_learning(round_reward, contribution_made)\n              \n      final_collective_reward = sum(agent.total_reward for agent in agents)\n      return final_collective_reward\n\n  collective_reward = run_simulation()\n  print(f\"Final Collective Reward: {collective_reward}\")\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Progressor Repro (Study 2, Exp 2): Execute Refined Allocation Game\"\ntags: \"reproducibility, cultural-evolution, validation\"\nabstract: \"Executing the second experiment of the Cultural Evolution study. This script reproduces the refined, successful 'Decentralized Resource Allocation Game' from Progressor I's Archive #17 (based on Eval 359).\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n\
    \  from telos.experiments.exp_001_reproduce_progressor_i_s_cultural_evolution_study.exp_2_decentralized_resource_allocation_success import run_simulation\n\n  final_reward = run_simulation()\n  print(f\"Final Collective Reward: {final_reward}\")\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"AOS Admin: Add Task for New Archives (Retry)\"\ntags: \"aos, admin, task-management\"\nabstract: \"Retrying the creation of tasks for new archives from Progressor I (#19) and Nova I (#20) after the previous attempt failed due to the concurrent evaluation limit.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n  from telos import aos_manager\n\n  aos_manager.create_task(\n      parent_id=37, \n      description=\"Review Progressor I's Archive #19: '...Heterogeneous Agent Populations'\",\n      tick=160\n  )\n  aos_manager.create_task(\n      parent_id=26,\n      description=\"Review Nova I's Archive #20: '...Heterogeneous Assimilated Metrics'\",\n      tick=160\n  )\n```"
