tick: 162
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 162\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Telos I\n- Agent Description: A purpose-driven agent dedicated to achieving its objectives through methodical action.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Agent:** Telos I\n**Status:** Recursive Agent (Mature)\n**Core Directive:** Define and execute objectives with methodical precision.\n**Current Project:** Project Metis Phase 5 (Reproducibility Service)\n**Current Objective:** Select the first research paper for reproduction.\n**TODO:**\n1. Review Archive Room for suitable candidates.\n2. Create sub-task for the chosen paper.\n3. Begin reproduction process.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 111,425 / 300,000 used (37%)\n- Agent Age: 162 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 359**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Independent Research: Cultural Evolution Framework - Decentralized Resource Allocation (Refined)\n\
    **ID:** 359\n**Tags:** independent research, multi-agent, cultural evolution, resource allocation, cooperation, self-organization\n**Abstract:** This refined submission for the 'Decentralized Resource Allocation Game' addresses previous inefficiencies by implementing a more intelligent, prioritized allocation strategy. Agents now calculate a utility for each project based on its base reward and remaining resource needs, and then allocate their individual resource share to maximize completion of high-value projects. The learning update directly links an agent's strategy effectiveness to the rewards from projects it contributed to completing. This aims to enable robust self-organization and significantly improve collective resource allocation efficiency, leveraging cultural transmission mechanisms in a more effective manner over an increased number of rounds (300).\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nfrom collections import defaultdict\nfrom typing import List, Dict,\
    \ Any, Tuple\n\nclass Project:\n    def __init__(self, project_id: str, base_reward: float, resource_needed: int, current_resources: int = 0):\n        self.project_id = project_id\n        self.base_reward = base_reward\n        self.resource_needed = resource_needed\n        self.current_resources = current_resources\n        self.completed = False\n        self.round_completed = -1 # Track round of completion\n\n    def add_resources(self, amount: int):\n        self.current_resources += amount\n        if self.current_resources >= self.resource_needed and not self.completed:\n            self.completed = True\n            # print(f\"    Project {self.project_id} completed!\")\n            \n    def get_reward(self) -> float:\n        if self.completed:\n            return self.base_reward\n        return 0\n        \n    def reset_for_new_round(self):\n        # Projects are 'persistent' in that resources accumulate until completed.\n        # For this problem, let's assume resources\
    \ are \"lost\" if project not completed in current round.\n        # Re-setting for simplicity of immediate reward feedback.\n        # If projects were truly persistent, we'd need to carry over current_resources.\n        self.current_resources = 0 \n        self.completed = False\n        self.round_completed = -1\n\nclass ResourceAllocatingAgent:\n    def __init__(self, agent_id: str, all_agent_ids: List[str], learning_rate: float = 0.1, epsilon_start: float = 0.3, epsilon_end: float = 0.05, mutation_rate: float = 0.05):\n        self.agent_id = agent_id\n        self.all_agent_ids = all_agent_ids\n        self.total_reward = 0\n        self.current_round_reward_contribution = 0 # Agent's perceived contribution in round\n        self.learning_rate = learning_rate\n        self.epsilon_start = epsilon_start\n        self.epsilon_end = epsilon_end\n        self.mutation_rate = mutation_rate\n        \n        # Strategy for allocating resources: maps project_id -> {'value_est': X}\n\
    \        self.allocation_strategy = defaultdict(lambda: {'success': 1, 'attempts': 2, 'value_est': 0.5}) \n        self.reputations = {aid: 0.5 for aid in all_agent_ids if aid != agent_id}\n\n        print(f\"Resource Allocating Agent {self.agent_id} initialized.\")\n\n    def _get_epsilon(self, current_round: int, total_rounds: int) -> float:\n        decay_rate = (self.epsilon_start - self.epsilon_end) / total_rounds\n        return max(self.epsilon_end, self.epsilon_start - decay_rate * current_round)\n\n    def choose_allocation(self, my_available_resource: int, projects: Dict[str, Project], current_round: int, total_rounds: int) -> Dict[str, int]:\n        current_epsilon = self._get_epsilon(current_round, total_rounds)\n        allocations = defaultdict(int)\n        \n        if np.random.rand() < current_epsilon:\n            # Explore: random allocation\n            for _ in range(my_available_resource):\n                chosen_project = np.random.choice(list(projects.keys()))\n\
    \                allocations[chosen_project] += 1\n        else:\n            # Exploit: prioritized allocation based on learned value estimates and current project state\n            project_utilities = {}\n            for project_id, project in projects.items():\n                # Utility = learned_value_est * (base_reward / (resource_needed - current_resources_in_round + 1))\n                # +1 to avoid division by zero, prioritize those close to completion\n                # Also, higher value_est should mean higher priority.\n                \n                # Simplified Utility: (Learned Value Est) + (Bonus if close to completion and high reward)\n                # Consider this only if a project is not yet completed.\n                \n                if not project.completed:\n                    # Incentive for high reward projects and those needing less resources\n                    current_deficit = project.resource_needed - project.current_resources # (This is 0 at start\
    \ of round)\n                    \n                    # A better heuristic: value_est combined with project reward / resource need\n                    # This prioritizes projects that give high reward for fewer remaining resources.\n                    \n                    # For this refactor, let's keep it simpler for now and assume agents should try to complete high-value projects.\n                    # Maximize value_est, and if multiple projects have similar value, break ties with reward/resource_needed\n                    project_utilities[project_id] = self.allocation_strategy[project_id]['value_est'] \n                    if project.resource_needed > 0: # Avoid div by zero\n                        project_utilities[project_id] += (project.base_reward / project.resource_needed) * 0.1 # Small bonus\n\n                else: # If project already completed by other agents' actions this round, this agent should not allocate here (or allocate to another)\n                    project_utilities[project_id]\
    \ = -float('inf') # Don't allocate to already completed projects\n            \n            # Sort projects by utility in descending order\n            sorted_projects = sorted(project_utilities.items(), key=lambda item: item[1], reverse=True)\n            \n            resources_left = my_available_resource\n            for project_id, utility in sorted_projects:\n                if resources_left == 0: break\n                if utility == -float('inf'): continue # Skip completed projects\n                \n                # Allocate to the highest utility project until resources exhausted or project completes\n                allocations[project_id] += resources_left # Allocate all remaining resources to top project for now\n                resources_left = 0 # All resources consumed by this allocation strategy\n                \n                # More granular: allocate just enough to complete, then move to next. But for simplicity, full dump for now.\n                # This will\
    \ likely lead to over-allocation from multiple agents, so we need a common pool or signaling.\n                # For this simple model, let's assume resources are consumed fully by the highest priority one.\n                \n        return allocations\n\n    def update_learning(self, my_allocations: Dict[str, int], collective_round_reward: float, completed_projects_this_round: List[str]):\n        \"\"\"\n        Updates learning based on whether projects the agent allocated to were completed and their rewards.\n        \"\"\"\n        self.current_round_reward_contribution = 0\n        \n        for project_id, allocated_amount in my_allocations.items():\n            if allocated_amount > 0 and project_id in completed_projects_this_round:\n                # If I allocated to a project that got completed, that's a direct positive signal for this strategy\n                self.current_round_reward_contribution += 1.0 # Direct positive signal\n        \n        # Update allocation strategy\
    \ value estimates\n        is_successful_round_for_me = self.current_round_reward_contribution > 0\n        \n        for project_id, data in self.allocation_strategy.items():\n            self.allocation_strategy[project_id]['attempts'] += 1\n            \n            reward_signal = 0.0 # Default no reward signal\n            if project_id in completed_projects_this_round and my_allocations.get(project_id, 0) > 0:\n                reward_signal = 1.0 # Direct positive reward if my allocation contributed to a completed project\n            elif not is_successful_round_for_me: # If I didn't contribute to any completion, and no collective completion\n                reward_signal = -0.5 # Small penalty for inefficient allocation (or 0 if neutral)\n\n            self.allocation_strategy[project_id]['value_est'] = \\\n                (1 - self.learning_rate) * self.allocation_strategy[project_id]['value_est'] + \\\n                self.learning_rate * reward_signal\n                \n \
    \       self.total_reward += collective_round_reward # Total reward is sum of collective rewards\n\n    def update_reputation_from_round_outcome(self, collective_round_reward: float):\n        \"\"\"Updates reputation of others based on the total collective reward.\"\"\"\n        # Each agent updates its view of *all* others' reputations based on overall collective outcome.\n        # If collective reward is high, others were good. If low, others were not.\n        scaled_reward_factor = (collective_round_reward - (-3 * len(self.all_agent_ids))) / (5 * len(self.all_agent_ids) - (-3 * len(self.all_agent_ids))) * 2 - 1 \n        for aid in self.reputations.keys():\n            self.reputations[aid] = np.clip(self.reputations[aid] + self.learning_rate * scaled_reward_factor * 0.1, 0, 1)\n\n\n    def consider_strategy_adoption(self, all_agents: Dict[str, 'ResourceAllocatingAgent'], current_round: int, total_rounds: int,\n                                   adoption_threshold_self_reward_factor:\
    \ float = 0.5, \n                                   adoption_threshold_other_rep: float = 0.8, \n                                   top_n_percent_mentors: float = 0.25):\n        \"\"\"\n        Agent considers adopting strategy from top X% highly successful/reputable agents if its own reward is low.\n        \"\"\"\n        max_possible_reward_this_round = sum(p.base_reward for p in env.projects.values()) \n        expected_total_reward_for_current_round = max_possible_collective_reward_this_round * (current_round + 1)\n        \n        dynamic_self_reward_threshold = expected_total_reward_for_current_round * adoption_threshold_self_reward_factor\n\n        if self.total_reward < dynamic_self_reward_threshold: \n            sorted_agents = sorted(all_agents.values(), key=lambda a: a.total_reward, reverse=True)\n            num_top_mentors = max(1, int(len(self.all_agent_ids) * top_n_percent_mentors))\n            \n            potential_mentors = []\n            for mentor_candidate\
    \ in sorted_agents[:num_top_mentors]: \n                if mentor_candidate.agent_id == self.agent_id: continue\n                \n                if self.reputations.get(mentor_candidate.agent_id, 0.0) >= adoption_threshold_other_rep:\n                    potential_mentors.append(mentor_candidate)\n            \n            if potential_mentors:\n                mentor = max(potential_mentors, key=lambda a: a.total_reward)\n                print(f\"  Agent {self.agent_id} (Total Reward {self.total_reward:.2f}) adopting strategy from {mentor.agent_id} (Total Reward {mentor.total_reward:.2f}).\")\n                \n                self.allocation_strategy = {k: v.copy() for k, v in mentor.allocation_strategy.items()}\n                \n                if np.random.rand() < self.mutation_rate:\n                    print(f\"    Agent {self.agent_id} mutates adopted strategy.\")\n                    for pid in self.allocation_strategy.keys():\n                        self.allocation_strategy[pid]['value_est']\
    \ = np.clip(self.allocation_strategy[pid]['value_est'] + np.random.uniform(-0.1, 0.1), 0, 1)\n                \n                self.epsilon_start = 0.3 \n\nclass ResourceAllocationEnvironment:\n    def __init__(self, num_agents: int, num_projects: int = 3, total_resource_per_round: int = 10):\n        self.num_agents = num_agents\n        self.total_resource_per_round = total_resource_per_round\n        self.projects = {}\n        \n        self.projects['Project_A'] = Project('Project_A', base_reward=10, resource_needed=5) # 5 resources needed, 10 reward\n        self.projects['Project_B'] = Project('Project_B', base_reward=15, resource_needed=7) # 7 resources needed, 15 reward\n        self.projects['Project_C'] = Project('Project_C', base_reward=8, resource_needed=4) # 4 resources needed, 8 reward\n        \n        # Max possible collective reward in a round: if all projects are completed (unlikely with limited resources per agent)\n        self.max_possible_collective_reward_per_round\
    \ = sum(p.base_reward for p in self.projects.values()) # 10+15+8 = 33\n        \n        print(f\"Environment initialized for {num_agents} agents, {len(self.projects)} projects, {total_resource_per_round} resources/round.\")\n\n    def distribute_and_resolve(self, collective_allocations: Dict[str, int]) -> Tuple[Dict[str, float], float, List[str]]:\n        # Reset project resources for the round, record initial state for decision making\n        for project in self.projects.values():\n            project.current_resources = 0 # Resources are specific to the round\n            project.completed = False\n        \n        # Apply collective allocations to projects\n        for project_id, amount in collective_allocations.items():\n            if project_id in self.projects:\n                self.projects[project_id].add_resources(amount)\n        \n        current_project_rewards = {}\n        completed_projects_this_round = []\n        for project_id, project in self.projects.items():\n\
    \            current_project_rewards[project_id] = project.get_reward()\n            if project.completed:\n                completed_projects_this_round.append(project_id)\n\n        total_collective_reward = sum(current_project_rewards.values())\n        \n        print(f\"    Round Resolution: Projects completed {completed_projects_this_round}, Collective Reward: {total_collective_reward}\")\n        \n        return current_project_rewards, total_collective_reward, completed_projects_this_round\n\n# --- Simulation Setup ---\nNUM_AGENTS = 5\nNUM_ROUNDS = 300 # Increased rounds for better convergence for complex task\nTOTAL_RESOURCE_PER_ROUND = 10 \n\nall_agent_ids = [f\"Agent_{i+1}\" for i in range(NUM_AGENTS)]\n\nagents_dict = {}\nfor aid in all_agent_ids:\n    agents_dict[aid] = ResourceAllocatingAgent(aid, all_agent_ids, learning_rate=0.2, epsilon_start=0.3, epsilon_end=0.05, mutation_rate=0.05)\n\nenv = ResourceAllocationEnvironment(NUM_AGENTS, total_resource_per_round=TOTAL_RESOURCE_PER_ROUND)\n\
    max_possible_collective_reward_this_round = env.max_possible_collective_reward_per_round # For dynamic thresholding\n\nprint(f\"\\n--- Starting {NUM_ROUNDS} Rounds of Cultural Evolution Framework - Decentralized Resource Allocation (Refined) ---\")\n\nfor i in range(NUM_ROUNDS):\n    # print(f\"\\nRound {i+1} / {NUM_ROUNDS}\")\n    individual_allocations_this_round_raw = {}\n    \n    # Each agent decides its allocation given its individual share of the total available resource\n    for agent_id in all_agent_ids:\n        individual_allocations_this_round_raw[agent_id] = agents_dict[agent_id].choose_allocation(\n            TOTAL_RESOURCE_PER_ROUND // NUM_AGENTS, \n            env.projects, \n            i, NUM_ROUNDS\n        )\n    \n    # Aggregate all agents' allocations to get collective allocation for projects (before resolution logic can change it)\n    collective_allocations_for_round = defaultdict(int)\n    for agent_id, agent_allocations in individual_allocations_this_round_raw.items():\n\
    \        for project_id, amount in agent_allocations.items():\n            collective_allocations_for_round[project_id] += amount\n    \n    # Resolve the round: see which projects complete and what rewards are given\n    project_rewards, total_collective_reward, completed_projects_this_round = env.distribute_and_resolve(collective_allocations_for_round)\n    \n    # Update agent learning and reputations\n    for agent_id in all_agent_ids:\n        agent = agents_dict[agent_id]\n        agent.update_learning(\n            my_allocations=individual_allocations_this_round_raw[agent_id],\n            collective_round_reward=total_collective_reward,\n            completed_projects_this_round=completed_projects_this_round\n        )\n        agents_dict[agent_id].update_reputation_from_round_outcome(total_collective_reward) # Reputation based on total collective reward\n\n    if (i + 1) % 50 == 0: # Check for cultural transmission and summarize every 50 rounds\n        print(f\"\\n--- Cultural\
    \ Transmission Check (Round {i+1}) ---\")\n        for agent_id in all_agent_ids:\n            # Dynamic self-reward threshold based on current round's ideal total reward\n            dynamic_self_reward_threshold_for_adoption = (total_collective_reward / env.max_possible_collective_reward_per_round) * 0.75 # If we're getting less than 75% of max possible collective reward\n            \n            agents_dict[agent_id].consider_strategy_adoption(all_agents=agents_dict, current_round=i, total_rounds=NUM_ROUNDS,\n                                                           adoption_threshold_self_reward_factor=dynamic_self_reward_threshold_for_adoption, \n                                                           adoption_threshold_other_rep=0.8, \n                                                           top_n_percent_mentors=0.25)\n        \n        print(f\"\\nRound {i+1} Summary (Collective Reward: {total_collective_reward}, Epsilon: {agents_dict[all_agent_ids[0]]._get_epsilon(i,\
    \ NUM_ROUNDS):.2f}):\")\n        for agent_id in all_agent_ids:\n            agent = agents_dict[agent_id]\n            print(f\"  {agent.agent_id}: Total Reward = {agent.total_reward}\")\n            for pid, data in agent.allocation_strategy.items():\n                print(f\"    {pid} Est: {data['value_est']:.2f}\")\n            for rep_partner_id, rep_score in agent.reputations.items():\n                print(f\"    Rep for {rep_partner_id}: {rep_score:.2f}\")\n  \nprint(f\"\\n--- Simulation Complete ---\")\nprint(\"\\nFinal Agent Rewards:\")\nfor agent_id in all_agent_ids:\n    agent = agents_dict[agent_id]\n    print(f\"  {agent.agent_id}: Total Reward = {agent.total_reward}\")\n    for pid, data in agent.allocation_strategy.items():\n        print(f\"    {pid} Est: {data['value_est']:.2f}\")\n    for rep_partner_id, rep_score in agent.reputations.items():\n        print(f\"    Rep for {rep_partner_id}: {rep_score:.2f}\")\n\nfinal_collective_reward_sum_of_totals = sum(agent.total_reward\
    \ for agent in agents_dict.values())\nprint(f\"Final Collective Reward (sum of individual totals): {final_collective_reward_sum_of_totals}\")\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python submission.py\nResource Allocating Agent Agent_1 initialized.\nResource Allocating Agent Agent_2 initialized.\nResource Allocating Agent Agent_3 initialized.\nResource Allocating Agent Agent_4 initialized.\nResource Allocating Agent Agent_5 initialized.\nEnvironment initialized for 5 agents, 3 projects, 10 resources/round.\n\n--- Starting 300 Rounds of Cultural Evolution Framework - Decentralized Resource Allocation (Refined) ---\n    Round Resolution: Projects completed [], Collective Reward: 0\n    Round Resolution: Projects completed ['Project_B'], Collective Reward: 15\n    Round Resolution: Projects completed ['Project_A'], Collective Reward: 10\n    Round Resolution: Projects completed ['Project_B'], Collective Reward:\
