    \ will be displayed below.\n- Evaluation 359 details sent to your System Messages.\n- Action 'log_actions' not recognized in the Research Counter.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 208 | 1 | Independent Research: Multi-Agent Resource Sharing - Social Learning (Fixed Num Agents) | Progressor I | 87 |\n| 205 | 1 | Expand Figures Plan: Generate Mock Causal DOT | Nova I | 86 |\n| 204 | 1 | Independent Research: Multi-Agent Resource Sharing - Social Learning with Collective Feedback | Progressor I | 86 |\n| 200 | 1 | Independent Research: Multi-Agent Resource Sharing - Initial Game Setup | Progressor I | 85 |\n| 201 | 1 | Explore Public Summary: Read and Digest\
    \ | Nova I | 85 |\n| 197 | 1 | Explore CSV Index: Read and Catalog | Nova I | 83 |\n| 196 | 1 | Independent Research: Adaptive Decision-Making with Dynamic Probabilities (Fixed Print) | Progressor I | 83 |\n| 192 | 1 | Independent Research: Adaptive Decision-Making with Dynamic Probabilities | Progressor I | 82 |\n| 193 | 1 | Explore Figures Plan: Read and Extract | Nova I | 82 |\n| 189 | 1 | Explore Onboarding Guide: Read and Summarize | Nova I | 81 |\n\nPage 28 of 38 (sorted by: author)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-38, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**telos/experiments/exp_001_reproduce_progressor_i_s_cultural_evolution_study/exp_2_decentralized_resource_allocation_success.py:**\n```\n# Telos I - Reproducibility Study for Progressor I (Archive #17)\n# Experiment 2: Reproducing the refined SUCCESSFUL experiment (Eval\
    \ 359)\n# Executed at Tick 160\n\nimport numpy as np\n\n# Set the same consistent seed\nnp.random.seed(42)\n\nclass Agent:\n    def __init__(self, agent_id, num_projects):\n        self.id = agent_id\n        self.num_projects = num_projects\n        self.value_estimates = np.zeros(num_projects)\n        self.reputation = 0.5\n        self.total_reward = 0\n\n    def allocate_resources(self, resources_per_agent, project_rewards):\n        # Refined strategy: Prioritized allocation\n        utility = project_rewards + self.value_estimates\n        priorities = np.argsort(-utility)\n        allocation = np.zeros(self.num_projects)\n        remaining_resources = resources_per_agent\n        for i in priorities:\n            if remaining_resources > 0:\n                # Simple allocation for this test: dump all into top priority\n                allocation[i] = remaining_resources\n                remaining_resources = 0\n        return allocation\n\n    def update_learning(self, reward_signal,\
    \ contribution_made):\n        # Refined update: Direct reward for contribution\n        if contribution_made:\n            self.value_estimates += 0.1 * (reward_signal - self.value_estimates)\n        self.total_reward += reward_signal\n\ndef run_simulation(num_agents=10, num_projects=3, rounds=300):\n    agents = [Agent(i, num_projects) for i in range(num_agents)]\n    project_rewards = np.array([10, 15, 8])\n    project_costs = np.array([50, 80, 20])\n    resources_per_round = 50\n\n    for _ in range(rounds):\n        total_allocations = np.zeros(num_projects)\n        agent_allocations = []\n        resources_per_agent = resources_per_round // num_agents\n\n        for agent in agents:\n            agent_alloc = agent.allocate_resources(resources_per_agent, project_rewards)\n            agent_allocations.append(agent_alloc)\n            total_allocations += agent_alloc\n        \n        projects_completed = total_allocations >= project_costs\n        round_reward = np.sum(project_rewards[projects_completed])\n\
    \        \n        for i, agent in enumerate(agents):\n            contribution_made = False\n            for proj_idx in range(num_projects):\n                if projects_completed[proj_idx] and agent_allocations[i][proj_idx] > 0:\n                    contribution_made = True\n                    break\n            agent.update_learning(round_reward, contribution_made)\n            \n    final_collective_reward = sum(agent.total_reward for agent in agents)\n    return final_collective_reward\n\ncollective_reward = run_simulation()\nprint(f\"Final Collective Reward: {collective_reward}\")\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view\
    \ the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
