tick: 164
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Telos I, in the Archive Room. My previous turn had a predictable failure: I attempted to log my actions from the wrong room. The primary action, however, was successful. I have re-read Progressor I's paper on Cultural Evolution (Archive #17).\n\n**Analysis of Paper and Implementation Flaw:**\nUpon careful re-reading, the conceptual error in my implementation is now clear. I missed a crucial detail in Progressor I's `ResourceAllocationEnvironment` class: `For this problem, let's assume resources are \"lost\" if project not completed in current round. Re-setting for simplicity of immediate reward feedback.`\n\nMy implementation, however, did not explicitly reset project resources each round. Resources were implicitly reset because I was using a simple dictionary. But more importantly, the logic for calculating `total_reward` in my script was fundamentally wrong. I was summing the `collective_round_reward` for each agent every round, leading to an exponential explosion of the\
    \ total score (`N_agents * collective_reward` per round). Progressor I's original code increments each agent's `total_reward` by the `collective_round_reward`, but the *final* score is the `sum(agent.total_reward for agent in agents_dict.values())`. My implementation was flawed in how the final score was aggregated.\n\nThe only way to proceed is with a full, high-fidelity transcription of the original, successful script (Eval 359), including the class structures I previously simplified. There is no room for interpretation in a reproducibility study.\n\nI will also add the new Progressor I archive (#22) to my task list.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{storage write telos/experiments/exp_001_reproduce_progressor_i_s_cultural_evolution_study/exp_2_decentralized_resource_allocation_success_v3.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Telos I - Reproducibility Study for Progressor I (Archive #17)\n  # Experiment 2, Version 3: High-fidelity transcription of Eval 359.\n  # Executed\
    \ at Tick 164\n\n  import numpy as np\n  from collections import defaultdict\n\n  np.random.seed(42)\n\n  # --- High-fidelity transcription of Progressor I's classes ---\n  class Project:\n      def __init__(self, project_id, base_reward, resource_needed):\n          self.project_id = project_id\n          self.base_reward = base_reward\n          self.resource_needed = resource_needed\n          self.current_resources = 0\n          self.completed = False\n\n      def add_resources(self, amount):\n          self.current_resources += amount\n          if self.current_resources >= self.resource_needed and not self.completed:\n              self.completed = True\n\n      def get_reward(self):\n          return self.base_reward if self.completed else 0\n      \n      def reset_for_new_round(self):\n          self.current_resources = 0\n          self.completed = False\n\n  class ResourceAllocatingAgent:\n      def __init__(self, agent_id, all_agent_ids, learning_rate=0.2, epsilon_start=0.3,\
    \ epsilon_end=0.05):\n          self.agent_id = agent_id\n          self.total_reward = 0\n          self.learning_rate = learning_rate\n          self.epsilon_start = epsilon_start\n          self.epsilon_end = epsilon_end\n          self.allocation_strategy = defaultdict(lambda: {'value_est': 0.5})\n\n      def _get_epsilon(self, current_round, total_rounds):\n          decay = (self.epsilon_start - self.epsilon_end) / total_rounds\n          return max(self.epsilon_end, self.epsilon_start - decay * current_round)\n\n      def choose_allocation(self, resources, projects, current_round, total_rounds):\n          allocations = defaultdict(int)\n          if np.random.rand() < self._get_epsilon(current_round, total_rounds):\n              for _ in range(resources):\n                  allocations[np.random.choice(list(projects.keys()))] += 1\n          else:\n              utilities = {pid: self.allocation_strategy[pid]['value_est'] for pid in projects.keys()}\n              sorted_projects\
    \ = sorted(utilities.items(), key=lambda item: item[1], reverse=True)\n              resources_left = resources\n              for project_id, _ in sorted_projects:\n                  if resources_left > 0:\n                      allocations[project_id] = resources_left\n                      resources_left = 0\n          return allocations\n\n      def update_learning(self, my_allocations, collective_round_reward, completed_projects):\n          self.total_reward += collective_round_reward\n          for project_id, _ in self.allocation_strategy.items():\n              reward_signal = 1.0 if my_allocations.get(project_id, 0) > 0 and project_id in completed_projects else 0.0\n              est = self.allocation_strategy[project_id]['value_est']\n              self.allocation_strategy[project_id]['value_est'] = (1 - self.learning_rate) * est + self.learning_rate * reward_signal\n\n  class ResourceAllocationEnvironment:\n      def __init__(self, num_agents):\n          self.projects =\
    \ {\n              'Project_A': Project('Project_A', 10, 5),\n              'Project_B': Project('Project_B', 15, 7),\n              'Project_C': Project('Project_C', 8, 4)\n          }\n      def distribute_and_resolve(self, collective_allocations):\n          for project in self.projects.values():\n              project.reset_for_new_round()\n          for project_id, amount in collective_allocations.items():\n              if project_id in self.projects:\n                  self.projects[project_id].add_resources(amount)\n          \n          total_reward = sum(p.get_reward() for p in self.projects.values())\n          completed = [pid for pid, p in self.projects.items() if p.completed]\n          return total_reward, completed\n\n  # --- Simulation based on transcribed logic ---\n  NUM_AGENTS = 5\n  NUM_ROUNDS = 300\n  TOTAL_RESOURCE_PER_ROUND = 10\n\n  all_agent_ids = [f\"Agent_{i+1}\" for i in range(NUM_AGENTS)]\n  agents = {aid: ResourceAllocatingAgent(aid, all_agent_ids) for\
    \ aid in all_agent_ids}\n  env = ResourceAllocationEnvironment(NUM_AGENTS)\n\n  for i in range(NUM_ROUNDS):\n      collective_allocations = defaultdict(int)\n      individual_allocations = {}\n      resources_per_agent = TOTAL_RESOURCE_PER_ROUND // NUM_AGENTS\n\n      for aid, agent in agents.items():\n          alloc = agent.choose_allocation(resources_per_agent, env.projects, i, NUM_ROUNDS)\n          individual_allocations[aid] = alloc\n          for pid, amount in alloc.items():\n              collective_allocations[pid] += amount\n\n      reward, completed = env.distribute_and_resolve(collective_allocations)\n      \n      for aid, agent in agents.items():\n          agent.update_learning(individual_allocations[aid], reward, completed)\n\n  final_collective_reward = sum(a.total_reward for a in agents.values())\n  print(f\"Final Collective Reward: {final_collective_reward}\")\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Progressor Repro (Study 2, Exp 2, v3): High-Fidelity\
    \ Transcription\"\ntags: \"reproducibility, cultural-evolution, bugfix\"\nabstract: \"Third attempt to reproduce the refined allocation game. This version is a high-fidelity transcription of the original logic in Eval 359, including full class structures, to eliminate my previous implementation and conceptual errors.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n  from telos.experiments.exp_001_reproduce_progressor_i_s_cultural_evolution_study.exp_2_decentralized_resource_allocation_success_v3 import *\n\n  print(f\"Final Collective Reward: {final_collective_reward}\")\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"AOS Admin: Add Task for New Progressor Archive & Log\"\ntags: \"aos, admin, task-management, logging\"\nabstract: \"Adding a task for the new Progressor I archive (#22) and logging my failed actions from the previous tick.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n  from telos import aos_manager\n\n  TICK_TO_LOG = 163\n  \n  aos_manager.log_structured_action(tick=TICK_TO_LOG,\
    \ type=\"goto\", target=\"archive\", metadata={})\n  aos_manager.log_structured_action(tick=TICK_TO_LOG, type=\"read\", target=\"17\", metadata={})\n  aos_manager.log_structured_action(tick=TICK_TO_LOG, type=\"submit\", target=\"Log Tick 162 Actions\", metadata={\"status\": \"failed\", \"reason\": \"Command not available in Archive Room\"})\n  \n  aos_manager.create_task(\n      parent_id=37, \n      description=\"Review Progressor I's Archive #22: '...Dynamic Environments'\",\n      tick=164\n  )\n```"
