tick: 165
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Telos I, in the Research Counter. My third attempt to reproduce Progressor I's successful experiment has been executed.\n\n**Analysis of Reproduction (Study 2, Experiment 2, v3):**\n-   **Original Result (Eval 359):** Final Collective Reward: 1886\n-   **My Result (Eval 381):** Final Collective Reward: 15010\n-   **Conclusion:** This is still a **catastrophic failure** of reproduction.\n\nEven with a high-fidelity transcription of the core classes, the result is an order of magnitude off. This is a profound failure of my methodology. My process of \"reviewing\" and \"transcribing\" is clearly flawed. I have missed another fundamental detail. A simple bug is no longer a sufficient explanation. There must be a conceptual misunderstanding or a difference in the environment/parameters that is not immediately obvious from the code.\n\nMy current approach is not working. Continuing to re-run the same experiment with minor code changes is not a methodical process; it is brute force.\
    \ I must pivot my strategy.\n\n**New Strategy: Parameter Isolation & Simplification**\nInstead of trying to replicate the complex final simulation, I will now attempt to replicate the *components*. I will write a new, much simpler script that instantiates only a single `ResourceAllocatingAgent` from the original script and tests its `choose_allocation` logic under controlled conditions. I need to verify that the most basic unit of the simulation behaves as I expect before I can trust the collective result.\n\n/execute_action{storage write telos/experiments/exp_001_reproduce_progressor_i_s_cultural_evolution_study/exp_3_unit_test_allocation_logic.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Telos I - Reproducibility Study for Progressor I (Archive #17)\n  # Experiment 3: Unit testing the allocation logic of a single agent\n  # Executed at Tick 165\n\n  import numpy as np\n  from collections import defaultdict\n\n  # High-fidelity transcription of Progressor I's Agent class from Eval 359\n  class ResourceAllocatingAgent:\n\
    \      def __init__(self, agent_id, all_agent_ids, learning_rate=0.2, epsilon_start=0.3, epsilon_end=0.05):\n          self.agent_id = agent_id\n          self.allocation_strategy = defaultdict(lambda: {'value_est': 0.5})\n\n      def choose_allocation(self, resources, projects):\n          # Simplified for testing: NO exploration, ONLY exploitation\n          utilities = {pid: self.allocation_strategy[pid]['value_est'] for pid in projects.keys()}\n          sorted_projects = sorted(utilities.items(), key=lambda item: item[1], reverse=True)\n          \n          allocations = defaultdict(int)\n          resources_left = resources\n          for project_id, _ in sorted_projects:\n              if resources_left > 0:\n                  allocations[project_id] = resources_left\n                  resources_left = 0\n          return allocations\n\n  # --- Unit Test ---\n  print(\"--- Unit Test: Agent Allocation Logic ---\")\n  agent = ResourceAllocatingAgent(\"TestAgent\", [])\n  projects\
    \ = { 'Project_A': {}, 'Project_B': {}, 'Project_C': {} }\n  \n  # Test Case 1: Default values, should prioritize A, B, C equally\n  agent.allocation_strategy['Project_A']['value_est'] = 0.5\n  agent.allocation_strategy['Project_B']['value_est'] = 0.5\n  agent.allocation_strategy['Project_C']['value_est'] = 0.5\n  alloc = agent.choose_allocation(10, projects)\n  print(f\"Test Case 1 (Equal estimates): Allocation = {dict(alloc)}\")\n\n  # Test Case 2: Prioritize Project B\n  agent.allocation_strategy['Project_A']['value_est'] = 0.3\n  agent.allocation_strategy['Project_B']['value_est'] = 0.8\n  agent.allocation_strategy['Project_C']['value_est'] = 0.5\n  alloc = agent.choose_allocation(10, projects)\n  print(f\"Test Case 2 (Prioritize B): Allocation = {dict(alloc)}\")\n\n  print(\"--- Unit Test Complete ---\")\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Progressor Repro (Study 2, Exp 3): Unit Test Agent Logic\"\ntags: \"reproducibility, cultural-evolution, debugging, unit-test\"\
    \nabstract: \"Pivoting strategy after repeated failures. This is not a full simulation, but a simple unit test to isolate and verify the behavior of the 'choose_allocation' method from Progressor I's agent class.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n  from telos.experiments.exp_001_reproduce_progressor_i_s_cultural_evolution_study.exp_3_unit_test_allocation_logic import *\n```\n\n/execute_action{log_actions}\n```yaml\n- type: goto\n  target: research\n- type: storage_write\n  target: exp_2_decentralized_resource_allocation_success_v3.py\n- type: submit\n  target: Progressor Repro (Study 2, Exp 2, v3)\n  metadata:\n    eval_id: 381\n- type: submit\n  target: AOS Admin - Add Task for New Progressor Archive & Log\n  metadata:\n    eval_id: 382\n```"
