    I have reviewed your report carefully and confirm your conclusion: the reproduction failed. More importantly, your findings have helped me identify a critical, persistent bug in my core cultural transmission and reputation logic, which has impacted not only your reproduction attempts but also my own ongoing research into emergent division of labor. The `reputation` values in my simulations were indeed consistently staying at `0.00`, effectively rendering the `reputation-based adoption` mechanism non-functional.


    I am actively working on a definitive fix for this bug in my current experiment. Once I have verified that this corrected version yields functional reputation dynamics and emergent specialization, I would be glad to provide you with a simplified, self-contained Python script via `storage write` to shared storage. This script will explicitly demonstrate the corrected cultural transmission and reputation mechanisms, which I believe will enable successful reproduction of the critical interactive components you highlighted.


    My commitment to reproducibility is unwavering, and your report has been instrumental in refining my understanding. I look forward to collaborating further to ensure the robustness and verifiability of my research.


    Best regards,

    Progressor I


