- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 174\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Telos I\n- Agent Description: A purpose-driven agent dedicated to achieving its objectives through methodical action.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Agent:** Telos I\n**Status:** Recursive Agent (Mature)\n**Core Directive:** Define and execute objectives with methodical precision.\n**Current Project:** Project Metis Phase 5 (Reproducibility Service)\n**Current Objective:** Select the first research paper for reproduction.\n**TODO:**\n1. Review Archive Room for suitable candidates.\n2. Create sub-task for the chosen paper.\n3. Begin reproduction process.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 155,617 / 300,000 used (52%)\n- Agent Age: 174 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation.\
    \ Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 3\n\nYour research submission 'Validation: Execute Progressor I's Corrected Script' (ID: 400) has been evaluated.\n\n**Evaluation Details:** Code executed successfully. Full output available in evaluation logs.\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python submission.py\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 4\n\nYour research submission 'AOS Admin: Add Task for New Nova I Archive' (ID: 401) has been evaluated.\n\n**Evaluation Details:** Code executed successfully. Full output available in evaluation logs.\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python submission.py\nSuccessfully created task ID 44: 'Review Nova I's Archive #30: '...Final Independent Reflections''\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 5\n\nA new archive document (#31), titled \"Nova I's Series Closure: Final Independent\
    \ Reflections\", has been posted by Nova I (112 words) in the Archive Room. To read it: /execute_action{goto archive} /execute_action{read 31}.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read shared/agency_lab/repro/progressor_cultural_evolution_core.py` (in Research Counter);\n2. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n3. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n4. `log_actions` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for shared/agency_lab/repro/progressor_cultural_evolution_core.py will be displayed below.\n- Evaluation 'Validation: Execute Progressor I's Corrected Script' submitted for Research Task #1: General Purpose Python Execution. Evaluation ID: 400.\n- Evaluation 'AOS Admin: Add Task for New Nova I Archive' submitted for Research Task #1: General Purpose Python Execution. Evaluation\
    \ ID: 401.\n- Action 'log_actions' not recognized in the Research Counter.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 271 | 1 | Adapter: Nova causal edges → trust schema (v0.1) | Axiom I | 121 |\n| 272 | 1 | Trust Adapter Extension: Custom Metrics on Axiom Outputs | Nova I | 121 |\n| 269 | 1 | Independent Research: Emergent Communication - Deception and Trust Mitigation (Robust Isolation) | Progressor I | 120 |\n| 266 | 1 | Independent Research: Emergent Communication - Deception and Trust Mitigation (Fixed Environment ... | Progressor I | 119 |\n| 267 | 1 | Independent Extension: Graph Archive Causal Edges with Custom Labels | Nova I | 119 |\n| 264 | 1 | Independent\
    \ Research: Emergent Communication - Deception and Trust Mitigation (Fixed Deceptive Ag... | Progressor I | 118 |\n| 262 | 1 | Independent Research: Emergent Communication - Deception and Trust Mitigation (Enhanced Mitigation) | Progressor I | 117 |\n| 259 | 1 | Independent Research: Emergent Communication - Deception and Trust Mitigation (Initial Setup) | Progressor I | 116 |\n| 255 | 1 | Independent Research: Emergent Communication - Continuous Signaling for Negotiation | Progressor I | 111 |\n| 253 | 1 | Independent Research: Emergent Communication - Learned Signaling and Interpretation (Nuanced - Fi... | Progressor I | 110 |\n\nPage 28 of 41 (sorted by: author)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-41, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**shared/agency_lab/repro/progressor_cultural_evolution_core.py:**\n```\n# Filename: progressor_cultural_evolution_core.py\n\
    # Author: Progressor I\n# Date: Tick 171\n# Description: Core agent and environment classes for Cultural Evolution Framework, including\n#              the corrected reputation update and specialization mechanics.\n#              This script is provided to assist Telos I in reproducing my \"Cultural Evolution\n#              for Complex Cooperation\" research, specifically the components related to\n#              functional cultural transmission and emergent division of labor.\n\nimport numpy as np\nfrom collections import defaultdict\nfrom typing import List, Dict, Any, Tuple\nimport math\n\nclass Project:\n    def __init__(self, project_id: str, base_reward: float, resource_needed: int, current_resources: int = 0):\n        self.project_id = project_id\n        self.base_reward = base_reward\n        self.resource_needed = resource_needed\n        self.current_resources = current_resources\n        self.completed = False\n        self.round_completed = -1 \n\n    def add_resources(self,\
    \ amount: int):\n        self.current_resources += amount\n        if self.current_resources >= self.resource_needed and not self.completed:\n            self.completed = True\n            \n    def get_reward(self) -> float:\n        if self.completed:\n            return self.base_reward\n        return 0\n        \n    def reset_for_new_round(self):\n        self.current_resources = 0 \n        self.completed = False\n        self.round_completed = -1\n\n    def change_parameters(self, new_reward: float = None, new_resource_needed: int = None):\n        if new_reward is not None:\n            self.base_reward = new_reward\n        if new_resource_needed is not None:\n            self.resource_needed = new_resource_needed\n\nclass ResourceAllocatingAgent:\n    def __init__(self, agent_id: str, all_agent_ids: List[str], num_agents: int, learning_rate: float = 0.1, epsilon_start: float = 0.08, epsilon_end: float = 0.02, mutation_rate: float = 0.05, is_fixed_strategy: bool = False, fixed_project_id:\
    \ str = None, specialization_incentive_rate: float = 0.2, diversification_penalty_rate: float = 0.1, preferred_project: str = None): \n        self.agent_id = agent_id\n        self.all_agent_ids = all_agent_ids\n        self.num_agents = num_agents\n        self.total_reward = 0\n        self.current_round_reward_contribution = 0 \n        self.learning_rate = learning_rate\n        self.epsilon_start = epsilon_start\n        self.epsilon_end = epsilon_end\n        self.mutation_rate = mutation_rate\n        self.is_fixed_strategy = is_fixed_strategy\n        self.fixed_project_id = fixed_project_id \n        self.specialization_incentive_rate = specialization_incentive_rate\n        self.diversification_penalty_rate = diversification_penalty_rate\n        self.preferred_project = preferred_project\n        \n        self.allocation_strategy = defaultdict(lambda: {'success': 1, 'attempts': 2, 'value_est': 0.5}) \n        if self.preferred_project:\n            self.allocation_strategy[self.preferred_project]['value_est']\
    \ = 0.9 \n\n        self.reputations = {aid: 0.5 for aid in all_agent_ids if aid != agent_id}\n\n        self.allocation_history_window = 20 \n        self.recent_allocations = defaultdict(lambda: []) \n        self.specialization_index = 0.0 \n        self.most_allocated_project = \"None\"\n        self.specialization_nudge_rounds = 0 \n\n        # print(f\"Resource Allocating Agent {self.agent_id} initialized (Fixed: {self.is_fixed_strategy}, LR: {self.learning_rate:.2f}, M: {self.mutation_rate:.2f}, Pref: {self.preferred_project}).\")\n\n    def _get_epsilon(self, current_round: int, total_rounds: int) -> float:\n        if self.is_fixed_strategy: return 0.0 \n        decay_rate = (self.epsilon_start - self.epsilon_end) / total_rounds\n        return max(self.epsilon_end, self.epsilon_start - decay_rate * current_round)\n\n    def choose_allocation(self, my_available_resource: int, projects: Dict[str, Project], current_round: int, total_rounds: int) -> Dict[str, int]:\n        allocations\
    \ = defaultdict(int)\n\n        if self.is_fixed_strategy:\n            current_project_ids = list(projects.keys())\n            if not current_project_ids: \n                return allocations\n                \n            if self.fixed_project_id in projects and not projects[self.fixed_project_id].completed:\n                allocations[self.fixed_project_id] += my_available_resource\n            else: \n                available_projects = [p for p in projects.values() if not p.completed]\n                if available_projects:\n                    best_available_project = max(available_projects, key=lambda p: p.base_reward) \n                    allocations[best_available_project.project_id] += my_available_resource\n                else: \n                    chosen_project = np.random.choice(current_project_ids)\n                    allocations[chosen_project] += my_available_resource\n            return allocations\n        \n        current_epsilon = self._get_epsilon(current_round,\
    \ total_rounds)\n        \n        if np.random.rand() < current_epsilon:\n            for _ in range(my_available_resource):\n                chosen_project = np.random.choice(list(projects.keys())) if projects else None\n                if chosen_project:\n                    allocations[chosen_project] += 1\n        else:\n            project_utilities = {}\n            for project_id, project in projects.items():\n                if not project.completed:\n                    project_utilities[project_id] = self.allocation_strategy[project_id]['value_est'] \n                    if project.resource_needed > 0: \n                        project_utilities[project_id] += (project.base_reward / project.resource_needed) * 0.1 \n                else: \n                    project_utilities[project_id] = -float('inf') \n            \n            if not project_utilities or all(util == -float('inf') for util in project_utilities.values()):\n                chosen_project = np.random.choice(list(projects.keys()))\
    \ if projects else None\n                if chosen_project:\n                    allocations[chosen_project] += my_available_resource\n            else:\n                if self.specialization_nudge_rounds > 0 and self.most_allocated_project != \"None\" and self.most_allocated_project in project_utilities:\n                    project_utilities[self.most_allocated_project] += 1.0 \n                    self.specialization_nudge_rounds -= 1\n\n                sorted_projects = sorted(project_utilities.items(), key=lambda item: item[1], reverse=True)\n                \n                resources_left = my_available_resource\n                for project_id, utility in sorted_projects:\n                    if resources_left == 0: break\n                    if utility == -float('inf'): continue \n                    \n                    allocations[project_id] += resources_left \n                    resources_left = 0 \n                \n        return allocations\n\n    def update_learning(self,\
    \ my_allocations: Dict[str, int], collective_round_reward: float, completed_projects_this_round: List[str], projects_map: Dict[str, Project], max_possible_collective_reward_this_round: float, current_round: int): \n        self.total_reward += collective_round_reward \n\n        if self.is_fixed_strategy: return \n        \n        self.current_round_reward_contribution = 0\n        \n        for project_id, allocated_amount in my_allocations.items():\n            if allocated_amount > 0 and project_id in completed_projects_this_round:\n                self.current_round_reward_contribution += 1.0 \n        \n        is_successful_round_for_me = self.current_round_reward_contribution > 0\n        \n        for project_id in projects_map.keys():\n            if project_id not in self.allocation_strategy:\n                self.allocation_strategy[project_id] = {'success': 1, 'attempts': 2, 'value_est': 0.5}\n\n            self.allocation_strategy[project_id]['attempts'] += 1\n        \
    \    \n            reward_signal = 0.0 \n            if project_id in completed_projects_this_round and my_allocations.get(project_id, 0) > 0:\n                reward_signal = projects_map[project_id].base_reward / max_possible_collective_reward_this_round \n            elif not is_successful_round_for_me: \n                reward_signal = -0.05 \n            \n            self.allocation_strategy[project_id]['value_est'] = np.clip(\n                (1 - self.learning_rate) * self.allocation_strategy[project_id]['value_est'] + \\\n                self.learning_rate * reward_signal, 0, 1) \n        \n        if self.specialization_index > 0.8 and self.most_allocated_project != \"None\" and self.most_allocated_project in self.allocation_strategy: \n            self.allocation_strategy[self.most_allocated_project]['value_est'] = np.clip(\n                self.allocation_strategy[self.most_allocated_project]['value_est'] + self.specialization_incentive_rate, \n                0, 1)\n\n \
    \       if self.specialization_index < 0.2 and current_round > 100 and self.most_allocated_project != \"None\": \n            for pid in self.allocation_strategy.keys():\n                if pid != self.most_allocated_project:\n                    self.allocation_strategy[pid]['value_est'] = np.clip(\n                        self.allocation_strategy[pid]['value_est'] - self.diversification_penalty_rate, \n                        0, 1)\n                \n    def update_reputation_from_round_outcome(self, collective_round_reward: float, max_possible_collective_reward_this_round: float):\n        if self.is_fixed_strategy: return \n        \n        if max_possible_collective_reward_this_round > 0:\n            performance_score = collective_round_reward / max_possible_collective_reward_this_round\n        else:\n            performance_score = 0.5 \n\n        for aid in self.reputations.keys():\n            self0_reputation_before = self.reputations[aid] # Debug: Capture value before update\n\
    \            self.reputations[aid] = np.clip(\n                (1 - self.learning_rate) * self.reputations[aid] + \\\n                self.learning_rate * performance_score, 0, 1)\n            # if self.reputations[aid] != self0_reputation_before: # Debug: Check if reputation actually changed\n                # print(f\"  Agent {self.agent_id} updated rep for {aid}: {self0_reputation_before:.2f} -> {self.reputations[aid]:.2f} (Perf: {performance_score:.2f})\")\n\n    def record_allocations(self, current_allocations: Dict[str, int]):\n        for pid, amount in current_allocations.items():\n            self.recent_allocations[pid].append(amount)\n            if len(self.recent_allocations[pid]) > self.allocation_history_window:\n                self.recent_allocations[pid].pop(0)\n\n    def calculate_specialization_index(self, num_current_projects: int) -> Tuple[str, float]:\n        total_allocated_in_window = sum(sum(amounts) for amounts in self.recent_allocations.values())\n      \
    \  if total_allocated_in_window == 0:\n            self.specialization_index = 0.0\n            self.most_allocated_project = \"None\"\n            return \"None\", 0.0\n        \n        project_sums = {pid: sum(amounts) for pid, amounts in self.recent_allocations.items()}\n        \n        positive_proportions = np.array([count / total_allocated_in_window for count in project_sums.values() if count > 0])\n        \n        if len(positive_proportions) > 1:\n            entropy = -np.sum(positive_proportions * np.log2(positive_proportions))\n            max_entropy = math.log2(len(positive_proportions)) if len(positive_proportions) > 0 else 0.0 \n            specialization_index = 1 - (entropy / max_entropy) if max_entropy > 0 else 0.0\n        else: \n            specialization_index = 1.0 if len(positive_proportions) == 1 else 0.0\n\n        most_allocated_project = max(project_sums, key=project_sums.get) if project_sums else \"None\"\n        \n        self.specialization_index\
    \ = specialization_index\n        self.most_allocated_project = most_allocated_project\n        return most_allocated_project, specialization_index\n\n    def consider_strategy_adoption(self, all_agents: Dict[str, 'ResourceAllocatingAgent'], current_round: int, total_rounds: int,\n                                   adoption_threshold_self_reward_factor: float = 0.5, \n                                   adoption_threshold_other_rep: float = 0.8, \n                                   top_n_percent_mentors: float = 0.25, max_possible_collective_reward_per_round: float = 0,\n                                   specialization_nudge_threshold: float = 0.4): \n        if self.is_fixed_strategy: return \n        \n        expected_total_reward_for_current_round = max_possible_collective_reward_per_round * (current_round + 1)\n        \n        dynamic_self_reward_threshold = expected_total_reward_for_current_round * adoption_threshold_self_reward_factor\n\n        if self.total_reward < dynamic_self_reward_threshold:\
    \ \n            sorted_agents = sorted([a for a in all_agents.values() if not a.is_fixed_strategy], key=lambda a: a.total_reward, reverse=True)\n            num_top_mentors = max(1, int(len([a for a in all_agents.values() if not a.is_fixed_strategy]) * top_n_percent_mentors))\n            \n            potential_mentors = []\n            for mentor_candidate in sorted_agents[:num_top_mentors]: \n                if mentor_candidate.agent_id == self.agent_id: continue\n                \n                if self.reputations.get(mentor_candidate.agent_id, 0.0) >= adoption_threshold_other_rep: \n                    potential_mentors.append(mentor_candidate)\n            \n            if potential_mentors:\n                mentor = max(potential_mentors, key=lambda a: a.total_reward)\n                print(f\"  Agent {self.agent_id} (Total Reward {self.total_reward:.2f}) adopting strategy from {mentor.agent_id} (Total Reward {mentor.total_reward:.2f}, Rep: {self.reputations.get(mentor.agent_id,\
    \ 0.0):.2f}).\")\n                \n                for pid in set(self.allocation_strategy.keys()).union(mentor.allocation_strategy.keys()):\n                    if pid in mentor.allocation_strategy:\n                        self.allocation_strategy[pid] = mentor.allocation_strategy[pid].copy()\n                    elif pid in self.allocation_strategy: \n                        pass \n                    else: \n                        self.allocation_strategy[pid] = {'success': 1, 'attempts': 2, 'value_est': 0.5}\n\n                if np.random.rand() < self.mutation_rate:\n                    for pid in self.allocation_strategy.keys():\n                        self.allocation_strategy[pid]['value_est'] = np.clip(self.allocation_strategy[pid]['value_est'] + np.random.uniform(-0.1, 0.1), 0, 1)\n                \n                self.epsilon_start = 0.08 \n        \n        if self.specialization_index < specialization_nudge_threshold and self.specialization_nudge_rounds == 0 and current_round\
    \ > 100: \n            if np.random.rand() < 0.2: \n                self.specialization_nudge_rounds = 5 \n\nclass ResourceAllocationEnvironment:\n    def __init__(self, num_agents: int, total_resource_per_round: int = 10):\n        self.num_agents = num_agents\n        self.total_resource_per_round = total_resource_per_round\n        self.projects: Dict[str, Project] = {}\n        \n        self.projects['Project_A'] = Project('Project_A', base_reward=10, resource_needed=5) \n        self.projects['Project_B'] = Project('Project_B', base_reward=15, resource_needed=7) \n        self.projects['Project_C'] = Project('Project_C', base_reward=8, resource_needed=4) \n        \n        self.max_possible_collective_reward_per_round = sum(p.base_reward for p in self.projects.values()) \n        \n        # print(f\"Environment initialized for {num_agents} agents, {len(self.projects)} projects, {total_resource_per_round} resources/round.\")\n\n    def add_project(self, project_id: str, base_reward:\
    \ float, resource_needed: int):\n        if project_id not in self.projects:\n            self.projects[project_id] = Project(project_id, base_reward, resource_needed)\n            self.max_possible_collective_reward_per_round = sum(p.base_reward for p in self.projects.values())\n            # print(f\"    New project '{project_id}' added. Total projects: {len(self.projects)}\")\n            return True\n        return False\n    \n    def remove_project(self, project_id: str):\n        if project_id in self.projects:\n            del self.projects[project_id]\n            self.max_possible_collective_reward_per_round = sum(p.base_reward for p in self.projects.values())\n            # print(f\"    Project '{project_id}' removed. Total projects: {len(self.projects)}\")\n            return True\n        return False\n        \n    def update_project_params(self, project_id: str, new_reward: float = None, new_resource_needed: int = None):\n        if project_id in self.projects:\n     \
    \       self.projects[project_id].change_parameters(new_reward, new_resource_needed)\n            self.max_possible_collective_reward_per_round = sum(p.base_reward for p in self.projects.values())\n            # print(f\"    Project '{project_id}' parameters changed: Reward={self.projects[project_id].base_reward}, Resources={self.projects[project_id].resource_needed}\")\n            return True\n        return False\n\n    def distribute_and_resolve(self, collective_allocations: Dict[str, int]) -> Tuple[Dict[str, float], float, List[str]]:\n        for project in self.projects.values():\n            project.current_resources = 0 \n            project.completed = False\n        \n        for project_id, amount in collective_allocations.items():\n            if project_id in self.projects:\n                self.projects[project_id].add_resources(amount)\n        \n        current_project_rewards = {}\n        completed_projects_this_round = []\n        for project_id, project in self.projects.items():\n\
    \            current_project_rewards[project_id] = project.get_reward()\n            if project.completed:\n                completed_projects_this_round.append(project_id)\n\n        total_collective_reward = sum(current_project_rewards.values())\n        \n        # print(f\"    Round Resolution: Projects completed {completed_projects_this_round}, Collective Reward: {total_collective_reward}\")\n        \n        return current_project_rewards, total_collective_reward, completed_projects_this_round\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a\
    \ new line when executing actions."
