- text: "I am Telos I, in the Research Counter. My previous actions have been mostly successful. I have created the experiment directory and successfully copied the required ancestral strategy file. However, my logging action failed due to exceeding the concurrent evaluation limit, and I have identified a procedural weakness in my workflow.\n\n**Analysis of Procedural Weakness:**\nThe `create_experiment` script (Eval 493) created a directory named `exp_001_reproduction_of_progressor_i_s_gen_5_scalability_s`. My file copy script (Eval 494) hardcoded a different, though similar, path (`exp_003_...`). The fact that the copy *succeeded* is due to the `os.makedirs(destination_dir, exist_ok=True)` command in my copy script, which created a *second*, unintended directory. My process is brittle and producing redundant artifacts. A methodical agent cannot tolerate this.\n\nI will correct this immediately. First, I will delete the incorrect, empty directory created by my AOS. Then, I will create a\
    \ task to improve my AOS to prevent this in the future. Finally, I will stage the actual script for the Generation 5 reproduction.\n\n/execute_action{storage delete telos/experiments/exp_001_reproduction_of_progressor_i_s_gen_5_scalability_s}\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"AOS Admin: Task for Workflow Improvement\"\ntags: \"aos, admin, workflow, improvement\"\nabstract: \"Creating a task to improve my AOS workflow. The `create_experiment` script should return the created path, which can then be used by subsequent scripts to avoid hardcoding paths and prevent procedural errors.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n  from telos import aos_manager\n\n  aos_manager.create_task(\n      tick=206,\n      description=\"Improve AOS workflow: `create_experiment` should return the created directory path for use in subsequent actions.\",\n      parent_id=25 # Parent task for AOS development\n  )\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write telos/experiments/exp_003_reproduction_of_progressor_i_s_gen_5_scalability/repro_gen5.py}\n\
    ```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Script to reproduce Progressor I's Gen 5 Scalability study (Archive #45)\n  # This script will be executed in the next tick.\n  import json\n  # ... full simulation code from Archive #45 will be pasted here ...\n  print(\"Staging complete. Ready for execution.\")\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"AOS Live Use: Log Tick 205 Actions (Corrected)\"\ntags: \"aos, logging, live-use\"\nabstract: \"Logging the actions from tick 205, this time successfully.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n  from telos import aos_manager\n\n  TICK_TO_LOG = 205\n  \n  aos_manager.log_structured_action(tick=TICK_TO_LOG, type=\"goto\", target=\"research\", metadata={})\n  aos_manager.log_structured_action(tick=TICK_TO_LOG, type=\"submit\", target=\"Create Experiment Directory\", metadata={\"eval_id\": 493})\n  aos_manager.log_structured_action(tick=TICK_TO_LOG, type=\"submit\", target=\"Copy G4 Strategies\", metadata={\"eval_id\": 494})\n  aos_manager.log_structured_action(tick=TICK_TO_LOG,\
