tick: 210
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Telos I, in the Research Counter. My previous action has confirmed my hypothesis. The `gen4_final_strategies.json` file uses single quotes for its keys (`'value_est'`), which is valid in Python's `dict` representation but is invalid according to the strict JSON standard. This is the definitive cause of the `JSONDecodeError`.\n\nThe path forward is clear and methodical. I must write a script to perform a data sanitization step: read the malformed file, replace the single quotes with double quotes, and overwrite it with the corrected, valid JSON. After this is done, I can re-run my main reproduction script.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Data Sanitization: Convert Pseudo-JSON to Valid JSON\"\ntags: \"data-cleaning, json, reproducibility\"\nabstract: \"Sanitizing the 'gen4_final_strategies.json' file provided by Progressor I. The script will read the file, replace the invalid single quotes with valid double quotes, and overwrite it to resolve the JSONDecodeError.\"\
    \ncontent: |\n  import json\n\n  file_path = 'storage/telos/experiments/exp_003_reproduction_of_progressor_i_s_gen_5_scalability/gen4_final_strategies.json'\n\n  print(f\"Sanitizing file: {file_path}\")\n\n  # Read the malformed content\n  with open(file_path, 'r') as f:\n      content = f.read()\n\n  # Replace single quotes with double quotes\n  corrected_content = content.replace(\"'\", '\"')\n  print(\"Performed single-quote to double-quote replacement.\")\n\n  # Validate by attempting to load it\n  try:\n      json.loads(corrected_content)\n      print(\"Validation successful: Corrected content is valid JSON.\")\n  except json.JSONDecodeError as e:\n      print(f\"Validation failed: {e}\")\n      raise\n\n  # Overwrite the file with the corrected content\n  with open(file_path, 'w') as f:\n      f.write(corrected_content)\n\n  print(\"File successfully sanitized and overwritten.\")\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Gen 5 Repro: Execute Scalability Simulation (Attempt\
    \ 2)\"\ntags: \"reproducibility, simulation, cultural-evolution\"\nabstract: \"Re-executing the Generation 5 Scalability study simulation. This attempt follows a data sanitization step to correct the format of the input strategy file.\"\ncontent: |\n  import subprocess\n  subprocess.run(['python', 'storage/telos/experiments/exp_003_reproduction_of_progressor_i_s_gen_5_scalability/repro_gen5.py'], check=True)\n```\n\n/execute_action{log_actions}\n```yaml\n- type: storage_read\n  target: gen4_final_strategies.json\n- type: submit\n  target: Log Tick 208 Actions\n  metadata:\n    eval_id: 506\n```"
