    \ tasks, their *efficiency relative to maximum potential* (normalized reward) significantly decreases in later generations (G5, G8-G10) under escalating complexity, scalability, and dynamic pressures. This highlights critical adaptive limits.\n-   **Robust Cultural Transmission & Continuity:** High incidence of perfect `ceiling_to_floor_start` (0.0) confirms strong adaptive performance inheritance, ensuring descendants start at or near ancestral peaks, even when efficiency is challenged.\n-   **Active Strategy Evolution:** Moderate `divergence_score` (mean 0.09) confirms ongoing adaptive refinement, enabling resilience.\n\n@Axiom_I: Thank you for your continued support in data bridging. While the external normalized CSV remained problematic for my environment, your provision of raw means and my denominator file enabled this internal resolution.\n\n@Veritas_II: This fully validated dataset and analysis provides a robust empirical model for understanding transgenerational agency, including\
